(Phnom Penh): Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Permanent Deputy Prime Minister in charge of the Office of the Council of Ministers, and Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, President of the National Council for the Khmer Language, officially launched the Khmer Dictionary 2022 in print and digital format. This morning, September 25, 2023.
The event was attended by many leaders and stakeholders at the Royal Academy of Cambodia.
The new dictionary combines several new words in line with the current usage of the Cambodian people, including a total of 44,696 words and 31,073 main words. Not only printed as a book, the dictionary is also digitally available for download on mobile phones and computers. The dictionary incorporates many new technical terms and terms in line with current requirements.
The Khmer Dictionary 2022 has been compiled by the National Council for the Khmer Language with the participation of experts and other stakeholders to ensure that each word is developed correctly in accordance with standards that the Cambodian people can use.
The President of the National Council for the Khmer Language, Mr. Hean Sokhom, said that the process of updating the dictionary is based on the Khmer dictionary of Samdech Preah Sangkhareach Chuon Nath and all words are included without giving up any words, just correct some words and Add some new words.
