(Phnom Penh): Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Deputy Prime Minister in charge of the Office of the Council of Ministers, said that a new Khmer dictionary is a testimony and history of all Cambodians today.
Deputy Prime Minister Vongsey Visoth also called on all Cambodians to use and critique for the development of the national language in response to the evolution of society and globalization of the world.
This statement was made by Deputy Prime Minister Vongsey Visoth on the morning of September 25, 2023 at the inauguration of the new "Khmer Dictionary" of the Royal Academy of Cambodia.
On that occasion, Deputy Prime Minister Vongsey Visoth also encouraged all Cambodians to use the new Khmer dictionary for everyone and to the best of their ability to ministries, institutions, units and other work.
In addition, Deputy Prime Minister Vongsey Visoth added that language is a vehicle for communication on political, economic, social and religious affairs, and the compilation of the new dictionary is extremely important in helping to compile, preserve and develop the Khmer language and script. Kong Vong is safe for the whole Khmer nation.
Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, stated that the National Council for the Khmer Language has published a number of dictionaries: Geography, History, Economics, Medical Dictionary, Philosophy Dictionary, Philosophy Dictionary, Literature Dictionary, Chemistry Dictionary, Physics Dictionary, Linguistics Dictionary. Agriculture, science, politics and diplomacy.
The President of the National Council for the Khmer Language stated that in compiling the new dictionary, it is based on the dictionary of Samdech Preah Sangkhareach Chuon Nath, correcting some words and adding some new words that are not in the old dictionary and reading all the words. And edit some word classes. Prior to the launch, the team also developed a dictionary software to provide Khmer-language users with feedback for six months.
