European Chamber of Commerce to Hold Two-Day ASEAN-Cambodia Business Summit to Promote Cambodia's Investment Potential to European Investors
The summit will explore the economy of the Mekong region through meetings of leaders from Cambodia, Laos, Thailand and Vietnam to promote economic integration in the region and with other countries in the world, which will improve the business environment. Cambodia's economic growth.
Speaking at a press conference on September 25, 2023, Mr. Tassilo BRINZER, President of the European Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia, said that the ASEAN-Cambodia Business Summit is a forum to promote Cambodia's potential to foreign investors, especially companies. Who are investing in Southeast Asia to know the investment climate in Cambodia.
He said that in the past, the European Union has invested a lot in neighboring countries such as Vietnam, Thailand, Singapore, etc., but the amount of European companies investing in Cambodia is still small. Therefore, through this forum will show them that Cambodia can also be a good choice in the area to invest.
According to the President of the European Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia, there are currently only about 250 European companies investing in Cambodia, a small number.
Mr. Martin Brisson, Executive Director of the European Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia, said that the forum will include businessmen from the European Union, European investors who are investing in Cambodia, representatives of ASEAN countries, Cambodian government officials, representatives of civil society organizations. More than 200 civilians and local businessmen will attend the summit.
During the summit, the European Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia will release two key documents highlighting the investment climate in Cambodia: the White Paper 2024 and the 2023 Business Confidence Survey, a detailed survey. One by allowing business leaders in Cambodia to clearly describe the business environment in Cambodia.
It should also be informed that the ASEAN-Cambodia Business Summit will be attended by Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, and Ms. Cham Nimmol, Minister of Commerce.
Kampong Cham Provincial Authorities Plant More Than 2,000 Trees in Trapeang Preah Commune, Prey Chhor District
(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, together with Mr. Keo Omalis, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of Forestry Administration of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, led government officials, students and people to plant more than 2,000 trees on September 25. 2023 in Rolous village, Trapeang Preah commune, Prey Chhor district, Kampong Cham province.
Mr. Keo Omalis praised the Kampong Cham provincial authorities as well as the professional officers who have done a lot to participate in tree planting activities in the past, such as planting trees along highways, small roads, pagodas and schools. The tree, which is an important work to inspire our people to participate in planting trees to love and take care of protection as well.
