The provincial governor confirmed that trees provide many benefits to our people, from birth to death, all need to use wood. Therefore, our people must plant trees together and love to take care of trees together.
Spokesman of the Royal Government: The mission of Samdech Hun Sen to attend the 78th General Assembly of the United Nations brings great success to the motherland
(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Moha Bovathi Hun Manet, led a high-level delegation of the Royal Government to return home to Phnom Penh this morning, September 25, 2023, after attending the United Nations General Assembly. 78th in New York, USA
The Royal Government Spokesperson's Office, through an official press release obtained by Fresh News, confirmed that the President's third overseas mission for 5 days has achieved even greater new results for the nation and its people. Cambodia as well as the promotion of the Khmer national prestige on the international stage.
Within the framework of the United Nations, the Prime Minister of Cambodia met with Mr. Antonio Guterres, Secretary-General of the United Nations. The Secretary-General praised the Royal Government of Cambodia's Pentagon strategy, which is in line with the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals, and thanked Cambodia for sending officials to join peacekeeping missions in other countries.
He thanked the United Nations for its full support of Cambodia since the first general election in 1993 and the trial of former senior Khmer Rouge leaders, and stressed that the Royal Government of Cambodia would continue to Politics and cooperation with the United Nations without change.
He also spoke about the results of Cambodia's participation in peacekeeping under the United Nations and the promotion of human rights based on the rule of law.
In response, Antonio Guterres expressed satisfaction and emphasized that the United Nations will continue to support and cooperate with Cambodia to achieve the path of setting sustainable development goals for the benefit of the Cambodian people.
This intention was expressed in a meeting with His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia in New York, USA on September 23, 2023, when the Prime Minister visited there to attend the meeting of the organization. United Nations.
The content of the meeting, which was officially released on September 25, 2023, said that after the welcome, Mr. Nick Lagonovic informed the President about Pfizer's intention to seek more opportunities in Cambodia through Support and assistance from the Royal Government of Cambodia.
He added that Pfizer has reviewed and monitored the Pentagon Strategy - Phase 1 of the Royal Government, the 7th Legislature of the National Assembly carefully and found out that Pfizer can fulfill some work with the Royal Government of Cambodia, especially in contributing Improve the public health system in Cambodia.
The Prime Minister also highlighted that what the company wants to do more work in Cambodia is more in response to the key measures that the Royal Government of Cambodia put out to implement on August 24, 2023, especially related to Improving the quality of health services, which focuses on strengthening the capacity of primary health care providers.
He added that in order to strengthen the capacity to provide primary health care services, an important focus is on the supply of medicines, medical equipment and equipments in health centers and referral hospitals across the country.
At the same time, the Prime Minister stated that the Royal Government also pays attention to building a strong partnership between the public health sector and the private sector so that people can receive quality, safe and effective health care services. In this regard, Samdech encourages Pfizer to continue to seek investment and business opportunities in Cambodia, as well as to continue to promote relations with stakeholders, especially the Ministry of Health of Cambodia.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Oum Rath, Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province, on September 25, 2023, organized the dissemination of the first phase of the Royal Government's Pentagon strategy to civil servants throughout the province.
The ceremony was also attended by government officials, judiciary, prosecutors, police officers and many stakeholders.
It should be informed that the Royal Government of the 7th legislature led by Samdech Thibodi Hun Manet, the Prime Minister, officially announced the implementation of the first phase of the Pentagon Strategy at the first meeting of the Council of Ministers on the morning of August 24, 2023.
The announcement of the implementation of this final strategy follows that in the last 25 years, the Royal Government of Cambodia has achieved complete peace, national unity and complete territorial unity through Samdech Techo Hun Sen's win-win policy, successfully implemented the triangle strategy and The four-phase rectangular strategy, with great achievements in all areas, both political, social and economic, which makes Cambodia change its face should be very proud.
The Pentagon-Phase 1 strategy is implemented in line with the "One-Person System" approach and continues to focus on the "Efficiency Achievement" agenda through the implementation of the "Mirror, Bath, Brush, Treatment" approach. And surgery. ”
The main goals of this strategy include: maintaining the movement of peace, economic growth and overall development, as well as building and strengthening the foundations for accelerating national development through the building of resilience in all five areas, including: Public sector, economic sector, financial sector, human and social capital, and environmental sector and climate change response.
The first phase of the Pentagon Strategy has five mottos: "Employment Growth, Equity, Efficiency and Sustainability" and has five key priorities: "People, Roads, Water, Electricity and Technology", especially "Digital Technology" in response to the Fourth Industrial Revolution and Revolution. Digitalization of the Cambodian economy and society, as well as the need to promote economic productivity, are fundamental and important means of achieving the vision of Cambodia 2050.
The first phase of the Pentagon Strategy has five strategic goals, including:
The first phase of the Pentagon Strategy also gives high priority and urgency to the implementation of five major priority policies, 18 sectoral development policies and six priority policy programs to be implemented by 2023.
Ministry of Economy and Finance Continues Training of Commune / Sangkat Administrative Financial Assistants in Siem Reap and Oddar Meanchey Provinces
(Siem Reap-Oddar Meanchey): In the morning of Monday, September 25, 2023, the Ministry of Economy and Finance opened 124 training courses on public financial management at Commune / Sangkat Administration to provide financial assistance to Commune / Sangkat Administration of Siem Reap and Oddar Meanchey Provinces. People. This training is to strengthen, expand capacity and improve knowledge related to public financial management.
The event was chaired by Mr. Pich Sambath, Undersecretary of State, Representative of Dr. Hean Sahip, Secretary of State and Chairman of the Capacity Building Working Group of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, and attended by the Deputy Governors of Siem Reap and Oddar Meanchey Provincial Governors. Leading the Departments of Economy and Finance of Siem Reap and Oddar Meanchey Provinces and the leaders of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, as well as trainers and trainees.
The Undersecretary of State stressed that the five-day training is not only to support and implement public financial management reform, but also to contribute to the development of human capital, which is considered the highest priority in The first pentagonal strategy of the Royal Government in the 7th legislature of the National Assembly, which was announced to be implemented on August 24, 2023 recently.
Public financial management reform is one of the key priorities of the Royal Government's reform program, which has the vision of "transforming the Cambodian budget system into a system based on results or achievements and decentralization" and has now reached The final phase is the fourth phase, which focuses on "performance accountability", which was officially announced on March 20, 2023.
