The Ministry of Health has confirmed that one case of diabetes occurred in a 7-year-old girl living in Po Pech village, Chong Dong commune, Baray district, Kampong Thom province, who was admitted to Baray-Santuk District Referral Hospital on September 18, 2023 at 18:00. 25 minutes in the pediatric emergency room with high fever, vomiting and diarrhea. After the doctor treated the girl, she was no longer vomiting. The doctor did a quick test for dengue fever, but the result was negative.
Zika virus usually causes a mild, mild syndrome that occurs two to three days after a person has been bitten by a tiger mosquito carrying the Zika virus. Common symptoms include fever and redness of the skin. Some may have red eyes, muscle aches, joint pain and fatigue. These symptoms usually go away in two to seven days and the mortality rate is very low.
The Ministry of Health would like to reiterate to all Cambodians that the best prevention of diabetes is the same as the prevention of dengue fever and chickenpox, including the prevention of mosquito bites on pregnant women. Pregnant or planning to become pregnant and their sexual partners need to be extra careful to protect themselves from tiger mosquitoes that carry the H5N1 virus and sexually transmitted infections, which can be prevented by:
If it is not necessary, pregnant women, couples or women planning to become pregnant should not or should not travel to an area where there is an outbreak or are having an HIV infection and must apply the following precautions to the utmost. .
Men and women returning from an outbreak or having diabetes should practice safe sex (using a condom) or abstain from sex for at least 6 months after returning to prevent infection. Sexually Transmitted Infections (STIs)
Couples or women who are planning to become pregnant just after returning from an outbreak or having Zika should wait at least 6 months before attempting to become pregnant to ensure that there is no Zika virus transmission to the unborn baby. Birth.
Women who have unprotected sex but do not want to become pregnant due to the H5N1 virus should use contraception immediately by consulting a specialist at a public health facility.
* Pregnant women with symptoms of hepatitis B infection should have regular prenatal check-ups with a specialist at a public health facility and a properly trained doctor.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Hong So Hour, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Securities Exchange (CSX), said that during the last period, the share price of some listed companies has dropped significantly, but investors should not There is concern because this could be an opportunity for investors, both new and old, to buy cheaply and sell when stocks rise.
Mr. Hong Sochua said that the current share price is not due to the operating or financial situation of the listed company, but from external factors such as global economic crisis and geopolitical war.
He said that during the downturn in the market, it is a buying opportunity for investors.
He explained that for investing in the stock market, if we are short and medium term investors, we need to be agile and not too greedy, following the market regularly if the price rises moderately and should be sold because the stock price does not fluctuate. However, if you wait too long (or Mr. Phlun too) may be at risk of loss.
Long-term investors, on the other hand, do not care how much the price fluctuates, they should monitor the financial condition of the company to get an annual dividend. And the more trading in the market, the more profitable the long-term investment will be.
He added, "For example, for the share price of Sihanoukville Port, the price has risen to a maximum of more than 20,000 riel, if short-term investors seize the opportunity to benefit. However, even though the current share price of Sihanoukville Port has dropped from more than 20,000 to more than 12,000 compared to the IPO price, the price is still more than twice as high. Long bought at the original price is still double the profit.
He said that currently, in addition to the shares of Sihanoukville Port, there are also shares of other companies that are still cheaper.
He also said that although most prices fell, listed companies distributed more dividends each year.
According to Mr. Hong Sohour, if you look at the information on the figures and financial statements of listed companies in general, they have reported a good situation, with only a small number of companies showing some declining figures.
"For me, this decline is not due to a business situation, but to a situation that means it is not the situation in the company itself that is causing the decline in revenue, it is the situation at Outside that no one can control. "In the future, if the situation outside changes, the company will be able to make more profit."
Please be informed that up to now, 20 companies have registered for sale of securities, including 11 listed companies and 9 listed companies.
