On the occasion of the 65th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic ties between Cambodia and China, His Excellency also wished the Cambodia-China steel friendship to last forever. Samdech Hun Manet announces efforts to help East Timor become a full member of ASEAN
(New York, USA): Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Manet has announced his efforts to help East Timor become a full member of ASEAN, while Timor-Leste is set to become a full member of ASEAN by 2025.
During the meeting, the President and the President welcomed each other in a friendly atmosphere. The President expressed his deep gratitude to Cambodia, especially to Samdech Techo, Chairman of the King's Personal Advisory Council, who has always supported Timor-Leste, such as its bid to become the 11th member of ASEAN.
The President of East Timor expressed his intention to invite Samdech Techo to visit Timor-Leste at an appropriate time.
The President and the President discussed the work of strengthening relations and cooperation between the two countries, as well as the continuation of regional and global integration. In fact, within the framework of bilateral cooperation, the two leaders further discussed the expansion of cooperation between Cambodia and Timor-Leste in a number of potential areas, such as tourism, agriculture and people-to-people contacts.
The President also asked Cambodia to consider the possibility of joint investment and business in the aviation sector and the opening of direct flights, which will further increase the closeness between the people and economies of the two countries.
As for the continuation of regional and global integration, the President requested that Cambodia continue to share its experience in preparing for ASEAN membership, as well as continue to support Timor-Leste's bid to become the 11th member of ASEAN. The President expressed Timor-Leste's commitment to meet all the requirements for early ASEAN membership and not to allow Timor-Leste to become a burden on ASEAN.
With the approval of the roadmap for Timor-Leste's full membership in May 2023, the President requested the Cambodian side to support the designation of 2025 as the year ASEAN officially declares its full membership. Timor-Leste in ASEAN.
In response, the President fully supported this proposal and Cambodia will continue to support Timor-Leste, especially for its preparations for ASEAN membership as soon as possible. He also stressed that ASEAN should expand its membership to contribute to strengthening regional resilience.
