Samdech President Hun Manet announces for American investors to invest in Cambodia
(New York, USA): Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Manet has invited US investors and businessmen to explore the investment potential in Cambodia.
The three overseas missions after the formation of the Royal Government, in addition to seeking to expand diplomatic relations and cooperation, and attracting investors to Cambodia is the work that President Hun Manet highly values. In Indonesia, China, as well as in New York, the United States, Hun Manet often takes time off from meetings to attend business forums.
In New York, on Friday, September 22, 2023, President Hun Manet presided over the opening of the US-Cambodia Business Forum, organized between the American Chamber of Commerce and the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce. This forum is designed to be a meeting place between Cambodian and American businessmen and learn from each other, find opportunities for cooperation and open investment between Cambodia and the United States.
Samdech Thibodi Hun Manet expressed his great pleasure to participate in this forum. He also said that the US-Cambodia Business Forum reflects the importance of strengthening bilateral relations between Cambodia and the United States on the basis of mutual respect, mutual benefit and common values.
The Prime Minister emphasized that today's forum was held at an appropriate time and important for both countries as the global economy continues to be affected by uncertainty caused by major global challenges and trends. .
After presenting the indicators, Samdech Hun Manet said that earlier this year, Samdech had the opportunity to meet with the US delegation organized by the US Chamber of Commerce and the ASEAN Chamber of Commerce, and he hoped that Cambodia regularly welcomes and meets with members of the new government of Samdech.
The Prime Minister expressed hope that US investors will see investment opportunities and learn more about the economic potential and investment opportunities in Cambodia. As the saying goes, "Once seen is better than heard a thousand times", so let investors come and find out about Cambodia.
In addition, Samdech Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government will provide strong support for opportunities for business operation and expansion, as well as address all challenges, both old and new, in order to fully accelerate and develop the private sector. As a key partner of the Royal Government in promoting development for the mutual benefit and common prosperity of the environment.
According to Hun Manet, Cambodia continues to expand its market size through integration into global supply and value chains through bilateral and multilateral free trade agreements. Bilateral mechanisms such as the ASEAN Free Trade Agreement, the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement, the Cambodia-Korea Free Trade Agreement, and the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership (RECP).
Please be informed that in the first eight months of 2023, the trade volume between Cambodia and the United States reached more than 6,272 million dollars, a decrease of 5.6% compared to the same period in 2022 amounting to 6.645 million dollars. This is according to data from the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia.
The United States and Cambodia have a long history of friendly relations and cooperation, dating back to the 1950s, when diplomatic relations between the two countries were first established. Order of diplomatic relations between the two countries.
Economic ties have also grown rapidly, with bilateral trade flows reaching $ 13.5 billion by 2022, and the United States remains the largest export market for Cambodia. Especially for the market of clothing, textiles, footwear and travel products.
But US direct investment in Cambodia is still low, despite the United States being one of the largest sources of investment in the world. In Cambodia, the amount of direct investment from the United States continued to increase from 225 million US dollars in 2010 to 893 million US dollars in 2022.
