UN Secretary-General praises Cambodia's development policies in line with UN development goals
(New York, USA): UN Secretary-General Antonio Guterres praised the Royal Government of Cambodia's development policy, especially the Pentagon-Phase 1 strategy, which is in line with the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals. National.
This appreciation was made during His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, during a courtesy call and discussion with the Secretary-General of the United Nations on Friday, September 22, 2023 (New York time) at the organization's headquarters. United Nations, New York, USA.
According to the press release on the outcome of the meeting, during the meeting, the Secretary-General stressed that each country, especially low-income countries, must clearly formulate a policy framework for socio-economic development. In harmony with the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals.
Regarding the development policy, the Secretary-General praised Cambodia for formulating a socio-economic development strategy, the Pentagon strategy, which is in line with the Sustainable Development Goals.
Samdech Hun Manet informed the UN Secretary-General that in order to achieve the vision of Cambodia by 2050, the Royal Government of Cambodia has announced the implementation of the Pentagon Strategy - Phase 1, which is linked to the organization's sustainable development goals. United Nations.
It should be noted that the Pentagon Strategy will be implemented from the first phase, focusing on the living standards of the people and promoting sustainable national economic growth. This strategy has five mottos: growth, employment, equity, efficiency and sustainability. Prioritize the five key "people, roads, water, electricity and technology", especially "digital technology" in response to the Fourth Industrial Revolution and the digital revolution of the Cambodian economy and society.
