A man selling fried crickets is suspected to have died of an allergic reaction to rheumatoid arthritis after being treated at the Chea Sovanda Clinic in Por Sen Chey district.
But still not relieved, the wife went to the doctor for a second check-up at home, then the doctor gave the serum, still not relieved after the doctor left, the disease worsened, the wife And the siblings took their husbands in their own car to another clinic for rescue.
However, when the doctor arrived, he was told that the man was dead, so he took the body to Wat Champouvorn and complained to the police to detain a doctor who was treating him for questioning because he suspected that the man had died from a drug and serum reaction. .
This incident happened at 2:20 pm on September 22, 2023 in O'Dim Village, Sangkat Choam Chao III, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
The dead man, 37-year-old Va Channak, who sells fried crickets, and his wife, 37-year-old Keo Phal, who sells fried crickets, live in Ta Set village, Popel commune, Tram Kak district, Takeo province. Separately, the doctor who was detained by the police for questioning was Chea Sovannda, a 35-year-old man who lived in the village where the incident took place.
Police said that after receiving a complaint from the man's wife, the police force of the 3rd Chao Chao Police Station went to the location of the "Chea Sovannda" clinic and arrested Dr. Chea Sovannda for questioning on suspicion of treatment. Causing death. After that, the above police reported to the police of the Technical and Scientific Office of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police for an autopsy to find out the exact cause.
