President Hun Manet tells the world about the political maturity in Cambodia with a turnout of more than 84% (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): In a speech at the 78th General Assembly of the United Nations on September 22 In 2023, Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Manet briefed UN member states on the political maturity in Cambodia and the Cambodian people's willingness to exercise democratic rights.
Samdech Hun Sen highlighted that the process of building democracy in Cambodia has also progressed steadily. In July 2023, Cambodia successfully held general elections with 18 political parties contesting more than 8.2 million people. Turnout was 84.59 percent, the highest since the 1993 UN General Assembly.
The Prime Minister also highlighted that the election was widely assessed as free, fair and credible by thousands of observers, including 333 international observers from 65 countries.
Samdech Hun Sen added that Cambodia, like many other developing countries, still has a lot of work to do. Cambodia has ambitions to become a high-middle-income country by 2030 and a strong, vibrant, prosperous and prosperous country by 2050.
To this end, in line with the Secretary-General's call on Member States to implement the "Salvation Plan for Humanity and the Planet of the Apes", the Royal Government of Cambodia is committed to promoting progress through the introduction of the recently announced Pentagon Strategy as an agenda. Socio-economic development of Cambodia in the next 25 years. Interior Ministry spokesman: 65 people arrested for criminal and drug offenses on September 22 yesterday
(Phnom Penh): At least 65 suspects were arrested in criminal and drug offenses across Cambodia on September 22, 2023 yesterday. This was confirmed by General Khieu Sopheak, spokesman for the Ministry of Interior, to Fresh News on September 23, 2023.
General Khieu Sopheak added that of the 65 suspects, 56 were arrested in 26 criminal cases and nine were arrested in 10 drug offenses.
The United States has announced that it will work closely with President Hun Manet and resume development assistance to Cambodia (Video inside) (New York, USA): The United States has announced close work with Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Manet to expand cooperation between Cambodia and America. In addition, the United States has also announced that it will continue to provide development assistance to Cambodia.
On the sidelines of the 78th General Assembly of the United Nations General Assembly in New York, His Excellency Hun Manet received Acting US Deputy Secretary of State Victoria Nuland on September 22, 2023.
According to the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs, during the meeting, Ms. Victoria Nolen warmly welcomed the President to New York to attend the 78th General Assembly of the United Nations General Assembly. She also congratulated Samdech on the election of the Prime Minister of Cambodia as the 7th legislature of the National Assembly.
Ms. Victoria Nolen added that the United States welcomes the opportunity to expand cooperation between Cambodia and the United States by working closely with the President and wishes to see the President as well as the whole of Cambodia succeed.
The talks focused on finding ways and means to strengthen bilateral relations and cooperation to another level.
On that occasion, Ms. Victoria Nolen informed the President that the United States has decided to re-provide approximately US $ 18 million in assistance through the United States Agency for International Development (USAID), which the United States has suspended after. Election of the 7th National Assembly in 2023.
The two sides also discussed the repatriation of Cambodian citizens, with Victoria Nolen proposing to expedite the process of accepting them. In response, the President stated that the relevant ministries and institutions of Cambodia will review the procedures to run smoothly, quickly and efficiently.
He also asked the United States to pay special attention to Cambodians who are repatriated and who have health problems. Ms. Victoria Nolen stated that health issues are something that the United States has been paying close attention to and will continue to pay special attention to at the request of the President.
During the meeting, the two sides also discussed areas of mutual interest. CSX chief expects to open more than 50,000 trading accounts by the end of 2023
