According to President Hun Manet, Cambodia strongly opposes the threat or use of force in international relations, interference in internal affairs and the invasion of any independent state.
In a speech at the 78th session of the United Nations General Assembly in New York on September 23, 2023, the Prime Minister emphasized: "I have common concerns about global instability and rising instability. "The geopolitical tensions we are all experiencing right now."
The common concern that the President has highlighted before the United Nations is the worsening progress of the war in Ukraine and the devastating effects of the war, which underscores the loss of trust from member states and the lack of confidence in multilateralism.
Samdech Hun Manet also said that competition between superpowers and superpowers has pushed for the diversion of resources for the purpose of expanding security capabilities, thus making the resources needed. To address the impact of the Kovid 19 crisis and efforts to achieve the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development Goals.
In line with the theme "Building Confidence and Promoting Global Solidarity, Accelerating Action on the 2030 Agenda and the Sustainable Development Goals Towards Peace, Prosperity, Growth and Sustainability for All", said President Hun Manet. As the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech is committed to working closely with all Member States under the auspices of the United Nations to achieve the common aspiration towards development goals.
In addition to concerns over rising geopolitical tensions, President Hun Manet said climate change is also threatening the existence of humankind. Without ambitious and urgent action, the world would be on the rise. Rising poverty rates, hunger, the risk of epidemics and the deep cycle of instability and conflict.
Samdech Hun Sen emphasized that Cambodia is highly committed to peacekeeping operations to contribute to international peace, security and stability, which are essential for sustainable development.
The Prime Minister stated that in order to further contribute to this process, Cambodia has decided to stand as a member of the Organizing Committee of the Peace Building Commission (OCPBC) for the 2025-2026 term. Cambodia hopes to gain support for Cambodia's candidacy in this institution.
"Overall, despite our many challenges and instability, we can still build a better world for all by working together towards our common goals and goals," said Hun Manet. "Strengthen mutual trust and global unity."
He also stated that Cambodia fully supports the adoption of the "Political Statement of the Summit on Sustainable Development Goals" and the "Draft Decision of the Summit of the Future".
For the President, these documents will help the Sustainable Development Goals maintain its development trajectory as planned and achieve the goal by 2030.
By 2023, Cambodia has sent nearly 9,000 peacekeepers to 11 missions in 10 countries, including the Republic of Sudan, South Sudan, Chad, Central Africa, Lebanon, Mali, Syria, Cyprus, Yemen and the Democratic Republic of Congo. Demining, horizontal-vertical construction engineering, military level 2 hospitals, airport engineering, unexploded ordnance disposal, officers, officers and military observers.
Currently, 903 Cambodian troops, including 147 women, are serving in five countries: the Republic of South Sudan, Lebanon, Central Africa, Mali and Congo.
