Deputy Prime Minister Hang Chuon Naron made the remarks on the evening of September 22, 2023, during a ceremony to announce the results of the "iYunna" program to Cambodia. The ceremony was held at the Royal Academy of Cambodia with the participation of Mr. Ek Sam Ol, President of the Cambodia-China Friendship Association, Mr. Chang Chien, in charge of the Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia, and Ms. Zheng Yuan, Member of the Standing Committee of the Yunnan Provincial Party Committee.
Deputy Prime Minister Hang Chuon Naron emphasized that this year marks the 65th anniversary of China-Cambodia bilateral relations, and may the friendship, brotherhood and people of our two countries live forever. In the new era, the relationship between the two countries has become an "iron friendship" that is inseparable and closer from generation to generation. He believes that under the wise leadership of the two heads of government, our relationship will be even brighter.
He added that President Hun Manet had just completed his first official visit to China recently after receiving support from the people and the National Assembly to lead the government. This first official visit is a clear indication of the continued commitment to strengthening diplomatic relations between Cambodia and China and adhering to the one-China policy position.
According to Deputy Prime Minister Hang Chuon Naron, China and Cambodia are strategic partners in all areas of cooperation between the two countries for prosperity, peace and development in all fields. He also pledged to strengthen cooperation to build a community of common destiny between Cambodia and China in the new era, and he hoped that this cooperation would become a new model for other countries.
Ms. Zhengyuan said that the "iYunnan" program has traveled from China to Cambodia and has received a warm response and active participation from all walks of life in Cambodia. The performance of the competition in this program made people want to watch and love Yunnan of China and fully reflect the deep friendship between the people of Cambodia-China and the people of Cambodia-Yunnan.
On that occasion, Mr. Ek Sam Ol emphasized that Cambodia and China are good neighbors and true friends who know each other well. Yunnan is adjacent to ASEAN countries, including Cambodia, and has a long history of people-to-people friendship. The "iYunnan" Walk to Cambodia program further strengthens the relationship between Cambodia and China.
He said that mutual understanding and trust between the two peoples have added new strength to the traditional friendship between the two countries. The future of Cambodia-China friendship depends on the younger generation. He hoped that Cambodia and Yunnan Province will continue to strengthen cooperation and work together to create a better future and continue the friendly relations between Cambodia, China and Yunnan Province to the younger generation.
