China and other developing countries share the same historical experience and struggles, which have been facing difficulties and common development tasks, as well as similar opinions and demands on current international order and global governance. When the "Southern Globalization Report" was released in 2004, the United Nations Development Program explicitly identified China as a member of the "Southern Global".
No matter how inflated the United States and the West propaganda, it is impossible to separate the two sides. Recently, China has raised the vision of jointly building a common destiny community of the "southern universe" and jointly creating a new era of common development. It is estimated that the influence of the "southern universe" will gradually increase, bringing a new perspective on global governance.
