(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia this morning, September 22, 2023, held a meeting to disseminate and implement the sub-decree on the transfer of functions in the field of education, youth and sports to the municipal, district and Khan administration.
The launching ceremony was presided over by Mr. Abhisandiband Sar Sokha, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior and Chairman of the National Committee for Sub-National Democratic Development, and Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Education. Youth and Sports. The ceremony was held at the Ministry of Interior with the participation of relevant ministries, institutions, sub-national administrations, development partners and many other stakeholders.
Speaking at the opening ceremony, Dr. Hang Chuon Naron said that the transfer of duties was aimed at improving the management and provision of effective education, youth and sports services, quality, accountability, transparency, environment and social equity. Decision-making, accountability, and responsibility for managing and providing these services to municipal, district, and khan administrations throughout the country.
At the same time, Mr. Aphisandit Dr. Sar Sokha, at the closing ceremony, said that although these functions in the field of education, youth and sports have been transferred to the municipal administration, but the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports is still the institution to be Be responsible and accountable to the Royal Government and the National Assembly for the quality of these transferred educational services.
He added that the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports still plays an important role in formulating national policies, national strategic plans, national curricula, minimum standards and standards, teacher selection and training, technical support, monitoring and evaluation. Education, youth and sports, transferred to the municipal, district and khan administration.
According to Dr. Aphisandi Dr. Sar Sokha, the transfer of functions in the field of education, youth and sports to the municipal, district and Khan administrations is to empower the municipal, district and Khan administrations to take responsibility for managing, managing and providing education services to the people. Within its jurisdiction to promote accountability to citizens.
He advised that the council and the board of governors of the municipal, district and Khan administrations must be accountable to the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, as well as be accountable to the people in their jurisdiction over the results of leadership, management and implementation of educational functions. Transfer them to ensure that the implementation of these functions must be in line with policies, national strategic plans, national curricula, standards and standards.
