This is the third invitation to complete a mission abroad after Samdech received support from the Royal Government for a month. 102 Civil Servants and Teachers of Fine Arts High School Succeed in Pedagogical Training, Teaching Methods and Classroom Management
(Phnom Penh): 102 civil servants and teachers of the Fine Arts High School of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts have successfully completed the pedagogical training, teaching methods and classroom management.
Ms. Chheng Simon, Secretary of State, on behalf of Dr. Pheung Sakona, Minister of Culture and Fine Arts, closed the pedagogical training course on teaching methods and classroom management for civil servants and teachers of the Fine Arts Secondary School on the afternoon of September 21. This year 2023 at the Fine Arts High School.
Mr. Bunthorn Sokha Narith, Acting Director of the Cultural Framework Training School, said that this training course was the first and second phase with a total of 102 participants, 50 women.
He added that the four-day curriculum includes four main topics, including:
* First. Subjects of professional ethics for teachers to improve the morale of teachers, promote the dignity of teachers and improve the quality and efficiency of education
* Second. The lesson plan course allows participants to learn how to write a timeline and evaluate the results of each lesson on the indicators they set and evaluate after school.
* Third. The subject of anger management methods for effective teaching allows participants to find ways to maintain a positive attitude and solve problems.
* And the fourth. Teaching and classroom management methods allow participants to gain a deeper understanding of effective time management techniques, better classroom communication, art to share, encourage students, and better student-teacher engagement. .
Ms. Chheng Simon stated that the four-day training course was linked to the human capital development policy of the first pentagon, the first angle, and the third point set by the Royal Government of Cambodia for the seventh term to strengthen the quality of teacher training and Teaching methods as well as continuing to improve the lives and values of academic staff at all levels.
She added that this training course really contributed to help teachers who have the role of classroom management to better understand how the jurisdictional system in the management and development of human resources, management and responsibilities. Better monitor and evaluate the quality of students in their classrooms.
On that occasion, on behalf of the Minister and the Minister, she thanked the trainers and stated that the teachers are the trainees who are present today as potential human capital in the field of promotion work. Culture and fine arts, both now and in the future.
