(Phnom Penh): Famous food expert and chef Mr. Lou Meng sees that Cambodia is now in need of professional chefs with international degrees and is also an opportunity for young people who have just graduated or love food. This skill should be taken for future success.
Mr. Lou Meng claims that only a small number of chefs in Cambodia have an international degree, so those who love the food industry, especially the chef skills, should seize this opportunity. He points out that chefs with this country's degree are more likely to earn a higher salary since leaving work.
Mr. Lou Meng made this statement in an interview with the media on the evening of September 21, 2023, on the occasion of attending the graduation ceremony for students of the Food Institute of Cambodia in 2023. One degree is recognized by the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and the other by Switzerland.
He expressed the view that for those who have just graduated from Baccalaureate or want to change careers to the food industry can be considered, because in each country, there is a need for chefs because people need to eat delicious food, so of course. Need good chefs and obviously Cambodia also needs chefs with such degrees.
Bruno Cardone, Dean of the Food Institute of Cambodia, also said that seeing the importance of the food sector, the Royal Government of Cambodia, through the Ministry of Economy and Finance, has provided $ 500,000 to the institute to provide scholarships to poor students. According to the provinces that want to study this skill for 2 years.
Mr. Bruno Cardone added that the scholarships offered by the Food Institute of Cambodia to students after receiving assistance from the Royal Government are only covered by the study, not including accommodation and meals. However, he claimed that the institute also used to consider providing accommodation and food for poor students from the provinces.
