Keo Duong agrees, adding that Jayavarman IV's reign began in 928, but he did not ascend the throne in Yasodharapura because he had previously ruled the city at Chok Korkor. Already, this area is rich in natural stone, which is suitable for the construction of architectural structures of the capital easily, he also spent a lot of energy to build this city long ago.
