Through social media, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said: "In 2022, today I am leaving for the United Nations, today the new Prime Minister is leaving. "I have said many times (today I am the Prime Minister and in the future I will be the father of the Prime Minister)."
Samdech added: "Opposition groups are depressed, but now they may see the truth that has already happened. I have been the father of the Prime Minister for almost a month now. "Amrek dropped from his shoulder, leaving you to continue to take responsibility."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also sent his condolences to the Cambodian people living in the United States and Canada who will receive the new Prime Minister instead of Samdech.
Samdech Kittipritthbandit Chairs a Discussion on "Youth Participation for the Future of the Red Cross and Red Crescent / New Solutions in Humanitarian Work"
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, led a discussion between leaders and youth delegates from 11 national associations under the theme "Youth participation for the future of the Red Cross and Red Crescent / Solution New in humanitarian work.
The discussion took place after Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen officially opened the 20th Leaders' Meeting of the National Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies in Southeast Asia hosted by the Cambodian Red Cross this morning. September 20, 2023 at Sokha Hotel.
In this discussion, each association also raised the opinion of the above chairman. Then, the youth representatives of the 2nd Youth Forum held on 17-20 September 2023 from the 11 national associations hosted by Cambodia gave a presentation on the results of the 2nd Youth Forum to 20th Leaders of the National Association of Red Cross and Red Crescent Southeast Asia.
Please be informed that on the occasion of the Cambodian Red Cross hosting the 20th Leaders Meeting of the National Red Cross and Red Crescent Association of Southeast Asia from September 21-22, 2023, the Cambodian Red Cross will also host Home of the 2nd Youth Forum Meeting of the National Association of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies in Southeast Asia from September 17-20, 2023, after the National Association of Red Crescent Societies in Brunei in 2022.
Prior to the 20th Leaders' Meeting, a second Southeast Asian Youth Forum was organized, with a total of 55 youth delegates from 11 national associations and coordinators from the International Federation of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies.
This youth forum focuses on building the capacity of young people to communicate and solve problems using digital technology and other platforms by implementing innovative solutions in humanitarian work.
Please be informed that after the successful conclusion of the above-mentioned talks, the national and international guests and ambassadors of the 11 Southeast Asian countries took photos with a warm and pleasant atmosphere. Representatives of Samdech Techo Hun Sen talk with the people and build a concrete road donated by Samdech Techo to the people of O commune, Phnom Sruoch district, Kampong Speu province
