The Ministry of Health has officially launched a framework to promote primary health care in Cambodia.
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of September 21, 2023, Dr. O Vandin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health and Chairman of the Working Group for Development and Management of the Implementation Framework for the Promotion of Primary Health Care and represented by Professor Chheang Ra, Minister of Health. Invited to chair a workshop to disseminate the framework for implementing the promotion of primary health care.
On this occasion, Dr. O Vandin was very pleased, with deep gratitude and deep gratitude to Professor Chheang Ra, Minister of Health, who assigned her to represent the opening ceremony. Workshop to disseminate the framework for implementing this primary health care promotion.
She said that under the wise leadership of His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, the promotion of people's well-being is one of the top priority policies in the field of sectoral development, with the promotion of system modernization. Provide health services towards achieving global health coverage by the end of 2030.
Therefore, the Ministry of Health has identified nine key priority activities, including education, population health, improving the health status of the population, the fight against non-communicable diseases, and the prevention and spread of global infectious diseases. Health effects due to climate change, strengthening medical examinations, improving the quality of services, private sector regulation, human resource development and digital health.
Dr. O Vandin also updated the framework for the promotion of primary health care in 2023, which has six core activities, including:
Dr. O Vandin also emphasized that the framework for promoting primary health care is important for sub-national authorities to use to monitor the status of primary care in their areas and to set the vision for future health care. And strategies based on practical resources to achieve its goals.
(Kandal): Mr. Chhay Puthisen, Minister of Rural Development, instructed the Kandal Provincial Department of Rural Development to establish a group of spokespersons to disseminate information and achievements of the Royal Government as well as the Ministry of Rural Development to the general public.
The Minister made this suggestion when he met with 53 leaders and officials of the Department of Rural Development of Kandal Province on September 21, 2023 at the Department of Rural Development of Kandal Province.
In response to two requests from the Department of Rural Development of Kandal Province:
First, to address the lack of facilities for the officials of the Department of Rural Development of Kandal Province, the Minister instructed the Director General of Administration and Finance to prepare inventory at both the national and sub-national levels to have clear data on shortages and needs. Obviously.
Second, the proposal to include rural road project along the international border, supported by the French Agency for Development (AFD), the Minister instructed the Kandal Provincial Department of Rural Development to submit a proposal through the Ministry to be based on discussions with development partners. International.
Taking the opportunity, the Minister continued that in order to contribute to the implementation of the Pentagon Strategy and Vision 2030 and 2050, the Ministry of Rural Development has strived to achieve its vision is to improve the quality and value of the people. In rural areas, sustainable and environmentally, economically, socially and culturally.
The Royal Government, as well as the Ministry of Rural Development, continues to strive to turn rural areas into sectoral and prestigious rural areas in order to reduce the gap between urban and rural areas. The Ministry has four priority strategies:
First, to develop physical infrastructure and cellular communication to ensure the integration of rural areas and to promote the arteries of economic growth to rural areas.
Second, improve the living conditions of rural communities in order for rural people to live in a good, healthy and hygienic manner and comfortable.
Fourth, strengthen administrative support services and general affairs to strengthen institutions in order to serve the people in rural areas with integrity and high responsibility.
At the same time, the Minister instructed the leaders and civil servants of the Department of Rural Development of Kandal Province to have the following contents:
- The Department shall establish a group of spokespersons of the Department to provide information in order to participate in disseminating the achievements of the Royal Government as well as the Ministry of Rural Development to the general public.
- Departments must strive to cooperate with authorities at all levels to promote the work of the rural development sector better.
The department shall regularly review the monthly, quarterly, semi-annual meeting schedule to evaluate the work based on collective principles.
- There must be good internal unity for the department to be successful, including taking care of disabled officials, civil servants who are pregnant or have small children.
- The management of the department must encourage the active civil servants through the promotion of positions, money, medals or other means.
Dr. Sar Sokha: The Ministry of Interior is ready to promote and enhance all working relations with the ASEAN Secretary.
(Phnom Penh): In a meeting with Mr. Kao Kim Hourn, Secretary-General of ASEAN on the afternoon of September 21, 2023, Mr. Abhisit Bandit Sar Sokha, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, stated that the Ministry of Interior is always ready to promote and Promote communication on all relevant matters between the Ministry of Interior and the ASEAN Secretary.
