(Thailand): Mr. Kong Vibol, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Director General of the General Department of Taxation, on September 19-20, 2023, led a delegation from the General Department of Taxation on a study visit on the use of blockchain technology. ) At the Thai Tax Administration in Bangkok, Kingdom of Thailand, accompanied by Deputy Director General Lim De Lux, Deputy Director General Lim Huy Chiv and other relevant leaders of the General Department of Taxation.
Overall, the purpose of this study tour is to learn about the evolution of digitalization of regional and global fiscal administration, which is in line with the Cambodian Digital Economic and Social Policy Framework (2022-2035).
However, the main focus of the study tour was on the Thai Tax Administration's efforts to understand the introduction of BlockchianTechnology in the management of value-added tax refunds. And the creation of electronic invoices (E-Invoice) to avoid and prevent invalid invoices, exchange of customs data, as well as monitoring transactions related to real estate transfer.
After a courtesy call, the delegation of the General Department of Taxation continued to meet with the expert team of the Thai Tax Administration to study, discuss and gain experience on key points, including:
2: The main legal basis for the use of blockchain technology in the tax administration, such as the evolution of the tax administration system, laws and regulations related to tax policy.
3: Systems and programs that the Thai Fiscal Administration has introduced the current blockchain technology.
4. Stakeholders, the main objectives of which are to cooperate in the design, development and implementation of the blockchain technology system.
The visit came to a successful conclusion with the acquisition of new ideas, experiences and key practices as a basis for learning, understanding and consideration of the adoption of Blockchain Technology. In the future data management operations of the General Department of Taxation, which will help increase the ability to manage the collection of tax revenue to another level in a sustainable manner.
