(Takeo): Mr. Chhay Rithi Sen, Minister of Rural Development, recommended to the leaders and civil servants of the Department of Rural Development of Takeo Province to continue their efforts to implement rural development work to improve the value of life of rural people in a comprehensive environment. Socio-economic and cultural in line with the vision and pentagon strategy of the Royal Government of the 7th legislature.
These recommendations were made on the occasion of Minister Chhay Rithy Sen's meeting with the people of Thmey Village Movement Community in Champou Prek Village, Champa Commune, Prey Kabas District, Takeo Province on September 21, 2023.
After listening to the progress report of the new village movement community, the Minister brought a greeting message from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister, and also donated a set of speakers to the community.
At the same time, he also inspected the achievements of the new village movement community, including: kindergartens, offices of the Village Development Committee, children's parks, ponds, schools, handicrafts, family weaving and family fish ponds.
In the afternoon of the same day, Mr. Chhay Rithi Sen, with the participation of Mr. Moul Vichet, Deputy Governor of Takeo Province and the accompanying delegation, met with the leaders and officials of the Department of Rural Development of Takeo Province.
Minister Chhay Rithy Sen instructed the leaders and civil servants of the Department of Rural Development of Takeo Province as follows:
1. Continue to strive to participate in the implementation of rural development work to promote the value of life of rural people in a comprehensive environment, both economically, socially and culturally, in line with the vision and strategy of the Royal Government of the 7th legislature.
2. Cooperate well with relevant ministries, institutions, departments and local authorities at all levels by fulfilling the role of technical staff of the Takeo Provincial Administration.
3. Strengthen the rules, procedures, meetings, monitoring, evaluation and monitoring of monthly, quarterly, semi-annual meetings.
4. Strengthen internal unity to work more effectively and achieve more good results in the new 7th legislature of the Royal Government.
5. Establish a spokesperson for the Department to provide information and coordinate with the spokesperson of the provincial hall and the spokesperson of the Ministry of Rural Development in order to participate in disseminating the achievements of the Royal Government as well as the Ministry of Rural Development to the public.
