Russia launched a series of airstrikes on the Ukrainian capital Kiev and several other Ukrainian cities on Thursday, injuring 18 people and damaging infrastructure across the country, officials said. This is according to the release by Reuters on Thursday, September 21, 2023.
In the wake of Russia's airstrikes on Kiev, Ukrainian President Vladimir Putin is attending the UN General Assembly, calling for Russia to be expelled from one of the five permanent members of the Security Council. Sanctions for invading Ukraine
Natural disasters! Lightning strikes a young man in Chantrea district
(Svay Rieng): Light rain caused lightning to strike a young man, causing his death at Tuol Pchak, Tuol Sdey village, Tuol Sdey commune, Chantrea district, Svay Rieng province. This incident surprised the villagers and their families at 2:40 pm on September 20, 2023.
Chantrea district police said that the victim was named Von Wanglong, 23 years old, a farmer, currently residing in Tuol Sdey village, Tuol Sdey commune, Sontrea district, Svay Rieng province. Before the incident, there was rain, thunder and lightning, then suddenly there was lightning and a heavy lightning strike, causing the farmer man to die on the hill.
In connection with this natural disaster, Chantrea district authorities have called on all residents to be extremely careful when it rains, wind, thunder and lightning to go to a safe place to prevent possible accidents.
The bodies were handed over to the parents by the police for a traditional ceremony at home.
Ministry of Posts Disseminates Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women Online
(Kandal): Two senior officials of the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications of Cambodia visited Kandal province to promote the Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination against Women and the work of gender mainstreaming and dissemination of online harassment. And human trafficking.
This program was held on September 20, 2023, which is a workshop to disseminate and monitor the implementation of the CED Convention and the main recommendations of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen to civil servants of the Department of Posts and Telecommunications of Kandal Province.
Ms. Ros Sokha, Secretary of State and Chair of the Working Group on the Work of the National Council of Cambodia for Women of the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications, said that the purpose of this workshop was to disseminate the 12 recommendations of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen and to disseminate the Convention on Elimination of all forms of discrimination against women and gender mainstreaming, advocacy on the disappearance of online abuse and human trafficking.
Please be informed that the National Council of Cambodia for Women is a national mechanism that monitors the implementation of recommendations and gender mainstreaming in all ministries, departments and institutions, and the working group that is visiting now is a working group in the Ministry of Posts. And Telecommunications for the work of each department to collect reports to the National Council of Cambodia for Women.
