Senate Fully Approves Draft Law on the Establishment of the Ministry of Inspection (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): During the Extraordinary Session of the 4th Legislature, the Senate reviewed and fully approved the draft law on the establishment of the Ministry of Inspection with unanimous vote. 59 of the total number of senators, which was presided over by Dr. Simka, Acting President of the Senate, this morning, September 21, 2023.
This draft law is a legal tool in response to the political program of the Royal Government of the seventh mandate and the Pentagon-Phase 1 strategy, continuing to carry out comprehensive and in-depth reforms that will focus on improving governance and institutional capacity. Favorable environment for socio-economic development, human capital development, economic diversification, increasing competitiveness, sustainable private sector development, environment and digital society.
After the two senators commented and asked questions, Mr. Huot Hak, Minister of Inspection, answered, explained and accepted the suggestions and recommendations of the two senators and informed the Senate meeting about the necessity of Renaming the Ministry.
After listening to the Minister's explanation, the Senate reviewed and unanimously approved the draft law on the establishment of the Ministry of Inspection without amendment by 59 votes out of the total number of senators.
It should be noted that this draft law has 10 articles and was approved by the National Assembly for the first time on September 14, 2023 at the first session of the National Assembly of the 7th legislature. Mr. Nut Sa An Conducted a Training Course on National and International Standards on Respect for Human Rights and Duties and Responsibilities of Kratie Provincial Judicial Police Officers
(Kratie): Mr. Nuth Sa An, Chairman of the National Committee Against Torture, on September 21, 2023, opened a training and education session on national and international norms related to respect for human rights and the role and responsibilities of the National Committee against Torture. To the Judicial Police in Kratie Province.
The training was attended by members of the National Committee Against Torture, Mr. Sreng Sopheap, Deputy Governor of Kratie Province, Deputy Prosecutor of the Provincial Court, Deputy Provincial Police Commissioner, Deputy Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie, District Governors, Municipal Police Inspectorate Municipal, district, provincial, prison, provincial, relevant departments, units and representatives of NGOs, human rights organizations, more than 150 people.
He said that during the training and dissemination, there were also presentations of national and international standards related to respect for human rights and national and international norms related to the fight against torture, as well as the role and duties of the National Committee against Torture. In this outreach training, there were also some suggestions to (NEC) to establish a committee at the provincial level.
The chairman of the National Committee Against Torture stated that torture and ill-treatment were not necessary measures to be taken against those deprived of their liberty, instead they were wrong. Laws and serious human rights violations.
The South Korean Foreign Ministry has said that North Korea's defense minister and North Korean military chief were among the new individuals targeted as the new sanctions were in response to various illegal activities. North Korea, which threatens the international community as well as the peace and stability of the Korean Peninsula.
