Cambodia Prepares for Global Conference on Assistance to Landmine Victims and Explosive Remnants of War and Disability Rights from October 17-19
(Phnom Penh): On September 21, 2023, at the Office of the Mine Authority, Dr. Ly Thuch, Senior Minister and First Deputy Chairman of the Mine Authority, chaired an inter-ministerial meeting to prepare for the Global Conference on Assistance to Mine Victims and Explosive remnants of war and the third disability rights that Cambodia will host will take place from October 17-19, 2023.
On behalf of His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister and Chairman of the Mine Authority and on behalf of the Cambodian people, Senior Minister Ly Thuch expressed his pride that Cambodia has become the first country in Asia and the third in the world to be The host is hosting the Global Conference under the framework of the Ottawa Convention, which Cambodia became a State Party in 2000.
On that occasion, the Senior Minister requested all parties concerned to continue to work closely, pay close attention to all aspects and warmly welcome the delegation to be invited to attend the three-day global conference. This is for the honor and benefit of the country and the people of Cambodia as a whole.
