Ministry of Public Function Introductory Meeting on the Content of the Royal Decree on the Principles for Appointing Advisors and Assistants in the Executive Institutions
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Youk Bunna, Permanent Secretary of State and Director of the Royal School of Administration of the Ministry of Public Works, on the morning of September 21, 2023, chaired a meeting to introduce the content of the Royal Decree on the principles for the appointment of advisors and assistants in the institution. Executive. The meeting was also attended by representatives from various ministries and institutions at the Royal School of Administration.
Speaking on the occasion, Mr. Youk Bunna said that the meeting was organized to discuss the advisors and assistants of the Office of the Council of Ministers and the Secretariat of State, as well as the advisors and assistants of the Prime Minister, Deputy Prime Minister and Senior Minister.
Mr. Youk Bunna further stated that this Royal Decree sets out the principles, conditions and procedures for the appointment of advisors and assistants in the executive branch in order to strengthen the administrative hierarchy in order to improve the efficiency of public administration as well as the efficiency of Advisor and Assistant in the Executive Organization.
He further claimed that this Royal Decree applies to all advisors and assistants in the executive branch, except for advisors and assistants of councils, authorities, committees or mechanisms of the Royal Government, which shall be determined by a separate legal document and this Royal Decree. There is no scope for application to the Cabinet of the Prime Minister, Deputy Prime Minister, Senior Minister and Minister, which shall be determined by a separate legal document.
