Mr. Sous Yara led a delegation of the National Assembly of Cambodia to attend the "Closing Ceremony of the Annual Meeting of the Kyungsang-Bukdo Provincial Volunteer Doctors Association" of South Korea
(Phnom Penh): At the invitation of the Kyungsang-Bukdo Volunteer Doctors Association, Mr. Sous Yara, Chairman of the National Assembly Committee on Foreign Affairs, International Cooperation, Propaganda and Information of the National Assembly and a Member of Parliament for Kampong Thom Province, led the Cambodian delegation. Participated in the "Closing Ceremony of the Annual Meeting of the Kyungsang-Bukdo Volunteer Doctors Association" in Daegu, Gyeongsang-bukdo, Republic of Korea.
The Association of Volunteer Doctors has been sending a team of volunteer doctors to Cambodia to examine and treat the Cambodian people in the "Parliamentary Program for the Welfare of the People" every year since 2013 on the 11th. On August 13, 2023, a group of 106 volunteer doctors visited and treated a total of 4,030 people and government officials in Kampong Thom province.
Mr. Sous Yara said that the relationship between Cambodia and Korea has been closely linked from the grassroots level, and especially the presence of Korean volunteer doctors has really built the confidence of local people in the cooperation between the two countries. Cambodia and Korea.
He also recalled that the cooperation between Kyungsang-Bukdo and Cambodia dates back to the organization of the Kyungyoo Expo 2006 in Siem Reap, based on the historical ties of the Angkor-Sila period.
On this occasion, Mr. Sous Yara, on behalf of the National Assembly President Khuon Sodary, also brought a medal to the volunteer doctors as a thank you for the contribution to the local welfare sector in Cambodia of the Medical Association. Volunteer in Kyungsang-Bukdo province for more than 10 years.
Taking the opportunity of this visit, on September 18, 2023, Mr. Sous Yara also led a delegation to visit Yongnam University, a university established by former President Park Geun-hye to train the initiative. The New Village Movement (Saemaul Undong), which promoted the post-war rural development and local economy of the Republic of Korea.
