The following is the sub-decree of the President: The Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie joins the security forces to maintain order in the mission of Samdech President Hun Manet to attend the "78th United Nations General Assembly" in New York
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of September 21, 2023, the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie joined forces to maintain security and order during the mission of His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, leading a delegation of the Royal Government of Cambodia to attend the "General Assembly" The 78th United Nations ”in New York, USA from September 21-25, 2023.
According to the announcement of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Cambodia, accompanied by Samdech Hun Manet, including: Deputy Prime Minister Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, key officials of the Royal Government and some leaders of the private sector of Cambodia.
The main theme for this year's discussion is "Rebuilding Confidence and Solidarity in the World: Promoting Action on the 2030 Agenda and Sustainable Development Goals for Peace, Prosperity, Progress and Sustainability for All."
According to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, the content of the President's speech at the UN General Assembly will focus on three key areas, including the global context, Cambodia's socio-economic progress and Cambodia's commitment to the revolutionary activities of the goals. Sustainable Development (SDGs). The President will also hold bilateral meetings with the UN Secretary-General and a number of foreign dignitaries during his stay in New York.
During the meeting, Deputy Prime Minister Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, will attend the 15th Regional and International Dialogue, including the 15th ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting and the Economic Cooperation Organization (ECO). The Deputy Prime Minister is also scheduled to hold separate bilateral talks with his counterparts from various countries.
