The blood donation program was held on the afternoon of September 20, 2023 under the chairmanship of Dr. Sik Bonna, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, Representative of the Minister of Health, and attended by Dr. Sok Phong, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, Under Secretary of State and Director General. Deputy Director General of Health Technology, as well as Mr. and Mrs. who are the leaders of Ang Duong Hospital and many other National Blood Transfusion Centers.
The director of Preah Ang Duong Hospital said that Preah Ang Duong Hospital will continue to cooperate with the National Blood Transfusion Center more closely to save lives.
Dr. Sik Bonna, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, congratulated about 120 health workers at Ang Duong Hospital who volunteered to donate blood to the hospital's regular blood donation program under the slogan "Save lives, donate blood." All together.
"Blood transfusions save the lives of people who need blood, people with anemia, people who lose blood suddenly, people with certain blood disorders and people with cancer," he said.
He said that this gesture shows the kindness of doctors who, in addition to their duties as civil servants, health professionals, respect the right ethics, in addition, our doctors donate blood to patients who need blood more. Donating blood is a charitable act that can save lives.
On that occasion, Dr. Sok Pheng, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, instructed the National Blood Transfusion Center to pay attention to the donors who volunteered to donate blood as food or gifts when they donated blood to increase blood pressure. Repeat.
At the same time, attention must be paid to the safety of blood, that is, blood taken from the National Blood Transfusion Center must ensure the safety of patients and encourage people to participate in donating more blood. People's voluntary blood is still limited.
