(Phnom Penh): Every year, the United Nations designates September 21 as a special day for countries around the world to celebrate "International Day of Peace" to show their shared commitment to the values of peace as well as Reminiscent of the heroes who contributed to achieving peace.
In 2023, the celebration of Peace Day under the theme "Action for Peace: A Joint Commitment to Global Goals", with a core value of action for peace, will call on all stakeholders to contribute to the development goals. Sustainable, successful in ending destruction, poverty, hunger, climate change and ensuring prosperity for all.
To congratulate and join the international community in celebrating the "International Day of Peace", His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, issued a message on the occasion of the International Day of Peace on September 21, 2023.
Through this message, the Prime Minister reaffirmed to his compatriots that the Royal Government of Cambodia, the seventh legislature, will continue to uphold "peace" as the highest value and adhere to the slogan "Thank you for peace" by Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
The difficult past of our nation was completely closed in 1998 after the successful implementation of the "win-win policy" of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, which brought peace to the nation. Full national unity and complete territorial unity. In the last 25 years, peace has given Cambodia the opportunity to change its proudest face under the cold shadow of the King, the highest deity.
