The Draft Royal Decree on the Organization and Functioning of the Public Administration Reform Committee was reviewed and discussed at a meeting of the Council of Ministers chaired by Samdech Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, this morning, September 20, 2023. .
According to a press release from the Office of the Council of Ministers, in order to promote more effective public administration reform, a new draft Royal Decree on the organization and functioning of the Public Administration Reform Committee (CSRC) has been launched. ) Was prepared with some edits from the old Royal Decree. Adapting this content to suit the new context of public administration reform.
The four sub-committees of the CCC These include: 1) Sub-Committee on Public Service Innovation and Innovation, 2) Sub-Committee on Public Service Excellence, 3) Sub-Committee on Human Resource Management, Institutions and Salaries, and 4) Sub-Committee on Capacity Building for Officials.
Based on this new arrangement, separate institutional mechanisms in charge of reform, such as the Salary System Reform Working Group and the Model Public Service Unit Evaluation Working Group, will be incorporated into the institutional mechanisms leading and coordinating public administration reform. Determined by the draft of this new Royal Decree.
The draft Royal Decree on the Organization and Functioning of the Public Administration Reform Committee was prepared in 21 articles and was approved by the Plenary Session of the Council of Ministers.
Please note that public administration reform is one of the priority policies of the Royal Government in the new legislature. In this regard, the appointment of the Minister's role as Deputy Prime Minister and the appointment of advisors and assistants have also been revised.
