(Phnom Penh): National and international businessmen have expressed their congratulations to the Koh Ker temple, which has been officially inscribed on the UNESCO World Heritage List, which will make the world know Cambodia better, leading to a positive impact. Attracting tourists and foreign investors.
Neak Oknha Lim Heng, Vice President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, said that the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, which represents the private sector throughout the country and abroad, congratulated the Koh Ker temple site, which is inscribed on the World Heritage List. He is in Riyadh, Saudi Arabia by UNESCO on September 17, 2023.
He added that the inclusion of the World Heritage Site, in addition to influencing the attraction of international tourists, also contributes to attracting foreign investors to invest in sectors such as transportation, restaurants, restaurants, hotels, as well as agriculture and tourism. Process various foods to serve and supply to tourists.
Meanwhile, Mr. CAO ZHENWEI, CEO of WICAM, who decided to invest in the provision of internet services in Cambodia, expressed his congratulations that the ancient temples of Cambodia are now included as a World Heritage Site.
He also said that he will continue to promote Cambodian cultural heritage to the Chinese people through the Internet so that they know Cambodia well to contribute to attracting Chinese tourists to Cambodia.
He said that the development of technology will make it easier for people in China and other countries to access information quickly and widely.
Mr. Thuon Sinan, a businessman in the field of tourism, also said that the inclusion of Koh Ker Temple as a World Heritage Site will wake up from Cambodia to the world that Cambodia is a peaceful country.
He noted that the Koh Ker temple seems to be of great interest to Thai tourists and hopes that after more public and private publicity about the inclusion of it as a World Heritage Site, it will become more attractive. Before.
At the same time, on behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia and through the Ambassador as well as the Director General, Minister Tho Chetha expressed his gratitude to the French Republic, especially AFD, which for more than two decades has always provided support and support to the country. Cambodia The people of Cambodia, both technical and financial assistance in all areas, especially the rehabilitation and development of water resources and meteorology in Cambodia.
Speaking at the meeting, the Minister informed the French side that he was considering the possibility of holding an annual forum between development partners and the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology to strengthen cooperation and investment in water resources and meteorology in Cambodia.
At the same time, Minister Tho Chetha also asked the French side, especially AFD, to help mobilize other development partners to contribute to the restoration and strengthening of water resources and meteorological systems in Cambodia.
The meeting ended in a cordial and cordial atmosphere, and both sides expressed their willingness to continue to strengthen cooperation in the field of water resources and meteorology.
