In fact, in 2022, Cambodia suffered from floods affecting 25 provincial capitals, causing more than 100,000 families to suffer and food shortages. Under the intervention of the Royal Government of Cambodia, the Cambodian Red Cross and other philanthropists, the families of the victims received emergency food aid and rice seeds from the Royal Government to rehabilitate the cultivated land.
