Samdech Kittipritthbandit Planted a Tree to Celebrate the 20th Leaders' Meeting and the 2nd Youth Forum of the National Association of Red Cross and Red Crescent Society of Southeast Asia
(Kampong Speu): On the morning of September 20, 2023, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, presided over a tree planting ceremony to celebrate the 20th Leaders' Meeting and the 2nd Youth Forum. National Association of Cambodian Red Cross and Red Crescent, Southeast Asia Region, held at the Buddhist Cultural Center in Suramarit National Park, Kosomak Kirirom, Kampong Speu Province.
The tree planting ceremony was attended by about 700 people, including dignitaries, leaders from ministries, youth institutions of the Cambodian Red Cross from Kampong Speu Branch, Sihanoukville Branch, Kandal Branch, Phnom Penh Branch, together with Branch Committee Chairman from Branch Each of the other 21 branches.
On the occasion of the Cambodian Red Cross to host the 20th Leaders Meeting and the 2nd Youth Forum of the National Association of Red Cross and Red Crescent Southeast Asia from 17 to 22 September 2023 after the Association Brunei Red Crescent hosts 2022
This event reflects the Cambodian Red Cross International's commitment and responsibility, as well as its strong belief that by working together, we can do more and more effectively.
Prior to the leadership meeting, a second Southeast Asian Youth Forum was held, the first of which took place in Bandar Seri Begawan, Brunei. The second Youth Forum, held from 17 to 20 September, will have a total of 55 youth delegates from 11 national associations and coordinators from the International Federation of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies (LRC).
This youth forum will focus on building the capacity of young people to communicate and solve problems using digital technology and other platforms by implementing innovative solutions in humanitarian work.
The youth delegation also planted 2,000 trees on an area of more than 2 hectares and on the farm around Chulamoni Stupa on September 20 at the Buddhist Cultural Center in Suramarit, Kosomak Kirirom National Park. There is cooperation from the Ministry of Environment, the Ministry of Agriculture and the President of the Center.
The tree planting aims to raise public awareness of nature-based solutions as well as encourage youth participation in tree planting to address climate crisis.
