The WTO Dispute Resolution Commission last month backed Washington on a tariff dispute with Beijing, stating that it had found that China had acted in violation of its obligations with the WTO by imposing additional tariffs. On US goods in response to US tariffs on steel and aluminum.
The United States will impose a 25 percent tariff on steel imports and a 10 percent tariff on aluminum imports from countries including China in 2018 under Donald Trump. In response, Beijing has announced additional tariffs to be applied to imports of some goods originating in the United States.
Reuters reports, citing a statement from the Chinese Ministry of Commerce, that the decision of the WTO Dispute Resolution Commission was "illegal."
The Chinese Ministry of Commerce said the US tariff exemption on steel and aluminum imports was "a unilateral measure and protectionism found to be in violation of WTO rules."
China urges the United States to take corrective action, abide by WTO rules and correct its "illegal measures" as soon as possible.
Beijing's call comes as tensions between China and the United States remain high despite recent efforts to boost bilateral ties.
EU not afraid of trade war with China (Video inside) (Brussels): The European Union reiterated last weekend that its economy could survive any retaliation from China after the city. Beijing has warned that Brussels' investigation into China's electric car subsidy would hurt trade ties.
The probe could see the EU trying to protect European carmakers by imposing fines on cars it believes are being sold at unfairly low prices.
The probe comes after France urged Brussels to take stronger action to protect European industry against growing threats from China and the United States.
