Stong District Governor Instructs Commune Administration to Regularly Monitor and Report Flood Situations
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Say Kim Lam, Governor of Stong District, Kampong Thom Province, on the afternoon of September 19, 2023, inspected the flood situation of Stung Stong in Banteay Stong and Rong Roeung communes.
On that occasion, Mr. Say Kim Lam instructed the commune chiefs in all communes to monitor and report on the current flood situation in their locality to the district administration regularly and in a timely manner.
He called on local people to be vigilant against floods that could cause danger at any time, such as flooding of crops, damage to roads, national roads, infrastructure or even drowning. In particular, care must be taken to take care of small children who like to play in the water or leave young children alone at home without the elderly who may be at risk of drowning.
The governor of Stong district also instructed all communes to inspect the sewer system which may be clogged due to garbage, to restore and reopen it widely to release the water to drain faster in order to save crops. And other infrastructure, especially the rice fields of the people who are flooding in time.
Mr. Say Kimlam advised all communes affected by the flood to collect statistics and other impacts, especially infrastructure, farmers' rice and other impacts from the floods and immediately report to the district administration. .
It should be noted that on the afternoon of September 19, 2023, at Stung Stong station, the water level of Stung Stong was 5.55 meters higher than yesterday, 0.01 meters and the emergency point was 5.80 meters.
The General Department of Customs organized a two-day workshop to disseminate the budget for the new phase of the "Achievement Budget" program to 100 customs and excise officials from all over the country in Kep province.
(Kep): The General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia organized a dissemination workshop on the budget of the new program "Achievement Budget" under the framework of the Public Financial Management Reform Program for 100 leaders and customs and excise officials from the Customs Unit. And central and local excise authorities throughout the country. This workshop started from 18 to 19 September 2023 at Sangkhamit Hotel, Kep Province.
The opening ceremony was held in the presence of Dr. Kun Nhim, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, and was attended and presented by the leadership and professional officers of the General Secretariat of the Ministry of Economy and Finance. General Department of Budget and General Secretariat of the Public Financial Management Reform Steering Committee.
The purpose of this workshop is to disseminate information on the current status and direction of the budget system, information on the achievements of the Public Financial Management Reform Program, Phase 4, 2023-2027, Budget Reform Strategy 2018-2025, budget planning. And preparation of achievement agreements.
