Samdech President Hun Manet sets May 26 next year for the 4th Capital, Provincial, Municipal, District and Khan Council elections
(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia, His Excellency Hun Manet, has set May 26, 2024 for the fourth election of the Capital Council, Provincial Council, Municipal Council, District Council and Khan Council. This is according to the decision to announce the date of the fourth election to elect the council, which Fresh News received on September 19, 2023.
Please be informed that the third council election was held in 2019.
According to the Law on the Election of the Capital Council, Provincial Council, Municipal Council, District Council and Khan Council, the term of office is 5 years and shall expire when the new council takes office. Council members shall be elected by free, fair and just universal suffrage by secret ballot.
WASHINGTON (Reuters) - Canada's allegations that India may have been involved in the shooting death of a Sikh activist on its territory have been fueling a heated diplomatic row between Ottawa and New Delhi. Classes expelled senior diplomats from their respective countries, deteriorating relations between the two countries.
In the face of tensions, Canada has said it has fired an Indian diplomat who is considered by Canadian Foreign Minister Mélanie Joly to be the head of India's intelligence service in Canada. In response, the Indian Foreign Ministry on Tuesday rejected the allegations made by Canada and took the same retaliatory action, leaving five days for a Canadian diplomat to leave the country.
