Russian Defense Minister to visit Tehran on Tuesday
Since Western sanctions on Russia following the invasion of Ukraine in February 2022, Tehran and Moscow have deepened their bilateral ties, especially in the military.
Last month, Russian Deputy Foreign Minister Sergei Ryabkov said Russia's military cooperation with Iran would not succumb to geopolitical pressure after reports that Washington had asked Tehran to stop selling drones. Moscow.
Tehran has admitted sending drones to Russia, but said it had sent them before Russia's invasion of Ukraine. Moscow has denied that its forces used Iranian drones in Ukraine.
