The statement by Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo came after a group of people attacked his accusations of his visit to China, as well as his declaration of one-China policy as a loss of national sovereignty. As a donkey or a satellite of China and so on.
Addressing a forum with workers in Bati district, Takeo province, on Tuesday morning, September 19, 2023, Samdech Hun Sen stated that Cambodia is a small country, but Cambodia is independent and has national sovereignty, and Samdech sat down to talk on an equal footing with Chinese leaders as well as leaders of other countries.
During his first official visit to China from September 14 to 17, President Hun Manet announced a clear political position following the old government's policy of adhering to the one-China policy and further promoting relations and cooperation. Deepen operations with China.
Both choosing to visit China for the first time, as well as presenting its foreign policy line with China, have led a number of political commentators, including radicals, to oppose the government, denouncing what the president did as a Chinese satellite. Loss of national sovereignty and loss of national interest.
Responding to these allegations, Samdech Hun Manet affirmed to the people that the leadership of Samdech as well as the leadership of the Cambodian People's Party does not lose the value of Cambodia's national sovereignty to become a donkey or a satellite of any country. .
In addition to reaffirming the leadership position of defending the national interest, the people defending the national sovereignty, Samdech Hun Sen also presented Cambodia's foreign position to the compatriots.
Mekong River continues to rise for the second time, Tbong Khmum provincial officials call on residents to be extra vigilant as the river flows into the Boeung Prek Dam
