(Phnom Penh): Tourism practitioners are optimistic that after the Koh Ker temple resort is inscribed on the UNESCO World Heritage List, it will help boost the number of tourists visiting Cambodia who will be involved in the restoration of tourism. Caused by an epidemic of Kovid 19 disease.
Ms. Chhay Sivlin, President of the Cambodian Tourism Association, told Fresh News on September 19 that the inclusion of Koh Ker Temple in the World Heritage List will give Cambodia another level of prestige and an opportunity to showcase. Cambodia's cultural wealth to the world.
She added that the registration of the World Heritage Site will help promote tourism in Cambodia better and attract more foreign visitors, because through the recent registration will be widely disseminated while in Cambodia. There was a lot of congratulations from the top leaders to the people. At the same time, the private sector has also joined in the promotion, which has led to a growing popularity.
She said that in the past, because Koh Ker is far from Angkor, so there are not many tourists, but expect that after the World Heritage List and the publicity will be more tourists.
Khieu Thy, President of the Angkor Tourist Guides Association, also told Fresh News that it is a matter of pride for Cambodia that another ancient Cambodian temple, Koh Ker, has been inscribed on the UNESCO World Heritage List. Khmer and temples are becoming more and more known to the world, attracting international visitors to visit Cambodia.
He added that Cambodia has many temples compared to neighboring countries, therefore, the Royal Government must increase the attraction of tourists through the development of infrastructure, increase the maintenance of access to the temple regularly, promote environmental protection and It is possible to study the possibility of lowering visa fees to attract more visitors.
