Minister Heng Sour Discusses the Progress of Implementing the 6 Recommendations of Samdech Hun Sen
(Phnom Penh): On the occasion of His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, continued to meet with more than 180,000 workers in Bati District, Takeo Province on the morning of September 19, 2023, Mr. Heng Sour, Minister of Labor. And Vocational Training also highlighted the progress of the implementation of the six recommendations of the Prime Minister on August 29, 2023.
The Minister stated that the implementation of the six recommendations that the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training to implement in 2023 is as follows:
1. The minimum wage for 2024 is being mediated by the Ministry, and through the meeting held on September 18 yesterday, all parties agreed to set the last meeting on September 28, 2023 to produce good results. Provide workers before the Pchum Ben holiday. According to preliminary results, Cambodia is the only country exporting textile products that will raise the minimum wage for 2024.
2. Implementation of the social security system for voluntary contribution to health care for self-employed individuals and their dependents The Ministry is discussing with the General Secretariat of the National Council for Social Support to prepare an inter-ministerial prakas to be implemented before the end of 2023.
4. Promoting apprenticeship obligations The Ministry has been in discussions with stakeholders, especially employers, to revise the implementation mechanism and adjust apprenticeship training programs in line with the training package for skills development and reorganization programs, including internships. And internships as well.
6. Established a working group to develop an assessment mechanism and set the criteria "One enterprise is a safe community" in consultation and cooperation with social partners to lead the launch of the competition campaign from 2024.
