He also instructed the staff of health centers and hospitals in all provinces to pay attention to education, dissemination and treatment with care in accordance with their professional ethics. Ouch Borith: The "Pentagon Strategy" is an acceleration towards sustainable development (SDG)
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ouch Borith, Senior Minister in charge of Special Mission on behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, stated that the "Pentagon Strategy" is a policy to accelerate the momentum towards sustainable development (SDG).
Mr. Ouch Borith mentioned some points on what has been achieved in Cambodia which is committed to do more until after 2030, including:
* First, Cambodia attaches great importance to aligning national policy with the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) to accelerate national development progress. As with the Millennium Development Goals, the MGD SDGs are well integrated into national development plans and strategies.
* Third: Cambodia is also focusing on strengthening partnerships to achieve the SDGs. To achieve this, my government has been working to strengthen the process of policy consultation with and among stakeholders, both regionally and internationally. This not only ensures that policies are well integrated, but also strengthens cooperation and coordination in the implementation phase.
Mr. Ouch Borith said that the dialogue on strengthening the integration of public policy and institutions to achieve sustainable development (SDG) is relevant and timely, while all need to increase efforts and take action. Measures to change poverty and ensure that everyone enjoys prosperity and coexistence in harmony with one another and with nature.
He added that the SDGs are the interrelationships needed to approve optimal policy integration. Public institutions must be effective, competent and have good cooperation to make good decisions.
