Mr. Robin Nay: Cambodia Leads Among Regional Countries Establishing National Institution for Anti-Torture
(Stung Treng): Robin Nai, a member of the National Committee Against Torture, said in front of a representative of the Office of the United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights in Cambodia that Cambodia was a leading country in establishing a national body in charge of anti-torture. First among ASEAN member countries and countries in the region that are parties to the Convention against Torture and Other Protocols.
He said that the establishment of a national body called the National Committee Against Torture in 2017 reflected that the Royal Government of Cambodia has fully implemented its obligations as a State Party to the Convention against Torture and the Protocol. Of the United Nations.
He added that the Royal Government of Cambodia, the seventh mandate, under the wise leadership of Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia, remains highly committed to the promotion of human rights and the rule of law in accordance with the Universal Declaration on Human rights and international instruments that Cambodia has ratified.
Mr. Robin Nay said this on the occasion of announcing the opening of training and education on national and international standards and roles and responsibilities of the National Committee against Torture in Stung Treng this morning, September 19, 2023.
On that occasion, Mr. Robin Nay instructed all participants to take care of the knowledge from this outreach course and to share it with lower level officials to use it in their daily work for the Royal Government as well as the people. Citizens.
At the same time, he also commended the relevant authorities for their efforts to fulfill their duties well and responsibly in the past, which is a contribution to raising the profile of the Royal Government on the international stage in the field of rights. People.
It should be noted that on the morning of September 19, 2023, the National Committee Against Torture organized a training and dissemination course on national and international standards on anti-torture and the role and responsibilities of the National Committee against Torture in Stung Treng province under the chairmanship. By Mr. Nut Sa An, Chairman of the National Committee Against Torture.
The ceremony was also attended by representatives from the Office of the United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights in Cambodia, the Deputy Governor of the Provincial Board of Governors, the President of the Provincial Court, representatives of the Provincial Prosecutor's Office, the Provincial Police Commissioner, and the Military Police. Prisons and relevant authorities under the Stung Treng Provincial Administration, a total of more than 200 people.
Coal from Russia-occupied territory in Ukraine traded to Turkey
MOSCOW (Reuters) - $ 14.3 million worth of coal produced in Russia's occupied territories in Ukraine will be exported to NATO member Turkey in 2023, according to Russian customs data. Published by Reuters on Tuesday, September 19, 2023.
Between February and July 2023, about 160,400 tonnes of coal from eastern Ukraine, the Donetsk and Luhansk regions, reached Turkey, the data show. Three producers listed in customs data told Reuters that they shipped coal from the two regions to Turkey. However, the Turkish Ministry of Commerce and the General Department of Customs did not respond to a request for comment on exports.
Turkey is a major consumer and importer of coal, which is blocking the global downward trend by seeking to increase its share of coal for power generation. Unlike the United States and the European Union, Turkey has not restricted trade with Russia or with Russia-controlled areas of Ukraine.
Cambodia earns more than $ 800 million from selling more than 600,000 tons of raw cashews in 8 months, while the price rises to more than 7,000 riel per kilogram
Uon Siloth, president of the Cambodian Cashew Association, told Fresh News that the reason for the drop in cashew exports was due to climate change, which reduced cashew yields this year by more than 634,000 tonnes. . Second, farmers cut down some cashew trees and another factor, competition to buy from local enterprises for storage, processing for local supply and export.
He said that although the export volume of cashew nuts has decreased, but the price of cashew nuts in August and September is better than last year, which can be sold at between 7,000 riel to 7,500 riel per kilogram or about $ 1,900 per ton.
However, he mentioned that only a handful of farmers could benefit from the increase in cashew prices this year, as most farmers who could not afford to dry their stocks sold out at the beginning of the year during March and April. Only 5,000 to 6,000 riel per kilogram.
"Because most farmers do not have the cashew storage infrastructure such as porches and warehouses, most of them sold during March and April, when they sold more than 230,000 tonnes," he added. Few farmers have warehouses and porches and can sell until August and September. The Cambodian Cashew Association has been telling farmers since March 2023 that prices will rise in August and September, however, we have already sold most of them. ”
