Acting President of the Senate will chair a meeting of the Senate Standing Committee to decide on five agendas tomorrow morning.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kitti Nitikosal, Dr. Sim Ka, Acting President of the Senate of the Kingdom of Cambodia, on Wednesday morning, September 20, 2023, at 8:00 am, will chair a meeting of the Senate Standing Committee to review and decide on five agendas.
1. Examine and decide on the request of the Committee on Interior, National Defense, National Assembly-Senate Relations, Inspection and Public Function to include the draft law on the establishment of the Ministry of Inspection in the agenda of the 4th Extraordinary Session of the Senate.
2. Examine and decide on the request of the Committee on Interior, National Defense, National Assembly-Senate Relations, Inspection and Public Function to include the draft law on the establishment of the Secretariat of State for Border Affairs in the agenda of the fourth extraordinary Senate session.
3. Determine the agenda, date and composition of the Secretary of the Extraordinary Session of the Senate for the 4th Extraordinary Legislature.
4. Examine and decide on the report on the activities and work results of the Senate between the 10th and 11th sessions of the 4th legislature.
5. Set the agenda and date of the composition of the Secretary of the 11th session of the Senate of the 4th legislature.
