Hun Many Opens the First Cambodia 4.0 Forum Focusing on Youth Participation in Building a Digital Socio-Economy
(Phnom Penh): This morning, September 19, 2023, the Cambodian Center 4.0 in collaboration with the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia organized the first Cambodia 4.0 Forum on "Youth 4.0" under the chairmanship of Mr. HUN Many, Team Leader Board of Directors of the Center for Cambodia 4.0 and President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia. The forum was attended by representatives from relevant ministries, institutions, private educational institutions and a total of 270 youth.
Today's forum is a show of concern and participation in promoting and inspiring a broader understanding of the use of technology as a solution for positive social and economic benefits.
During his keynote address, Mr. HUN Many emphasized that the purpose of the forum was to bring together experts and stakeholders, including experts from the public, private and non-governmental sectors, to discuss, exchange views and share views on key topics. Related to building a digital social economy.
The topic of discussion at the first Cambodia 4.0 Forum focused on young people in the digital age, as young people are an important driving force for Cambodia in the future to promote the building of a digital economy and society as they A potentially active workforce and a group of people who are easy to adapt to new contexts and who are fond of using technology.
He assessed that the first Cambodia 4.0 Forum highlighted the role and importance of youth participation in the digital transformation process in Cambodia, as youth are a powerful driving force in promoting economic and social development. Digital.
Mr. Hun Many shared his views on the relationship between youth and the Industrial Revolution 4.0, the potential of youth and human capital development, the exploitation of the existence and potential of digital technology, the use of technology and mental health.
The first round of discussions was attended by representatives from the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and the Cambodian Science Fair, highlighting the role of education and training institutions in developing strategic plans and activities. Additional tips to strengthen digital education and digital skills development, as well as to motivate young people to embrace digital careers.
For the second part of the discussion, there were speakers from the Ministry of Health, Mengli J. Kouch Education and Smart Asiata, who discussed the use of technology and mental health of young people.
Discussions focused on the benefits of using technology as an aid in addressing mental health issues, as well as ways to balance the use of technology effectively, targeted and without compromising the mental health of consumers in particular. Youth.
In addition, the role of relevant institutions in highlighting public awareness of the benefits of using technology and preventing the risks of overuse and misuse of technology is also highlighted.
At the end of the forum, the presidium presented a letter of thanks to the distinguished speakers and facilitators who shared their views, experiences and best practices on the theme of the forum focused on youth in the digital age. Let the first Cambodia 4.0 Forum on "Youth 4.0" run successfully and fruitfully.
(Svay Rieng): Police in Bavet City arrested a Chinese man in a case of intentional violence after stabbing his Cambodian girlfriend with a bottle of gas because of jealousy.
This incident happened at midnight on September 18, 2023 at a restaurant in Bavet Kandal village, Bavet commune, Bavet city, Svay Rieng province.
According to Bavet police, the suspect was identified as Feng Gufa, 54, a Chinese national with an unspecified occupation, residing in Fujian Province, China. The victim was Chum Vathana, 43, a Cambodian national. Residence: Kampong Pil village, Wat Tamim commune, Sangke district, Battambang province.
Sources said that the Bavet Administrative Police received information from residents reported to the restaurant that at the restaurant in Bavet Kandal Village, Bavet Sangkat, Bavet City, there was a case of intentional violence. Immediately after receiving the information, the police arrived at the scene to investigate and brought a Chinese man to the Bavet Administrative Police Station for questioning.
In front of the police, the suspect confessed that he actually took a bottle of gasoline and poured it on the victim, who was his real girlfriend, due to jealousy and his girlfriend and others.
The victim is currently being treated at the Cambodia-China Friendship Polyclinic in Bavet Kandal Village, Bavet Sangkat, Bavet City, while the suspect is in charge of building a case for legal action. National Committee Against Torture Organizes Training on Dissemination of National and International Standards Concerning Respect for Human Rights and Duties and Responsibilities in Stung Treng Province
(Stung Treng): The National Committee Against Torture (NEC) on September 19, 2023 organized a training and education dissemination of national and international norms related to respect for human rights and the duties and responsibilities of the Committee. The National Committee Against Torture is chaired by Mr. Nut Sa An, Chairman of the National Committee Against Torture.
Mr. Robin Nay added that during the training and dissemination, there were also presentations of national and international standards related to respect for human rights and national and international norms related to the fight against torture, as well as the role and responsibilities of the National Committee against Torture. . In this outreach training, there were also some suggestions to (NEC) to establish a committee at the provincial level.
Mr. Nut Saan said that the purpose of this outreach will provide a better understanding of the rights of the National Committee against Torture and the UN Subcommittee on Torture Prevention.
He stressed that torture and ill-treatment were not necessary measures to be taken against those deprived of their liberty. On the contrary, such conduct is illegal and a serious violation of human rights. It is an injustice that can create endless resentment.
He added that the outreach will provide insight into national and international norms regarding the treatment of deprived persons, the Convention against Torture and the Protocol on the Roles, Duties and Rights of the National Anti-Torture Committee and its sub-committees. United Nations Committee on the Prevention of Torture.
Mr. Nuth Sa An also confirmed the expected results of all relevant authorities and officials to gain an understanding of the relevant national and international norms on those who have been deprived of their liberty to prevent and combat torture, as well as to understand the role and responsibilities of the committee. National Committee Against Torture (NEC). 757 Families in Sangkat Trapeang Krasaing, Khan Por Senchey Receive Real Estate Ownership Certificates (Hard copy)
