Director of Pailin Provincial Health Department calls on citizens and local authorities to join the movement to reduce and prevent mosquito breeding
(Pailin): Under the leadership of Mr. Chheang Ra, Minister of Health and under the guidance of Ms. Ban Srey Mom, Governor of Pailin Province, in recent days, the Provincial Health Department has educated people to understand how to prevent dengue fever and Sprayed mosquito repellent in communities to join the movement to reduce and prevent the growth of mosquitoes.
Mr. Sleth You, Director of the Provincial Health Department, said that the team of the department sprayed mosquito repellent in the community and disseminated to ensure the safety of people without dengue fever and encourage the health center of the Provincial Referral Hospital to continue spraying. Mosquito repellent and albatross eradicate tiger mosquito breeding grounds in the community to help prevent the spread of dengue fever on a regular basis.
The director of the Department of Health confirmed that the campaign will continue throughout the province to promote people to better understand how to protect themselves from dengue fever. In addition, the campaign also includes the application of albatross to people's homes and the spraying of tiger mosquito repellent in public places to help prevent the disease from recurring.
"Tiger mosquitoes are a fast-transmitting agent of dengue fever through the water as a tiger mosquito shelter (water in car tires, motorcycle tires, cans, bottles, rainwater as a tiger mosquito shelter), so do not leave Put car and motorcycle tires in the rain in the community because it creates a tiger mosquito shelter after the rain.
At the same time, the Ministry of Health announced that from January to September 12, 2023, there was a significant increase in dengue cases. Experience, research and disease monitoring of the National Dengue Fever Program in the past shows that the dengue condition always has an abnormally high cycle of disease every 5 to 6 years.
It should be noted that dengue fever can occur in people of all ages, both young and old, caused by the dengue virus through the bite of mosquitoes, which like to lay eggs as water worms in watery places. Clear, odorless, such as: jars, basins, water containers, flower pots, bowls, table legs, cupboards, special cups, tires, motorcycles, cans, bowls, glass bowls, etc., which are stored or disposed of in open fields, forming a source of water and mosquito nets. .
Therefore, the Ministry of Health also reminded all people to continue to be vigilant and responsible in protecting their personal and family health, to prevent the spread of dengue fever, and to participate in preventing the spread of dengue fever. Grow in the community to be more effective. Chinese Foreign Minister hails strategic cooperation in meeting with Russian counterpart
MOSCOW (Reuters) - Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi met with his Russian counterpart Sergey Lavrov in Moscow to strengthen closer ties in the face of strained relations with the West over the Ukraine war and escalation. Military presence in the Pacific. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Tuesday, September 19, 2023.
At the beginning of the talks, Wang praised the strategic cooperation between the two countries and highlighted the joint commitment to a more polar and orderly world. "China and Russia, as the world's leading powers and permanent members of the United Nations Security Council, have a special responsibility to maintain strategic and strategic stability," Wang said. "Global development."
Lavrov stressed that "the importance of Russia-China cooperation is to ensure justice in world affairs, to balance the interests in the development process of different directions." Mr Lavrov added that Russia and China would coordinate their efforts during this week's UN General Assembly, as well as other international forums.
The Chinese diplomat, who remains in Russia until Thursday this week, also plans to hold strategic security consultations with Russian officials. The visit comes after Wang met with National Security Adviser Jack Sullivan in Malta to try to defuse tensions between the United States and China.
