(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Tuesday, September 19, 2023, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, continued to meet with 18,104 workers. Others from factories in Bati district, Takeo province.
Dr. Heng Sour, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, said that the workers who participated in the event came from 18 factories. These 18 factories have 13 garment factories, 2 travel products and bags, 2 shoe factories and 1 laundry factory.
According to Dr. Heng Sour, among the workers who participated in the ceremony, there were 694 pregnant workers.
The minister, a former scholarship student from Japan, said that Takeo currently has 233 factories and employs a total of 68,000 workers, earning a total of 209 million US dollars a year. Of these, 66 garment factories employ a total of 58,000 workers, earning more than $ 182 million a year.
According to Heng Sour, Takeo province ranks fourth as the province with the most industrial development after Phnom Penh, Kampong Speu and Kandal provinces.
The policy of creating jobs for the people is one of the priority policies of the Royal Government led by the Cambodian People's Party in both the old and new mandates. Immediately after the formation of the new Royal Government, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet arrested workers in the textile, garment, footwear and travel products and bags industry for the first public meeting.
Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet has already met with workers three times. The first time was held on August 29 in Prey Speu area, Phnom Penh, with 18,013 workers participating, the second time was held on September 1, 2023 in Takhmao city, Kandal province, with 18 workers participating. 289 people and the third time was held on September 9, 2023 in Samrong Tong district, Kampong Speu province, with 18,265 workers participating.
In the last three meetings, His Excellency Hun Manet presented the policy of the Royal Government in the new legislature, especially the Pentagon strategy - the first phase, which is a strategy to focus on job growth and improve people's lives. Citizens for the better.
