To prevent the disease, he said, the campaign will be conducted throughout the capital to spread awareness about how to prevent dengue fever. In addition, the campaign also includes the application of albatross to people's homes and the spraying of tiger mosquito repellent in public places to prevent the disease from recurring.
At the same time, the Ministry of Health would like to inform the public that from January to September 12, 2023, there has been a significant increase in dengue cases. Experience, research and disease monitoring of the National Dengue Fever Program in the past shows that the dengue condition always has an abnormally high cycle of disease every 5 to 6 years.
