(Phnom Penh): The French Government, through its Embassy in Cambodia and the French Agency for Development (AFD), continues to support Cambodia's rural development sector at the request of the Ministry of Rural Development to accelerate development towards the Cambodian vision. High middle income country by 2030 and high income country by 2050.
On that occasion, Mr. Chhay Rithy Sen thanked the French Government through the French Agency for Development (AFD), which has always cooperated and provided assistance to Cambodia since the Royal Government of Cambodia, the sixth mandate under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen. Former Prime Minister.
In order to be in line with the first phase of the Pentagon strategy of the new government, the Ministry has prepared four priority programs, including:
1. Develop physical and transport infrastructure to expand the scope of rural road systems to promote economic growth to rural areas.
2. Improve the living conditions of rural communities by providing adequate access to clean water, maintaining adequate sanitation, and educating people to change their attitudes toward ending open defecation (ODF).
3. Diversify rural economic activities, continue to promote the rural economy by training people in basic skills to create businesses other than agriculture.
4. Strengthen administrative and general affairs support services to strengthen institutions at both the national and sub-national levels to increase efficiency, integrity and accountability to serve the people better and faster.
In response, the ambassador and the director confirmed that "the French government will support more rural development at the request of the ministry."
The French Ambassador highlighted the good cooperation between the French Government and the Royal Government of Cambodia in the past, helping to build physical infrastructure as well as help in the field of education by providing scholarships to many Cambodian students. .
