The National Bank of Cambodia, the Saxon Center and the Bank for International Settlements hold a seminar on "Monetary Policy Restrictions and the Impact on Financial Stability in Asia"
This high-level workshop was organized by Dr. Chea Serey, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia as the Chairman of the Board of Governors of the Central Bank for Research and Training Center of the Central Bank of Southeast Asia (SASIN) for 2023, held on 18 September. 2023 in Siem Reap province.
The high-level workshop aims to provide a forum for senior policymakers to discuss key regional issues. For 2023, the workshop selected topics on "Monetary policy constraints and their impact on financial stability in Asia" with the participation of 19 ASEAN members and representatives from international financial institutions. .
Also present were Dr. Bo Li, Vice President of the International Monetary Fund, Dr. Tao Zhang, Country Representative for the Asia-Pacific Bank of the International Settlement Bank, and guest speakers from major universities.
In particular, the raising of interest rates by the central banks of major countries to combat inflation has caused emerging and developing countries to face many problems, such as declining capital flows, depreciating currencies and pushing both countries. This raises its benchmark interest rate.
In this situation, emerging and developing countries must not only control inflationary pressures and exchange rates, but also pay more attention to maintaining financial stability risks.
Regional and global cooperation will reduce the risk of widening the development gap, also dividing the global economy, which will support the growth of international trade and investment.
Ms. Chea Serey briefed the meeting on the economic growth situation in Cambodia after the Kovid-19 crisis and the launch of policies of the Royal Government and the National Bank of Cambodia to promote economic recovery and address challenges. . National Assembly Celebrates Historical Day for Registration of "Koh Ker Temple Resort" as a World Heritage Site
