The price of frog meat and baby frogs has risen. A frog farm in Svay Antor district can sell between 1 and 2 tons of frog meat and more than 10,000 offspring per month
(Prey Veng): Farmers who used to raise frogs in Prey Veng province are happy that frog meat is more expensive compared to the cost of frog feed, which is a decent profit, which makes a farm in Svay Antor district Can sell frog meat from 1 to 2 tons per month to the market in Phnom Penh and sell from 10,000 to 20,000 frogs.
Mr. Ry Vuthy, a farmer living in Dom village, Pean Rong commune, Svay Antor district, Prey Veng province, and the owner of Meach Chulsa farm, who is currently engaged in the business of raising frogs and raising fish, has been earning a decent monthly income from Raising frogs and selling at the mother breeds frogs, meat and baby frogs to other farmers who wish to raise frogs at home as well.
Mr. Ry Vuthy said on September 18, 2023 that today he has been supplying meat frogs to the market in the province and especially to Phnom Penh, with a supply of 1 to 2 tons of meat frogs per month. Selling per kilogram at about 7,500 riel, compared to the previous price of only 4,500 riel, so can sell more profit between 1,500 to 2,000 riel.
He said that the reason for the increase in the price of frogs is due to the demand in the market more than before, and the neighboring countries in this rainy season is not rich in meat frogs sold in the market, so it is an opportunity for farmers. Local meat frogs can make a profit.
At the same time, he also said that today, his frog farm has more demand for frogs than frog meat, and also a reasonable price, a frog costs from 250 to 500 riels, which also has local people. Like in other districts, they buy frogs to take home.
He said that in terms of techniques for raising frogs today, he has collaborated with EU partner projects to train farmers in fish farming, so he has many opportunities to gain new knowledge, which is organized by the Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Development. Fisheries Administration as well.
Mr. Ry Vuthy stated that the area where he planned to raise frogs is more than 3 hectares and his frog farming has been used for 8 years, he started raising in 2016.
