Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun Instructs Border Authorities to Facilitate Workers' Travel and Solve Any Challenges (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): On the morning of September 18, 2023, Cambodia instructed all border authorities to eliminate any inactivity that causes difficulties for Cambodian workers when traveling in and out.
In the first meeting of the Commission after the establishment of the Royal Government, Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun emphasized to the leaders of the various units in the Commission for this task, especially the border authorities must change their attitude. Work to make sure that migrant workers are comfortable receiving services.
At the same time, Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun also urged relevant institutions, including the General Department of Immigration and the governors of border provinces to meet with the Thai side to facilitate the travel of migrant workers. He added that the place has been criticized as an individual involved in receiving informal compensation from workers, so this point must be eliminated.
In order to be a mechanism to facilitate migrant workers, the Deputy Prime Minister and Chairman of the Commission on the plan to establish a mechanism for inspection from the national level to inspect through the gate to accept the concerns and put measures to solve the workers. In addition, he recommended the establishment of a hotline and social media so that all workers can have a way to report to the national level to prevent any phenomenon.
