Ministry of Labor: The inclusion of Koh Ker Khmer temple as a World Heritage Site is another great national pride of another nation
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training on September 17 issued a statement to congratulate the decision to register Cambodia's Koh Ker temple as a World Heritage Site at the 45th meeting in Saudi Arabia. .
The Ministry of Labor stated that the success of this registration is another great national pride after the Angkor, Preah Vihear and Sambor Prei Kuk sites were inscribed on the World Heritage List in 1992, 2008 and 2017. Meanwhile, the Ministry also highlighted the gratitude to the King and Queen who have worked hard to prepare the registration documents from 2018 until the final result for the motherland.
For the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, the construction of Koh Ker temples by kings and Khmer ancestors of all generations has left behind a unique cultural heritage and an ancient civilization, a proud national identity for all generations of Cambodians.
It should be noted that the UNESCO World Heritage Committee decided to include the Koh Ker temple resort of Cambodia as a World Heritage Site in the 45th session in Riyadh, Saudi Arabia at 12:18 in Riyadh at 1:28 p.m. In Phnom Penh on September 17, 2023.
