General Vong Pisen: The word "peace" has become popular all over the world
(Phnom Penh): General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, said that the word "peace" has become popular all over the world, because without peace, do not talk about the development of democracy and human rights. Currently, some countries are still at war and many effects have arisen from this war.
This statement was made by General Vong Pisen during the appointment ceremony of Lt. Gen. Huot Chheang as Deputy Commander and Chief of Staff of the Army on the morning of September 18, 2023 at the Army Command.
The General continued that for Cambodia, which has suffered from decades of war, ended the war and developed the country from scratch under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who took life as capital and set out a win-win policy. Winning gives Cambodia complete peace throughout the country.
Because peace comes with difficulties, Samdech Techo Hun Sen uttered the words "Thank you for the peace" to highlight the importance for all humanity. In this sense, the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces is committed to safeguarding peace, defending the achievements, which are the greatest achievements in history left by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Guide to Peace.
At the same time, the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) is determined to protect the legitimate Royal Government that emerged from the election led by His Majesty the King Hun Manet and to destroy all acts of treason, extremist ideology that seeks to overthrow the Royal Government by inciting unrest in Society.
The Commander-in-Chief also instructed all levels of commanders and troops to pay close attention to the management and use of explosive weapons to ensure national security. With this, we must cooperate with the authorities to prevent the trafficking of all kinds of drugs that are in the country. Phnom Penh Police Commissioner Receives Thai Embassy Deputy Chief of Police
(Phnom Penh): With the permission of General Sar Thet, National Police Commissioner at the Phnom Penh Municipal Police this morning, September 18, 2023, Major General Chuon Narin, Deputy National Police Commissioner and Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner Let Colonel Biyavath Kietkang pay a courtesy call on the Thai Embassy in Cambodia and the Phnom Penh Municipal Police.
Lt. Gen. Chuon Narin welcomed Lt. Col. Biyavath Kietkang and his delegation to pay a courtesy call and discuss the cooperation between the Thai Embassy and the Phnom Penh Municipal Police as good neighbors. In particular, strengthen cooperation on security, order, security and stability between the two countries.
Lt. Col. Biyavath Kietkang also mentioned that under the guidance of the Deputy Chief of Police of the Old Thai Embassy, he appreciated and praised Major General Chuon Narin during his tenure as the Sihanoukville Provincial Police Commissioner for his good cooperation with the Thai Embassy. Especially on security and safety for Thai people who come to work and travel in Sihanoukville.
This cooperation work continues to be stronger in the name of Major General Chuon Narin, who has recently been appointed Deputy General Commissioner of the National Police and Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner. He also requested the Commissioner to continue to help provide security for Thais in Cambodia, especially in Phnom Penh.
