(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chea Somethy, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, on September 18, 2023, led dignitaries and professional officers under the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation to visit the National Institute of Social Affairs, Exit World Wide and the National Center for Infants and Children. Located in Damnak Thom Village, Sangkat Steung Meanchey, Khan Meanchey, Phnom Penh.
The Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, Mr. Chea Somethy, met with the students in each classroom where the students are studying and commended the institute management for their hard work in training the students there, including Cambodian students and students. Foreign.
In a meeting with professors and students at the National Institute of Social Affairs, Exit World Wide and the National Center for Infants and Children, Chea Somethy said that disability was an important issue that needed to be addressed, including the rehabilitation of the disabled. Fitness.
