The Minister of Social Affairs also thanked Ex-Worldwide for its assistance and cooperation with the National Institute of Social Affairs and thanked the teachers, caregivers of infants and children, especially children with severe disabilities.
It should be noted that the National Institute of Social Affairs was established in 2011 for the purpose of educating, training and researching civil servants of the Ministry and relevant officials to carry out social work, study and research in the field of social work to meet the requests and practical needs for the benefit of the people. Vulnerable and vulnerable from birth to death. "According to Mr. Vong Phea, Deputy Director of the National Institute of Social Affairs."
The institute has two main missions: training and research in the field of social affairs. At present, the institute has a total of 78 officers, 38 teachers, 4 contract officers.
The institute has already trained seven generations of students, equivalent to a total of 457 students, including 128 social studies students and 18 foreign students. Of the 128 social studies students, only about 15-20 percent have joined the civil service, a small number compared to the actual social needs.
