(Phnom Penh): Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, Acting Head of State of Cambodia, on September 18, 2023, expressed his deepest congratulations on the occasion of UNESCO's inclusion of "Koh Ker Temple Resort" as a World Heritage Site. .
In a letter from Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, he stated: "I would like to express my deepest national pride on the occasion of the 45th session of the UNESCO World Heritage Committee at Rhea, Saudi Arabia, decided to include the Khmer island of Koh Ker as a World Heritage Site on September 17, 2023.
