(Kampong Speu): General Sem Sovanny, First Vice-Chairman of the National Committee and Director-General of the National Peacekeeping Center, on the morning of September 18, 2023, visited a multinational operation training course at the Humanitarian Mine Action Field within the framework of the Ministerial Meeting. ASEAN Defense - Plus under the theme "Precious Homeland - 2023" at the Multinational Peacekeeping Force Training School, Kampong Speu Province.
This exercise will be an important contribution to the journey towards a landmine-free Cambodia in 2025, especially in support of Samdech Techo's initiative to "provide safe land, create a smile".
During the 10 days of the training, participants will have study tours to potential tourist sites in Cambodia, as well as humanitarian work in addition to on-site training. At the same time, there are also art performances between Cambodia and China to show the traditions and customs.
The training course under the theme "Beloved Homeland - 2023" hosted by Cambodia and co-chaired by a Chinese friend was conducted effectively and technically. However, all participants always strive to train.
In particular, all multinational forces, including the three great powers such as China, the United States and Russia, have jointly learned, exchanged experiences, and strengthened the bonds of solidarity and friendship between ASEAN countries and the region.
At the same time, General Sem Sovanny also visited to clear mines and unexploded ordnance on the actual field.
General Sem Sovanny observed that the operation went well in all aspects in terms of technical specifications. For the accommodation of all participants is to live comfortably, harmoniously, hygienic, good atmosphere under the shade of peace.
General Sem Sovanny emphasized that the experiences of the trainees of each country shared with each other are also elements for humanitarian demining.
In addition, General Sem Sovanny said, "Although the colors are different, but for the same purpose is to clear humanitarian mines for peace."
General Sem Sovanny also conveyed the cordial greetings of Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet, Deputy Prime Minister of Cambodia and Deputy Prime Minister Tea Seiha, Minister of National Defense to Cambodian military trainees and friendly countries who are attending multinational operational training courses on the field. Humanitarian mines in the framework of the ASEAN-Plus Defense Ministers' Meeting, which is also hosted by Cambodia.
