(Kratie): Kratie Provincial Disaster Management Committee has informed people living along the Mekong River, Dang Prek to be very careful about the flood due to the water level in Kratie province has risen to 19. 95 meters as of September 17, 2023.
According to the forecast, the water level of the Mekong River in Kratie province will continue to rise tomorrow and the water level in Kratie province will be 22 meters high.
In order to avoid any possible accidents, the Provincial Disaster Management Committee would like to advise the people living in Kratie province, especially the families living along the Mekong River, Prek Metta, to be very careful as follows:
1. Pack important materials in advance, such as ID card, birth certificate, budget and other documents.
2. Prepare essentials such as food, water, first aid kit, soap, blankets, raincoat, mobile phone 1294 and other items.
4. Collect and store flood-prone agricultural products to avoid serious damage or loss.
6. Pay attention to the telephone system 1294 of the Kratie Provincial Disaster Committee.
Please note that the water also flooded some communes in Chit Borei, Chhlong, Sambo and Prek Prosop districts.
