This was stated by Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Minister of Information on the occasion of presiding over the closing ceremony of the training course on management skills and leadership of 381 media units organized by the Professional Development Association: Journalists of Cambodia (CJDS) this afternoon. September 17, 2023 at the Royal Academy of Cambodia.
The Ministry of Information's Code of Conduct for Journalists must be supported by journalists to improve the quality of journalism in Cambodia. Minister Neth Pheaktra emphasized the important role of journalists in society, helping society to participate in the development of the national economy by disseminating accurate, accurate and fast information to the people.
Dr. Hor Kunthea, President of the Association of Professional Development of Journalists of Cambodia, confirmed that the training was organized to strengthen and enhance the capacity of journalists to be stronger and more efficient, ethical and professional journalism.
Closing the training, Mr. Neth Pheaktra confirmed that the Ministry of Information will prepare a professional code of ethics for the press association to have a common standard throughout the country, because in the past there were many associations and there are different ethics in the future. Will be prepared because ethics is the armor for the right professional journalists.
The Ministry of Information plans to launch a professional training institute for journalists and public relations to promote the development of human resources in the field of information to provide journalists with more capacity, knowledge, quality and diversity to meet the needs of the labor market in the context of society. Digital.
