The first and historic official visit of Samdech Hun Manet as the leader of Cambodia has yielded high results, especially the continued strengthening of political, economic and social relations and cooperation with China, a great power. The second largest economy in the world and the largest in Asia.
Please be reminded that at the invitation of Mr. Li Chheang, Prime Minister of the People's Republic of China, His Majesty the King Hun Manet and Lok Chumteav Pech Chanmony Hun Manet led a high-level delegation of the Royal Government of Cambodia to pay an official visit to China on the 14th. September 2023.
After a five-hour flight, President Hun Manet and his wife and delegation arrived in Beijing on the afternoon of September 14. Arriving at Beijing Capital International Airport, the Prime Minister and Lok Chumteav were welcomed by senior Chinese officials and the Cambodian Ambassador to China, as well as other embassy officials.
Upon arrival in China, the President laid a wreath and paid tribute to the Chinese hero. Then pay homage to the King and Queen who are sitting in Beijing for medical check-ups.
Fundraising is a priority of the Royal Government to boost the national economy and create jobs for the people. Therefore, this first official visit to China, attracting investment is also a necessary agenda for President Hun Manet.
On September 15, His Excellency Hun Manet began with China's top leaders on the agenda of the visit as planned. The President paid a courtesy call on Chinese President Xi Jinping.
In particular, the Chinese President also expressed a strong position to continue to respect all internal affairs of Cambodia. The President also pledged to join Cambodia in defending any attempt to interfere in Cambodia's internal affairs. In particular, will strive to protect the relations and cooperation between Cambodia and China without any power to separate to ensure the interests between the country and the people of Cambodia and China.
On regional and global issues, Cambodian and Chinese leaders are committed to continuing to respect and abide by international law. In particular, will strive to resolve issues to maintain peace and stability in the world, which is a necessary desire of mankind.
After meeting with President Xi Jinping, His Excellency Hun Manet also met with Chinese National People's Congress Chairman Zhao Leji. During the meeting, Mr. Zhao Leji also warmly welcomed Mr. Hun Manet to pay an official visit to China.
In this meeting, Samdech Hun Sen and Mr. Chao Le Chi also discussed the relationship and cooperation between Cambodia and China for the past 65 years and have the same position to continue to cultivate and promote relations and cooperation. Better operation.
In addition, His Excellency Hun Manet also suggested the exchange of visits between parliamentary leaders between the two countries, especially young MPs, to strengthen relations and cooperation between the two countries' parliaments and parliaments.
After the bilateral talks, His Excellency Hun Manet and Mr. Ly Chheang co-chaired the signing ceremony of up to 15 important documents. These documents were signed by senior officials of both countries.
The 15 documents include an action plan for building a new Cambodian-Chinese common destiny community in the new era between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Chinese government (2024-2028) and cooperation on "Industrial and Technology Corridor", "Fish Corridor and Rice ”, infrastructure, digital economy, green development, control and forestry and wildlife development cooperation.
During his visit to Beijing, His Excellency Hun Manet also attended a solidarity dinner and dinner organized by Chinese and Cambodian investors and businessmen. During the forum, Samdech Hun Manet outlined some of the policies of the Royal Government of Cambodia regarding investment, especially the Royal Government provides high protection to the private sector, which the Royal Government considers a necessary partner for national development.
In this regard, Samdech Hun Sen called on Chinese investors and businessmen to come to Cambodia to seize investment opportunities in Cambodia. He assured that investment in Cambodia will be fruitful and prosperous.
The official visit of His Excellency Hun Manet to the Chinese capital, Beijing, ended on the evening of September 15. On the morning of September 16, Samdech Hun Manet and Lok Chumteav Pech Chanmony Hun Manet led a delegation of Cambodia Special Flight 001 to Nanning, Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region, China to attend the 20th China-ASEAN Expo. .
Samdech Hun Sen expressed his gratitude for all the information related to the cooperation that the Autonomous Region has done with Cambodia. He also praised the economic growth and development of the autonomous region, which is one of China's major economic drivers.
On that occasion, the Prime Minister requested the Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region to further strengthen and expand cooperation, especially to strengthen trade and investment, support for Cambodian agricultural products, provide public health care services and promote development. Tourism expands vocational training, education and sports, as well as increasing direct flights between Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region and Cambodia.
In response, he said he would look into the possibility of increasing direct flights from the Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region to Cambodia, and would begin discussions with stakeholders in both China and Cambodia. .
On the morning of September 17, His Excellency Hun Manet attended the opening ceremony of the 20th China-ASEAN Expo with Chinese Prime Minister Li Chiang and leaders of other ASEAN member countries. At the opening ceremony of the 20th China-ASEAN Expo, held under the theme "Building a Harmonious Community and One Destiny", the Prime Minister of Cambodia also delivered a keynote speech.
In his keynote speech, Samdech Manet highlighted some of the problems that cause Kovid-19 disease. For Kovid-'s 19's illness, the world was in turmoil. In addition, in 2021 and 2022, trade in goods will exceed the previous level of Kovid-19 outbreak, which emphasizes the important role of trade in ensuring the socio-economic security of the world's people. .
President Hun Manet also mentioned that the world is currently facing other challenges such as rising commodity prices, strategic food security and the impact of climate change. In response to these issues, the Prime Minister of Cambodia highlighted that trade plays an important role in addressing these global challenges to ensure that interdependence and globalization are mutually beneficial. .
He said trade should not be used as a weapon to undermine global economic security. In this sense, ASEAN and China are key players in exemplifying the benefits of strengthening multilateral cooperation without leaning towards protectionism, unilateralism or economic nationalism. That no.
After opening the 20th China-ASEAN Expo, on the morning of Sunday, September 17, 2023, His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Lok Chumteav Pech Chanmony Hun Manet cut the ribbon to inaugurate the Cambodian National Pavilion. Visit the exhibition of Cambodian products on display at the Nanning International Convention and Exhibition Center.
At the 20th China-ASEAN Expo, which officially opened on the morning of September 17, many Cambodian products were on display, including rice, pepper, cashew nuts, wine, fruit, palm sugar, natural coffee, Cambodian ingredients. Handmade carvings, jewelry, fabrics and Khmer clothes and many other agricultural products.
The China-ASEAN Expo is an opportunity to promote Cambodian products and to find Chinese partners to distribute in the Chinese market. Samdech Hun Sen is excited and encourages businessmen and investors to promote the export of more Cambodian agricultural products to help farmers have a better life.
Samdech Hun Sen also praised and appreciated the working group of all relevant ministries and institutions and traders who worked hard to organize and bring Cambodian products to the public in the "20th China-ASEAN Expo".
The Prime Minister also thanked the leadership of the Guangxi Provincial Administration of the Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region for providing a warm and hospitable hospitality to the Cambodian delegation, as well as for cooperation and coordination for all relevant working groups. Arrange to bring Cambodian products to be displayed at the 20th ASEAN-China Expo with attractive and good results.
He said that this work is to contribute to the promotion of national prestige and culture on the international stage by showcasing foreign products to Cambodian people, as well as to promote investment potential for Cambodia. In addition, the event has really played an important role in boosting China-ASEAN trade volume, especially in the context of the recovery from the Kovid-19 crisis.
Before leading the repatriated delegation, Hun Manet also attended the 3rd Summit on Business, Economic Cooperation and Trade in the framework of the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement, which was held in Nanning, Guangxi Province.
The meeting was held under the theme "Integration in the Open Market of the ASEAN Agreement and Promoting Win-Win Cooperation in the Asia-Pacific Region."
He also said that with the current global uncertainty, Assad's role is increasingly important in strengthening confidence in the multilateral trading system, post-crisis economic recovery and promoting regional and global economic integration. Based on win-win principles and mutual benefits.
To further strengthen the role of the Prime Minister, the Prime Minister shared the following views:
First, I believe that all member states share the common view that China's economy is important in leading the Asia-Pacific economic growth. Therefore, ASEAN and China need to further strengthen the resilience of economic cooperation and interaction to show the world that promoting free, open, environmental and rule-based multilateral trade remains the most appropriate common solution for us. All together.
Third, we must recognize that the private sector is a key player in the implementation of this agreement and helps to distribute economic benefits widely to the people. Therefore, we need to continue to highlight the importance of ASP to the private sector as well as encourage and support their ability to participate in ASEAN, especially small and medium enterprises.
Fourth, we should begin to expedite the completion of the procedure for applying for new membership, and consider expanding the membership. This is ASEAN's common policy to promote integration into the global economy as well as strengthen cooperation with potential external partners.
Fifth, ensuring the environment of the ASEAN Agreement is important in creating attractiveness and demonstrating the benefits of multilateral trade participation. In this regard, I encourage the effective implementation of chapters on economic and technical cooperation that will enable members of least developed countries to be able to participate in the performance of their obligations.
