1,000 Poor Students in Ou Raing Ov District, Tbong Khmum Province Receive $ 45,000 Donation from Korean People
(Tbong Khmum): South Korean people donated 2,000 sets of clothes and materials totaling $ 45,000 to about 1,000 students and poor people in Chak commune, Ou Raing Ov district, Tbong Khmum province. Jin Hee and a group of volunteers for a smile on September 17, 2023.
The distribution of the charitable donations was led by Mr. Kim Jin-wook, the leader of the Smile Volunteer Team, who was very happy to meet with the students and people in Ou Raing Ov district who are suffering in their daily lives. He will continue this charitable activity in other provinces.
Mr. Kim Jin-wook also urged all people, especially grandparents, in situations where the weather is changing, to pay attention to health care, personal safety, to adhere to hygiene, eat clean, drink clean and live clean.
For the distribution, 100 poor families, each family received 20 kg of rice, 1 stick of fish sauce, 1 stick of soy sauce, 1 stick of fish, 1 stick of noodles, 2 sets of shirts, bread and milk. Each of the 400 students received a book, a pen, a pencil, an eraser, a drill, a set of clothes, a set of milk and bread, and about 400 people who participated in the program each received two sets of clothes, bread and milk. .
Please be informed that this is the second time that Jinhei Technical Training Center and Volunteers for Smiles have distributed charitable gifts, the first time was in 2018.
The Jinhei Training Center is also the legal center for sending thousands of Cambodian workers to work in the Republic of Korea for the E7 visa type in the field of welding (ships).
