This is something that business owners need to find out to avoid some corrupt officials threatening to extort money that could affect their day-to-day business.
According to Kong Vibol, Deputy Prime Minister and Director General of the General Department of Taxation, businesses with a gross annual turnover of less than 250 million riels or $ 60,000 will not be required to register for tax at The General Department of Taxation, while small businesses are also not required to apply for administrative services in the districts so as not to affect small businesses.
He said that for businesses that earn more than 250 million riel to 750 million riel, or about 180,000 dollars, a small tax is required, which is a type of business to record a simple list, recording only income and expenses. Businesses that earn more than 750 million to 40 billion riels, or about $ 1 million, are subject to the average tax, which requires business owners to register clearly and accurately.
In a live broadcast on "Tax Awareness" on September 15, 2023, Mr. Kong Vibol encourages all business owners with legal income to register for tax transparency and avoidance. Fines or any action that leads to harm to the business.
At the same time, the issuance of business licenses for commercial services and licenses for the wholesale and retail trade of agricultural equipment does not require administrative services.
