Lightning strike kills couple, kills emergency couple
(Svay Rieng): Two couples were cutting grass when their wife was struck by lightning and their husband was seriously injured at 12 o'clock on September 17, 2023 in Tuol Sala village, Chrung Popel commune, Romduol district, Svay Rieng province.
Romduol district police said that before the incident, a couple was cutting grass in the field, suddenly rain, lightning, lightning, shot and killed two couples, while the wife died while being taken to the hospital. Also seriously injured.
According to the police, the victim, Peam Ra, 32, of Tuol Sala village, Chrung Popel commune, Romduol district, Svay Rieng province, and his wife, Chou Sovanndara, 35, of the same commune, died at the hospital. .
Currently, the victim was sent to Svay Rieng Provincial Referral Hospital for treatment, while the deceased was taken by his family for a traditional ceremony.
In connection with this natural disaster, Rumduol district authorities call on all residents to be very careful when it rains, wind, thunder, lightning to go to a safe place to prevent possible accidents. Khmer Civilization: Khmer Nation Celebrates Koh Ker Temple as a World Heritage Site of Mankind
Along with this happy celebration, there is also the question of what are the islands of Koh Ker as a World Heritage Site based on the outstanding universal values?
The Koh Ker temple, built during the reign of Jayavarman IV in the 10th century CE, is dedicated to the seven-story pyramid and is 35 meters high. The capital has no walls, is an open city of art, religion, politics, administration, as well as the construction of many dams to prevent the flooding of the capital in a messy and unique work of the Khmer ancestors.
Therefore, the Koh Ker temple site, which has been inscribed on the World Heritage List today, is invaluable, representing the national identity, the soul of the Khmer nation, invaluable because it is a work and a legacy. Of the previous generation of Khmer ancestors who built it for a long time.
