Preah Vihear Provincial Governor Confirms No Clearing of Seedlings in Rovieng District, Posted by Military Officials
(Preah Vihear): Mr. Kim Rithy, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, confirmed that there was no clearing and deforestation on the forest land in Phnom Dek village, Romney commune, Rovieng district, Preah Vihear province, as some media advertised. The provincial governor confirmed that the road was built by an iron ore mining company to study iron ore and facilitate people's travel.
The governor of Preah Vihear province confirmed this after the news that Global Green Company destroyed seedlings in the forest area in Phnom Dek village, Romney commune, Rovieng district.
In response to this announcement, Mr. Kim Rithy stated, "I would like to emphasize that Global Green is not encroaching on land, it is building roads. "This road is going to iron ore, which they have a valid license."
In response to this announcement, Mr. Hor Bun Hour, Governor of Rovieng District, also confirmed that the clearing to widen the old road, but did not affect the community forest. The district governor continued that the construction of this road is to serve the benefit of the people as well.
The district governor confirmed that "the expansion of this road does not affect the community forest land. That road has an old plan. "This road is also to make it easier for people to transport non-timber agricultural products."
According to the district governor, the construction of this road is also a request from the authorities and the community.
According to sources from Preah Vihear provincial officials, the promotion was carried out by a military official who seized state land in the area. According to a senior official in Preah Vihear province, the military officer took the name of a senior official of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) to the site and accused the company of mining iron ore into its land.
