The study tour is based on the successful experience of the CAPFish Small and Medium Fisheries Support Program (VCIS), which has supported 28 fisheries enterprises in modernizing business operations, creating positive impact through job creation. Effective use of resources and increased profits.
Study tours organized especially for journalists of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and other institutions for the following specific purposes:
First, provide some educational messages to the media on business development, concepts and practices, food safety and private sector development. Second: Disseminate the successful implementation of projects of the Fisheries Administration and UNIDO. Third, demonstrate compliance with food safety requirements and certification processes. Fourth, disseminate to the public the important message and benefits of food safety.
The study tour was led and coordinated by Ms. Im Rachana, Undersecretary of State and spokesperson for the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries (MAFF), and the Fisheries Administration (FiA).
The visit will include a variety of activities, including: food safety training, press conferences, visits to fisheries enterprises supported by the project, interviews with experts, business owners and consumers.
The visit demonstrates the commitment of stakeholders, including government, the private sector, the media, development partners, to improve business operations, increase competitiveness, new investment opportunities, increase food safety awareness, and strengthen the value chain. Fisheries and public health promotion.
