(Phnom Penh): During the global crisis, all sectors, especially the real estate sector, are affected. However, Oknha Dr. Kim Heang, Founder of KW Cambodia, said that these issues should not be a burden to society, instead to spread a lot of positive information to overcome all those problems and contribute to the restoration. The situation has improved.
The expert, who has more than 20 years of experience, confirmed that all problems always have a solution, but if everyone talks about problems that have no solution, he worries that the future of real estate will be as bad as they say. Therefore, he urged all media and people to spread what is positive, what Cambodia has and is developing and growing.
"I urge journalists and citizens to spread the good news on social media. Good news related to society, country, economy, politics, agriculture, tourism, etc. "Information does not need to be personal or slightly dangerous. Do not try to publish too much because it is of no benefit to society." Dr. Kim Heang added.
He said that the dissemination of positive information, whether within the framework of the media or individuals, even if it can not help much to society does not cause additional problems to society. Therefore, he always advises all staff and members, all advertisements, whether related to real estate or any sector, must always embed positive thoughts, because only positive individuals say positive things and get positive results.
It should be noted that the above expert statement after KW Cambodia organized a program on real estate solutions in Cambodia on September 16, 2023 to show many people have confidence in the real estate sector in the future and the project. Land, housing and condominiums, which still play an important role to meet the needs of the people and contribute to the national economy.
