BEIJING: China's real estate slump worsened in August, with new home prices, real estate investment and sales falling sharply despite recent supportive measures, according to a report. According to Reuters.
New home prices fell the fastest pace in 10 months in August, falling 0.3 percent from July, according to data from Reuters, according to data from the National Bureau of Statistics (NBS). From a 0.2 percent decline in July.
In recent weeks, China has introduced a number of measures to boost homebuying activities, including easing some lending laws and easing homebuying restrictions in some cities.
These policies have given big cities like Beijing little incentive to sell new homes, but some worry that these stimuli could be short-lived and could dampen demand in smaller cities.
