(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian and Chinese governments are committed to opposing politics on human rights issues, the implementation of double standards and interference in the internal affairs of other countries under the pretext of human rights or democracy.
The two sides agreed to strengthen cooperation against external interference and the color revolution. This is according to the joint statement of the Cambodian-Chinese government on the results of the three-day official visit of His Excellency Hun Manet, the new Prime Minister of Cambodia to China.
The commitment was made during a bilateral meeting between Hun Manet and Chinese Premier Li Chiang in Beijing on September 15, 2023.
"Both sides express their strong opposition to politics on human rights issues, the implementation of double standards and interference in the internal affairs of other countries under the pretext of human rights or democracy." "Both sides agreed to strengthen cooperation against external interference and the color revolution." This is according to the joint announcement.
The joint statement reiterated that the Chinese side reaffirmed its full support for Cambodia's efforts to safeguard national sovereignty, security and development interests, while reaffirming its strong opposition to foreign interference in its internal affairs. Cambodia.
The joint statement reiterated that the Cambodian side reaffirmed its firm adherence to the "One China Policy" in which the Government of the People's Republic of China is the only legitimate government representing the whole of China and Taiwan is Part of it is inseparable from China's territory and internal affairs, which do not allow foreign interference.
Cambodia also opposes any attempt to interfere in China's internal affairs or obstruct or confront China under the pretext of using the Taiwan issue as an excuse or any form of separatism to demand "Taiwan independence." Cambodia strongly supports China's efforts to achieve national unity and does not establish formal relations with Taiwan in any form.
