(Phnom Penh): The National Authority for Combating Drugs, chaired by Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun, has set out five priority work directions for the future to fight drug offenses with a strong commitment. Srouch of Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia to eliminate this crime in the future.
This priority work direction was outlined by General Meas Virith, Secretary General of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, in a press conference this morning, September 16, 2023, at the Anti-Drug Department of the General Commission of Police, a day later. After the first meeting of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, which recently revised its composition in the 7th legislature yesterday.
General Meas Virith said that the National Anti-Drug Authority has divided its work into two parts, one acting politically and the other law enforcement. However, these two actors must cooperate in enforcing the law at both the national and sub-national levels in order to reduce and eliminate drug problems in the future.
Separately, the five priority work directions set by Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun, President of the National Authority for Combating Drugs and announced by General Meas Virith include:
* First, the work of education and dissemination must be done more widely, including the use of total force, special means, the use of the media and the organization of additional education and guidance to be more active, including songwriting, composing disciplines for Students take exams and shoot straight at young people and people in remote areas.
* Second: Chemical control by urgently setting up a clear chemical control mechanism. These mechanisms must be activated and sustainable, in which the Secretary-General of the National Authority for Combating Drugs must coordinate with the ministries, units and institutions involved in the use of chemicals, such as the Ministry of Health, the Ministry of Agriculture, the Ministry of Industry.
* Third: Continue to work hard to prevent the influx of drugs into Cambodia, including land, sea and air.
* Fourth: Continue to work to prevent the processing of drugs in the country by using mechanisms established in the management of chemical compounds and to control areas at risk by criminals using the place to secretly process drugs. Examples: forest areas, warehousing areas and areas sheltered under development labels.
* Fifth: Efforts to eliminate drug distribution in entertainment venues such as karaoke, entertainment club, beer garden. Currently, there are more than 1,300 suspected locations across the country that are suspected of being involved in drug cases, and the inspection of these locations is assigned to law enforcement agencies.
According to the report of General Meas Virith, Secretary General of the General Secretariat of the NEC In the first eight months of 2023, Cambodian law enforcement authorities cracked down on 5,133 drug offenses, arrested 12,491 offenders and seized 2,658.56 kilograms of drugs. 910.87 kg of chemical compound together with some related exhibits.
