Interview with General Ith Sarath on the organization of the first joint health exercise between Cambodian and Chinese troops "Angel of Peace - 2023" in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and the Chinese People's Liberation Army have launched a joint health exercise called "Peace Angel - 2023". The exercise was organized under the theme "Joint International Humanitarian Health Relief Operation in the Disaster, Flood and Flood Areas of the Cambodian and Chinese Armed Forces."
Tevta Santepheap Exercise - 2023 organized the content of the exercise as a real military force, moving to locations related to the actual situation on 7 topics, including: 1: Joint command of the joint health force, 2: Transportation Troops: 3rd: Deployment of operations, 4th: Rescue at the site, 5th: Transfer of victims for further treatment, 6th: Transfer of victims by air, and 7th: Prevent and prevent infectious diseases.
The joint exercise will last for 13 days from September 14 to 26, 2023 at the Army Special Forces Command. The Chinese side has a total of 126 personnel, including 20 exercise leaders, 10 pilots, and 95 medical personnel. The Cambodian side has a total of 595 people, including 24 exercise leaders, 237 training forces, 334 service personnel.
General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Chairman of the Joint Steering Committee for Exercises and Exercises between the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Friendly Countries and Assignments in the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, opened the exercise and gave an interview. The process of joint exercises between the two armies.
