(Phnom Penh): Cambodia and China have started six joint exercises since 2016 until 2023, of which five were military exercises, but for the sixth exercise. This both sides chose on the health sector.
The joint military exercise between the two armies was named "Peace Angel - 2023" by the two sides under the theme "Joint International Humanitarian Health Rescue Operation in the disaster areas, hurricanes and floods of both armies." From Cambodia to China. For 13 days from 14 to 26 September 2023 at the Army Special Forces Command.
At the same time, General Ith Sarath stated that the name Tevta is the one who saved the lives of the people, so the working group of the two armies decided to name it "Tevta Santepheap-2023". For naming, this is not just a nomination.
General Ith Sarath confirmed that the naming of this joint health exercise was a coincidence with the name and logo of the Cambodian People's Party. The joint health exercise between the Cambodian and Chinese armies is to save humanity, and the CPP is the party that saves the lives of the people.
It should be noted that this joint health exercise is a real force of troops moving around the location related to the actual situation on the above 7 topics, including: 1: Joint health force command, 2: Transportation Troops: 3rd: Deployment of operations, 4th: Rescue at the site, 5th: Transfer of victims for further treatment, 6th: Transfer of victims by air, and 7th: Prevent and prevent infectious diseases.
The exercise is to celebrate the 65th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic ties between Cambodia and China, to enhance capacity, exchange experiences in health cooperation, effective disaster relief and communicable disease operations. And so on.
In the first medical exercise, the Chinese side had a total of 126 participants, including 20 exercise leaders, 10 pilots, and 95 health personnel. The Cambodian side has a total of 595 people, including 24 exercise leaders, 237 training forces, 334 service personnel.
In the first Cambodian-Chinese military health exercise, the Chinese side used one Y-9 ambulance, three ambulances (one ambulance, one ambulance, one ambulance). 1 low-pressure rescue unit) about 1,000 sets of rescue equipment and all kinds of warranty equipment and use 6 Y-20A transport aircraft to transport troops and equipment.
For the Cambodian side, use 2 Mi-17 helicopters, 2 Z-9 helicopters, 6 ambulances, as well as some medical and rescue equipment.
