Japan has deployed personnel to UN peacekeeping operations for the first time in its history. This year marks the 30th anniversary of the Constituent Assembly elections organized by UNTAC. The National Assembly issues a decision on the principle of appointing advisers and assistants without equal status for civil servants, lawyers and tycoons
(Phnom Penh): The National Assembly has issued a new decision on the principles of appointing advisors and assistants of the National Assembly. The conditions for the appointment of advisors and assistants are the same as for the appointment of advisors and assistants within the framework of the Royal Government. The decision emphasizes the appointment of advisers or assistants who are civil servants, lawyers or tycoons, the duke does not provide equal status and compensation.
Article 1 states that this decision is made for the purpose of determining the principles, conditions and procedures for the appointment of advisors and assistants of the National Assembly, including advisors and assistants of the National Assembly, advisors and assistants to the President of the National Assembly and the Vice President of the National Assembly. Perform functions.
Article 5 emphasizes that the appointment of advisors and assistants of the National Assembly, advisors and assistants to the President of the National Assembly and the Vice-President of the National Assembly must meet any of the following principles and conditions:
1: Political officials or other persons who are not in the framework of civil servants, police officers or soldiers can be appointed as advisors or assistants of the National Assembly by receiving equal status in addition to the current position and any level of salary. .
2. The appointment of civil servants of the General Secretariat of the National Assembly to serve as advisors or assistants of the National Assembly, advisors or assistants to the President of the National Assembly and the Vice President of the National Assembly in addition to the current functions shall not affect the performance of duties as civil servants and shall not be given equal status. And no severance pay.
3. Civil servants, national police officers and soldiers may be appointed as advisors or assistants of the National Assembly in addition to their current positions, provided that the civil servants do not receive the same status and any additional salary.
4. A lawyer or a freelance professional who is practicing may be appointed as an advisor or assistant to the National Assembly and an advisor or assistant to the President of the National Assembly and the Vice President of the National Assembly on the condition that there is no promotion equal to any level of salary.
5. A lawyer or a freelancer who is not a professional can be appointed as an advisor and assistant to the National Assembly, an advisor and an assistant to the President of the National Assembly and the Vice President of the National Assembly with the same status and salary.
6. A person who is a member of the board of directors or manages a private company or a person who has been conferred the title of Duke may be appointed as an advisor or assistant to the National Assembly on the condition that there is no status equal to any level of salary.
It should be noted that on September 6, 2023, the Acting Head of State, Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, also issued a Royal Decree on the principles for the appointment of advisors and assistants in the executive branch.
These decisions are seen as a reform in the appointment of advisers and assistants, which in part helps reduce national budget expenditures.
10 benefits that the government continues to provide workers in the new mandate
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia, the seventh mandate, continues to implement the 10 recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the former Prime Minister, which provide benefits to workers.
This is the confirmation of Samdech Moha Boravati Hun Manet, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, who spoke at a recent meeting with workers.
The 10 benefits include:
First. The minimum wage is $ 200, excluding the other five benefits that an average worker earns between $ 217-259 and is paid twice a month.
Fourth. Received postpartum allowance, with one child receiving 800,000 riels, two children receiving 1.2 million riels and three children receiving 1.6 million riels, as well as an additional 5 million riels from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit himself.
Fifth. Employers pay 100% social security contributions for health care on behalf of workers.
Sixth. Continue to monitor rents without raising them too high, while the price of water and electricity in rented houses connects to the electricity and water supply from the state and the state.
7th. Strengthen the implementation of the SPI law, especially the social security system for pensions.
8th. Implement the labor law to determine the payment of seniority pay to workers almost every six months.
9th. Addressing safety issues in transportation and travel of workers, improving transportation and enforcing traffic laws.
10th. Expanding cooperation with partner countries to provide employment opportunities, protect the rights and interests of overseas workers, and access to social protection, both now and in return.
