BEIJING: Chinese President Xi Jinping said on Friday that China supports Zambia in defending its national sovereignty, security and development interests and encourages more imports from the South African country. . This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Friday, September 15, 2023.
Xi met with Zambian President Hakainde Hichilema in Beijing to promote the two countries' relationship as a "comprehensive strategic partnership." Xi is committed to working with Zambia to expand cooperation in the fields of agricultural infrastructure, mining and clean energy.
He thanked China for supporting Zambia's membership in the 20-nation bloc of the African Union and China's positive role in resolving Zambia's debt problems.
At the meeting, President Xi Jinping extended a warm and cordial welcome and emphasized that Cambodia-China friendship is like a huge tree that is deeply rooted and strong and the nation Both bear priceless fruit forever.
The President also congratulated Samdech Hun Sen, who was elected by the people and the National Assembly as the Prime Minister of Cambodia for the 7th legislature of the National Assembly. The President is confident that under the leadership of the President, the friendship and solidarity of the two countries will continue to grow and become even stronger.
The President also took this wonderful opportunity to send his condolences and love to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Chairman of the Supreme Council of the King, who has overcome and overcome all obstacles and external pressures to maintain and strengthen Friendship and solidarity between the two countries.
In response, President Hun Manet thanked for the warm welcome from the Chinese leadership, especially from the President during his official visit.
The President conveyed the condolences and greetings from Samdech Techo to Samdech Techo's old friends and especially to the President.
He also thanked the country and the people of China for their attention and warm welcome to the visit of His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia and His Majesty the King of Cambodia. Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, Queen Mother of Cambodia in Beijing. Your Excellency, please appreciate this priceless gesture.
During the meeting, the President and the President discussed the continuation of the policy of peace between the two countries. In fact, the President affirmed that China remains a good friend and will continue to assist Cambodia on the path of economic development. The current official visit of the President will bring more success to the achievement of building a common destiny community in the new era between Cambodia and China.
The President informed the Chinese President of Cambodia's policy position on China, especially the continued implementation of a Chinese policy.
He further highlighted the long-standing Cambodia-China relations that the two nations are bearing fruit in all fields, especially economy and education. The development and progress of Cambodia today is inseparable from the support and cooperation of the Chinese friends, as was the support of China in the difficult circumstances of the fight against Kovid-19.
He outlined the direction and areas of future cooperation between the two countries, such as energy, food security and investment. In fact, the President requested the Chinese side to continue to support Cambodia's guarantee of energy security and food security, and thanked for the import of rice and other agricultural products from Cambodia.
He also thanked China for its past efforts to encourage and encourage Chinese investors to invest in Cambodia. Especially in key priority areas that benefit the Cambodian people.
Before concluding the talks, the Chinese President reaffirmed to the President that China will continue to support and cooperate with Cambodia in all areas without change, and China is committed to protecting justice for both nations from any attempt at roadmap. Any negatives.
The President stated that China is always ready to welcome the visit of Samdech Techo, his old friend.
