Attracting investors is an important agenda of the Prime Minister's first official visit to China. On the morning of Friday, September 15, 2023, His Excellency Hun Manet took the time out of a busy visit to participate in a forum and talk with Chinese and Cambodian investors and businessmen.
President Hun Manet told Cambodian and Chinese investors and businessmen attending the event that Cambodia has set 2023 as the year to start boosting its economy towards achieving the policy of being a high-economic country by 2050. .
The Prime Minister stated that in the spirit of the Royal Government led by Samdech himself, the investment law with attractive and specific incentives, as well as the Public-Private Partnership Law, was an example of commitment. In addition, the Royal Government has identified improving the business environment, investment and the private sector as a priority.
At the same time, the Royal Government will strengthen the dialogue with the private sector by organizing regular forums of the Royal Government and the private sector, with Samdech directly presiding.
For Samdech President Hun Manet, according to the commitment and mechanism set by the Royal Government, Cambodia will be an attractive and potential destination of the private sector.
With the urging of Chinese investors and businessmen to come to study and invest in Cambodia, President Hun Manet assured the protection of Chinese investors. "Chinese investors can do business and invest in Cambodia fruitfully and grow."
Please note that mobilizing investment is a priority of the Royal Government to boost the national economy and create jobs for people. Therefore, this first official visit to China, attracting investment is also a necessary agenda for President Hun Manet.
