On the evening of September 15, she was invited by Chinese government officials to visit the Great Hall of the People. Her Excellency carefully examined the presentation of the leadership of the Great Hall of the People of China.
The Great Hall of the People is a state building located west of Tiananmen Square in Beijing. The Great Hall of the People is used for legislative activities and celebrations by the Chinese government and the Chinese Communist Party. The Great Hall of the People serves as a meeting place for the plenary session of the National People's Congress, which takes place every year during March, along with the national session of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference.
The Great Hall of the People is also the meeting place of the National Congress of the Communist Party of China. Since the 12th Congress in 1982, meetings have been held every five years, and the Party Central Committee has met once a year.
The Great Hall of the People is also used for many important events, including national meetings of various social and political organizations, national anniversaries, as well as memorials for former leaders.
The People's Monument is also a popular tourist attraction in the city, with tourists visiting the capital frequently each year.
The Great Hall of the People is also used by the Chinese government as a venue for the presence of leaders of friendly countries.
On the occasion of the visit, the leaders of the Great Hall of the People of China exhibited beautiful paintings in the Great Hall of the People, especially the works of previous generations of Chinese great men. She thanked the Chinese leadership for allowing her to visit and explore the glorious civilization of the Great Hall of the People.
This morning, she was also scheduled to visit the Great Wall of China.
