The Speaker of the National People's Congress (NPC) made the remarks during a courtesy call and discussion with President Hun Manet on Friday morning, September 15, 2023, at the Great Hall of the People in Beijing, China.
During the meeting, in addition to praising the selection of China for the official visit, Zhao Liji also congratulated the President, who was elected by the people and the National Assembly as Prime Minister. Le Chi also congratulated the CPP on its glorious victory in the July 23, 2023 election.
He also stressed that Cambodia-China friendship, solidarity and cooperation will contribute to building a common destiny community in the new era, and the two nations will benefit from this community building.
He thanked the Chinese people and government for their significant contribution to Cambodia's socio-economic development process, such as providing timely support to Cambodia during the difficult period of the Kovid-19 crisis.
The President also reiterated to Chao Le Chi that the continuation of Cambodia's position and foreign policy under the leadership of the President, despite the changing world and uncertainty. The President and Zhao Liji further discussed the direction of enhancing relations between the two countries, especially within the framework of parliamentary relations.
As a member of the National Assembly, the President encouraged the frequent and regular exchanges of visits between the Cambodian and Chinese parliaments, as the visit would benefit both legislatures, especially for the younger members of parliament. Exploring and exchanging experiences and perspectives together.
Zhao Liji also agreed to the proposal and pledged to promote better and more peaceful relations between the two parliaments without setting any conditions or embedding any agenda.
While agreeing to continue cooperating, exchanging experiences and striving to successfully implement previously agreed projects, the President and Mr. Zhao Liji agreed on the principles of continuing to build democracy in accordance with the conditions of each nation. Serve the benefit of the people as a whole. Overall, Cambodia and China are committed to continuing to work together as good, trustworthy friends and to continue to unite together to resist any outside attempt or interference.
Before concluding the discussion, Mr. Zhao Leji sent a message of congratulations to Samdech Moha National Assembly President Khuon Sodary and to Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Vibol Sena Phekdey Say Chhum.
Minister of Public Works Leads Helmet Ride Campaign in Siem Reap to Promote Traffic Safety
(Siem Reap): Mr. Peng Po, Minister of Public Works and Transport, presided over the campaign to ride motorcycles wearing helmets, send messages and remind all road users to respect the law on road traffic in order to contribute to prevention and reduction. Traffic accidents should be kept to a minimum and in line with the National Road Safety Action Decade 2021-2030.
The event was held at the Siem Reap Teacher Training College this Friday morning, September 15, 2023, with the participation of the Deputy Governor of the Board of Governors of Siem Reap and representatives of the Asian Injury Prevention Foundation in Cambodia, teachers and A total of 450 students.
Speaking on that occasion, the Minister also mentioned the data related to traffic accidents and the main causes of traffic accidents to inform the ceremony to raise awareness to participate in the prevention of all circles.
He also urged all members of the ceremony, especially government officials, teachers and students present here to be a good example of road safety work by wearing a helmet while traveling on a motorcycle. Go near and far and participate in obeying the law on road traffic consistently.
The Minister also handed over 500 helmets to students, teachers and then led a procession of about 100 motorbikes to ride helmets and visit traffic safety booths. (Video inside) (Beijing, China): The Prime Minister of Cambodia, His Excellency Hun Manet, has announced the position of the Royal Government of Cambodia for the seventh mandate by continuing to adhere to the one-China policy.
The remarks were made on the occasion of His Majesty the King's participation in a forum to talk and eat with Chinese and Cambodian investors and businessmen on Friday morning, September 15, 2023 in Beijing.
In this forum, Samdech forgot to appreciate the belt and road initiative launched by Chinese President Xi Jinping. He considered that this initiative is the key to boosting economic growth, trade and Chinese investors, as well as promoting cooperation in all fields between Cambodia and China.
He added that in this spirit, the Royal Government of Cambodia considers China as a strong and reliable partner for Cambodia's future development, and Cambodia will continue to support and welcome the Belt and Road Initiative.
"The Royal Government of Cambodia under my leadership will also continue to maintain a strong policy for China, especially the one-China policy, and oppose any internal Chinese interference," he added.
He said that Cambodia sees national and international businessmen and investors as indispensable actors, and the Royal Government is committed to promoting the development of the private sector to become a real driving force in boosting national economic growth.
Through this business forum, Cambodia hopes that Cambodia will become an attractive and potential investment destination. Samdech invited Chinese investors to study the potential and invest more in Cambodia.
Phnom Penh Unity Command focuses on the successful implementation of the first phase of the Pentagon Strategy
