(Phnom Penh): A police officer was handcuffed and sent to court for legal action after driving a car and hitting a woman, falling from a motorbike and then driving to death in front of Wat Russey Sros, concrete road, Koh Nora village, Niroth commune, Khan Chbar Ampov on the afternoon of September 13, 2023.
The victim was Prum Eang, 64, a salesman living in Koh Nora village, Niroth commune, Chbar Ampov district. Separately, the suspect named Sot Sethy, 53 years old, the position of Deputy Chief of Police, Logistics, Prek Eang Intervention Unit, living at house No. 15F8, Chrey Kong Village, Sangkat Choam Chao 2, Khan Por Sen Chey.
When the victim saw the car, he told his daughter to ride in the back of the car so that the car could drive first, but the suspect did not drive forward. The victim continued to ride a motorcycle to the scene, the suspect drove the car and hit the victim to fall from the motorcycle on the sidewalk and then drove the car, crushing the victim's head, causing his immediate death.
After crushing the victim, the suspect drove away and left in front of the unnumbered plot next to the fence of Chbar Ampov High School. .
After that, the police checked the camera and did the forensic examination, took the nails in the car and the suspects were the same person. On September 13, 2023, the police detained the suspect and sent him to the Chbar Ampov District Police Inspectorate for questioning.
At present, the suspect and the car exhibit have built a case to be sent to court for legal action.
After receiving this information, the Ministry of Justice conducted an urgent search on the morning of September 15, 2023. According to the research and records in the condemnation list of the General Department of Criminal Affairs of the Ministry of Justice, Khim Phearun did not apply for a judgment bulletin from the Ministry of Justice, and the Ministry of Justice did not provide the bulletin.
The above research results show that the publication of information on a Facebook page called San Prum is a false information that is defamatory to the Ministry of Justice. Therefore, the Ministry of Justice will take legal action in this case for disseminating false information that is defamatory of state institutions.
