Speaking on the special live program on "Tax Awareness" on September 15, 2023, Mr. Kong Vibol, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Director General of the General Department of Taxation, confirmed that as scheduled on January 1. In 2024, the General Department of Taxation will start implementing the collection of tax revenue "on capital gains tax" unless there is a decision from the Royal Government to extend the implementation or not.
He said that the capital gains tax is not a new tax, as it was introduced in the law a long time ago, but the government has continued to delay its implementation and needs time to study the tax in its entirety.
He stressed that although the real estate sector has not improved, the implementation of the capital gains tax will not affect the real estate sector, as the tax is only on the sale of profitable real estate.
Resident legal entities who have already registered the tax and declared the annual income tax are no longer liable for this tax.
Capital gains tax is levied on capital gains achieved at the time of the sale or transfer of profitable capital only, in the absence of profit, there is no obligation to pay this tax.
For the calculation of tax on capital gain is the profit from the sale or transfer of capital multiplied by the tax rate of 20%, and for capital as real estate, the property owner can choose the method of deducting expenses. Expenditures account for 80% of the proceeds from the sale or transfer of real estate;
The Chinese President paid tribute to Samdech Techo Hun Sen during a working meeting with Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Manet on Monday morning, September 15, 2023.
