World Food Program Executive Director Cindy McCain told the UN Security Council that the lack of funding has forced the agency to cut food for millions and make more cuts. . It is estimated that this is just the first step in the famine for nearly 47 million people in more than 50 countries, and that 45 million children under the age of five are suffering from acute malnutrition.
