"The Ministry would like to congratulate the company for its efforts to work closely with hydropower to achieve the first export of Cambodian fishery products to the Chinese market on September 14, 2023," she said.
She added that the first priority will be to maintain quality in accordance with the hygiene and phytosanitary standards set by the Chinese Customs Administration to ensure that Cambodian fishery products can still be imported into the Chinese market.
The next task is to promote Cambodian fishery products with higher quality, better aesthetics, safer and tastier in order to strengthen and expand the needs of customers in the Chinese market. Exports of fishery products from Cambodia to China will increase. As for aquaculture, fish farmers in Cambodia will have more jobs.
She added that by promoting the export of Cambodian fishery products to the Chinese market, the Ministry hopes that it will be able to improve the livelihood of our Cambodian fishermen and contribute to the national economic growth. .
