The Prime Minister thanked for the congratulations and praised the success of the company in achieving many achievements in Cambodia, especially the construction of the Lower Sesan 2 Dam, which is a large project and can be considered a model station. By ensuring a good environment.
He also said that Cambodia welcomes the import of new and modern technologies to develop the energy sector in Cambodia and encourages companies to learn more about the expansion of the electricity grid to better serve the interests of the people. Up. He also encouraged companies to develop clean energy systems and battery-powered power systems.
In response, Mr. Vin Su Kaing confirmed that the company will continue to promote the study and introduction of new technologies, and the company will discuss with the relevant ministries and institutions and examine the possibility of training this technical technical skills to young Cambodians.
He also congratulated CRBC on its achievements in the past and praised the study and exploration of other potential areas in Cambodia.
Mr. Wang Tongju expressed his congratulations to the President, who was elected by the people and the National Assembly to lead the Royal Government for the 7th legislature, and expressed his deep gratitude for allowing him and the company delegation to pay a courtesy call.
Mr. Wang Tong Chou also reported to the President on road investment projects in progress in Cambodia, as well as new projects that the company is studying and evaluating, as well as requesting further cooperation and coordination from the Royal Government of Cambodia.
He highlighted the important role of investment projects in roads, bridges and expressways in the process of socio-economic development, especially in enhancing Cambodia's competitiveness through the improvement of logistics systems. For the project that is being studied and evaluated, Samdech Thipadei requested the company side to speed up these matters by continuing to cooperate with the ministries, institutions or relevant parties in Cambodia.
He also instructed the relevant ministries and institutions to continue to provide cooperation and coordination to ensure job sustainability in order to encourage the projects under study to be completed and put into operation soon.
He praised CRBC for its contribution to the development process in Cambodia through the achievement of road investment projects, especially the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway. He stressed that the Royal Government of Cambodia is ready to cooperate and coordinate further with the company and encourage CRBC to continue to invest more in Cambodia.
