Ministry of Health warns of rising dengue fever
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health has called on people to be very careful about the increase in dengue cases for 2023, as the dengue fever cycle has an abnormally high cycle every 5 to 6 years.
The Ministry of Health also reminded all people to continue to be vigilant and responsible in protecting their personal and family health, to prevent the spread of dengue fever, and to participate in preventing large-scale dengue outbreaks in Make the community more effective by implementing the following measures:
Step # 4- Discovering Your Purpose There is no such thing as a "clean" home. And that can easily bite us. During the day it is necessary to wear long-sleeved clothes, sleep under a mosquito net regularly day and night and not to sit near dark places.
Step 5: In case of high fever, the patient should be taken to the nearest health center and hospital immediately.
At the same time, the Ministry of Health urges the general public to follow the above simple advice to protect your health and the health of your family and wish you all good health and avoid dengue fever. The Ministry of Health will continue to inform the public about the development of health problems through the telegram, Facebook page and website of the Ministry of Health, as well as the website which has health education materials that can be downloaded and used. .
British government says China is trying to lure British spies to access intelligence and special skills
LONDON (Reuters) - Chinese intelligence is targeting British officials in sensitive positions as part of a more sophisticated intelligence operation to gain access to intelligence and special skills, the British government said on Thursday. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on September 14, 2023.
"The government is aware that Chinese recruitment schemes are attempting to lure British and allies into key positions with sensitive knowledge and experience," the government said.
Concerns about Chinese activity in Britain have been growing and worsening since the revelations over the weekend that a parliamentary researcher was arrested in March on suspicion of spying. China.
The arrest of the young researcher has led to calls from British MPs to take a tougher stance on China. The Chinese Foreign Ministry described the allegations as "baseless."
British Prime Minister Sunak has come under pressure from some lawmakers in his Conservative party to take a hard line on China, but he wants to strengthen economic ties with tightening national security.
A report by the British Parliament's Intelligence and Security Committee said Beijing had successfully infiltrated all sectors of the British economy and that ministers had been slow to address the threat.
