On September 13, 2023, up to 28 schools and 14,412 students across the country announced their commitment to participate in the "Do not use plastic bags" campaign. The announcement of the active participation of students in schools is a hope and a good current to move towards the maximum reduction in the use of plastic bags in Cambodian society.
As the launcher of this campaign, Mr. Eang Sophalleth expressed his great pleasure for the commitment of the school leaders, teachers and students.
"On behalf of the Ministry of Environment and on my own behalf, I would like to express my deepest gratitude to Excellencies, Lok Chumteavs, Ladies and Gentlemen, Teachers and all my dear children who participated in the campaign to reduce the use of bags. Plastic. This is a happy expression of thanks from the Minister of Environment.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth emphasized that the participation of school leaders, teachers and students will help make the country environment beautiful, non-toxic, a paradise for all Cambodians.
However, the Minister continued to call on teachers to help promote this campaign even more.
It should be noted that on September 1, 2023, Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Minister of Environment, announced a campaign to reduce the use of plastic bags in schools. This campaign aims to reduce the use of plastic bags in Cambodian society.
Since the launch of the campaign on September 1, a total of 80 schools have participated in the campaign for environmental value, with a total of 79,068 students in the capital, including: Tbong Khmum, Siem Reap, Pailin, Prey Veng, Kampot, Svay Rieng and Phnom Penh ....
Plastic bags are a worrying issue that is spreading around the world. Every year, 300 million tons of plastic waste are generated and it takes 1,000 years to decompose. This problem is also happening in Cambodia. Population growth and rapid economic growth have led to a significant increase in the amount of waste. In Phnom Penh, more than 3,500 tonnes of waste is generated daily, of which 20 percent is plastic.
