Kampong Cham Provincial Governor Orders Authorities to Inspect and Close Cafe near Sihanoukville High School After Finding Impact on Students' Education
(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, ordered the police to immediately investigate the cafe near Sihanoukville High School in Kampong Cham City after receiving information that the business was irregular and affected the students' education. .
The provincial governor assigned the authority on September 14, 2023 in the 52nd Ordinary Meeting of the third mandate of Kampong Cham Provincial Council.
Provincial Councilor, Ms. On Heng Leakena, said that recently, parents of students reported that there are many coffee shops in the New World Borey block near Sihanoukville High School, which looks like the business. Beyond regular coffee sales.
The provincial councilor added that students were sometimes seen smoking and playing loud loudspeakers, disturbing the neighbors. Students are sometimes spotted playing games such as poker and some online games, such as cockfighting or football betting. Therefore, there is a request from the people in the area, as well as parents of students to ask the authorities to take action on this case.
At the suggestion of the provincial councilor, Mr. Un Chanda also ordered the police to inspect and take strict measures. If there are any irregularities that affect the future of the students, the authorities should close the cafes immediately.
