(Phnom Penh): The Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) in Cambodia is committed to continuing its cooperation and supporting the Royal Government of Cambodia as well as the Ministry of Rural Development in achieving the rural development goals, especially focusing on Build physical infrastructure, schools, hospitals, as well as provide education, send specialists to train in Cambodia.
On that occasion, the Minister thanked the Royal Government of Japan through JICA, which has always cooperated and provided assistance to Cambodia since the Royal Government of Cambodia, the sixth mandate under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
The Minister said that the Ministry of Rural Development has prepared four priority programs:
1. Develop physical and transport infrastructure to expand the scope of rural road systems to promote economic growth in rural areas.
2. Improve the living conditions of rural communities by providing adequate access to clean water, maintaining adequate sanitation, and educating people to change their attitudes towards stopping open defecation.
3. Diversify rural economic activities, continue to promote the rural economy by training people in basic skills to create businesses other than agriculture.
In response, the President of JICA mentioned the good cooperation between the Royal Government of Japan and the Royal Government of Cambodia in the past by helping to build physical infrastructure, build schools, hospitals, as well as help in the field of education through the provision of Scholarships and sending specialists to train in Cambodia.
He also mentioned the close cooperation with the Ministry of Rural Development in building rural roads to connect with potential urban areas.
"The Royal Government of Japan, through JICA, has pledged to continue to support the Royal Government of Cambodia as well as the Ministry of Rural Development in achieving the goal of improving rural development and eradicating poverty," he said.
Minister Chhay Rithy Sen thanked the Government of Japan through JICA for its continued assistance to Cambodia in all areas, despite the current global crisis. He regarded the Japanese government as a strategic friend and committed to continue cooperating and supporting each other forever.
