(Pursat): The 135.25 km South National Road 5 Rehabilitation Project is divided into three packages, starting from Prek Kdam (Kandal Province) to Thla Mam (Pursat Province). At a cost of 246.35 million US dollars, 90% of the construction has been completed so far.
The project includes the construction of 5 inter-city roads with a total length of 62 km, 4 lanes, 23 meters wide, and Sour Chbar Kandal, the expansion of the old bridge and the construction of a new bridge in the section of National Road No. 5 in total. 80 places.
