The official visit of His Excellency Hun Manet to the country, which has been named the great power of the region and the world, was made at the invitation of Chinese Premier Li Chheang. This official visit takes place from 14 to 16 September 2023.
According to the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs, accompanying Samdech Manet on his official visit to China are: Deputy Prime Minister, Ministers, as well as senior government officials and other private sector leaders. .
Hun Manet will also hold bilateral talks with Chinese Premier Li Chiang on bilateral and multilateral cooperation between the two countries. The two prime ministers will also preside over the signing ceremony of a number of cooperation documents.
In addition to the official visit, His Excellency Hun Manet will also attend the 20th ASEAN-China Expo from September 16 to 17 in Nanning, Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region.
The official visit of His Excellency Hun Manet has become an exchange visit that has attracted a lot of attention from the national and international community, coinciding with the interesting visit of two other world leaders, the President's visit. US President Joe Biden to Vietnam and North Korean President Kim Jong Un's visit to Russia.
These visits are seen not only as a framework for strengthening bilateral relations and cooperation, but also for the development of regional and global political situations.
Please note that Cambodia and China were connected on July 19, 1958. On December 13, 2010, the two countries' relations were upgraded to a comprehensive strategic partnership, a high-level relationship.
Through this top-level relationship, Cambodia and China have established many cooperation agreements on political, economic and people-to-people contacts. Through this relationship, the exchange of royal visits and frequent visits between the two countries was made. His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni has visited China 21 times. Samdech Techo has been to China 15 times.
Apart from the previous leaders, the current Chinese leaders are all visiting Cambodia. Xi Jinping paid state visits in 2016, Li Keqiang paid official visits in 2018 and 2022.
In addition, Chinese Foreign Ministers and senior officials have frequently visited Cambodia to promote bilateral relations and cooperation.
In terms of trade, the two countries have decided to establish a free trade agreement and enter into force in January 2022, which will open up greater trade. The two countries have set a trade target of $ 15 billion by 2025.
China is also a country that has contributed to building human resources in Cambodia. From the 2018-2019 academic year to the 2022-2023 academic year, China provides scholarships to a total of 778 Cambodian students. China has also announced an increase in the number of scholarships by about 500 a year for five years from 2022 to 2027.
China has also contributed a lot of aid and interest-free loans to help develop Cambodia. From 2001 to September 30, 2022, China provided more than $ 2 billion in interest-free loans and assistance to Cambodia, the report said.
From 2001 to September 30, 2022, China provided more than $ 5 billion in loans, focusing on the construction of transport infrastructure, including roads and bridges.
China is also a major contributor to the fight against the 19 epidemic of Kovid. China has become an indispensable support for preventing the spread of Kovid 19 in Cambodia. Of that, a total of nearly 42 million doses of vaccines were received from Cambodia from China.
