The death toll from a fire that engulfed a residential building in the Vietnamese capital of Hanoi has risen to more than 30, local media reported on Wednesday. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on September 13, 2023.
However, Vietnamese authorities have not yet issued a statement confirming the latest death toll.
The fire broke out just minutes before midnight on Tuesday at the parking lot of a 10-storey apartment building.
Firefighters took full control of the situation Wednesday morning as the search for survivors continued. The blaze comes just one year after 32 people died in a fire at a karaoke bar in Ho Chi Minh City. In Vietnam, fires have become more frequent in recent years, especially at karaoke bars.
