(VOVworld) - At the invitation of the Government of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region of the People's Republic of China on the morning of September 13, 2023 in Hong Kong, ASEAN Secretary-General Dr. Kao Kim Hourn attended the opening ceremony of the Belt and Road Summit. The eighth time.
The theme of the summit is "Growth under a Decade of Collaboration." The ceremony was attended by John KC Lee, Chief Executive Officer of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region, ministers and other business leaders.
During the meeting, the two sides discussed new ways and ideas to enhance educational opportunities for ASEAN students in Hong Kong and Hong Kong students in ASEAN, to increase people-to-people exchanges, and education between ASEAN and Hong Kong.
In the afternoon of the same day in Hong Kong, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn addressed a luncheon at the Belt and Road Summit.
The ASEAN Secretary-General highlighted the need to strengthen the integration of the Belt and Road Initiative (BRI) with the 2025 ASEAN Connectivity Roadmap and the ASEAN Vision on the Indo-Pacific to Provide More Effective and Efficient Cooperation. Paving the way for areas to become more resilient and interconnected.
During a working visit to Hong Kong on the afternoon of September 13, 2023, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn also met with John Lee, Executive Director of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region at the Government House.
During the meeting, the two sides discussed practical cooperation between ASEAN and Hong Kong, especially in areas where Hong Kong can contribute to supporting ASEAN initiatives. The two sides also discussed progress on the implementation of the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership (RCEP), including procedures for joining the RCEP.
At the meeting, the ASEAN Secretary-General encouraged people-to-people contacts to be strengthened by seeking cooperation with ASEAN sports, as well as exchanging best practices for the development and implementation of industry, tourism and related industries. Will travel.
In the evening of the same day, at the Hong Kong Government House, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn hosted a welcome dinner hosted by Hong Kong Special Administrative Region Executive Director John Lee to welcome international guests to the 8th Belt and Road Summit. .
