Strengthen audit and inspection work to increase work efficiency and transparency between project implementation units and fund owners.
In response to the leaders' challenges and suggestions during the meeting, the Minister also agreed with the leaders in charge.
With that, the Minister reiterated the four priority programs that the Ministry must strive to achieve, including:
* Develop physical infrastructure and cellular communication to ensure integrated rural areas and to stimulate the arteries of economic growth to rural areas.
* Improve the living conditions of rural communities in order to change the living habits of people in rural areas with comfort and hygiene.
Diversify rural economic activities through basic skills training to create jobs and careers in order to increase household economic income in rural areas.
Strengthen administrative and general affairs support services to strengthen institutions aimed at serving the rural people with integrity and high responsibility.
The Minister also gave recommendations and instructions to the leaders in charge and civil servants under the supervision of the two units as follows:
1. The officers of both units must continue to work hard to fulfill their existing roles and responsibilities in order to achieve more success for the Royal Government of the 7th legislature in order to achieve the vision "2030 Cambodia is a high middle income country and 2050 as a country "There is a high income."
2. The leaders and officials of both units must abide by the rules and regulations of the regular monthly, quarterly and semi-regular meetings and must report and ask for advice in a timely manner.
(Phnom Penh): The Government of the French Republic and the French Agency for Development (AFD) have expressed their commitment to continue cooperation with the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, especially in the areas of education, technical and vocational training (TVET) and the security sector. Society (CPF), which these two parts are in line with the recommendations of Samdech Hun Sen Net, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
