The Minister also expressed support for the above-mentioned areas and pledged to continue to strengthen cooperation with the French government, especially with the AFD project, to achieve maximum results. Samdech Thep Hun Sen Comes Out to Seek Justice to Help a Woman in Banteay Meanchey Get Her Land Back
According to Uth Kim Eng, she and her family often live and work in Thailand and have an elderly mother guarding their house and more than 30 acres of land near the village. This land is also grown by her mother every year. Unfortunately, her mother died in 2021.
After her mother died, her farm, which she used to grow potatoes every year, became the property of three people, divided into three new titles.
Ms. Uth Kim Eng described that she had been trying to sue through the commune for two years to demand justice for the return of her mother's land, but the local authorities were unable to provide justice. The commune chief's compromise was for her to divide the land into two equal parts with the new occupiers, but she did not agree with the verdict and continued to protest and spread the word on social media.
The news also reached Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, and Samdech assigned Mr. Panh Khem Bunthorn, Deputy Director of the Prime Minister's Cabinet, to resolve this issue, which is one of 21 disputes in O'Bei Choan commune.
As a result, only one day, Mr. Panh Khem Bunthon found the truth and helped Ms. Uth Kim Eng get justice to get her mother's land back.
With the return of justice, Ms. Uth Kim Eng expressed her deep gratitude to Samdech Hun Sen Manet for coming out to seek justice for her.
"Today I received a new plot of land on my old land," she said on her Facebook page. I am really excited and happy to find something incomparable. Justice exists and justice does exist for weak people like me. Living under the shadow of peace, the suffering of the people as well as the suffering of the leaders ... "
Ms. Kim Eng continued, "In the past, I used to cry for months and years because of the land issue that the former commune clerk and former sub-village conspired to resell after my mother died."
Along with thanking His Majesty the King Hun Manet, Ms. Kim Eng prayed to the sacred objects throughout Cambodia by helping to nurture and care for His Majesty the King Hun Manet to meet only peace, health and peace for the people of Cambodia. Both Cambodia. Good young people unite to support drug eradication! Nationwide drug crackdown for September 13: 43 cases cracked, 154 arrested
