Senior Minister Ouk Rabun makes 10 recommendations to stakeholders to improve food security and nutrition
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Ouk Rabun, Chairman of the Council for Agricultural and Rural Development and Chairman of the Joint Technical Working Group on Food Security and Nutrition, made 10 recommendations to stakeholders to work together to improve food security and Nutrition is one of the challenges in the world today.
On the morning of September 13, 2023, Dr. Ouk Rabun, Senior Minister, met with development partners in the Joint Technical Working Group on Food Security and Nutrition. The ceremony was also attended by relevant officials.
Senior Minister Ouk Rabun emphasized that the food security and nutrition sectors have played an important role in contributing to human capital development, work efficiency, economic growth and social progress.
During the ceremony, the Senior Minister raised a number of issues that negatively affected the food security and nutrition situation. According to the senior minister, issues that negatively affect food security and nutrition include rapid urban development, migration, global epidemics of Kovid 19, climate change, demographic change and economic and social progress.
For Senior Minister Ouk Rabun, the issue also poses new challenges that threaten the health and potential of economic growth, both now and in the future.
"Without attention to health, food security and nutrition, the benefits of economic development will be diminished by the inevitable losses of malnutrition and the cost of care and treatment. Non-infectious diseases such as diabetes, stroke and heart disease. And so on. ” This is the highlight of Senior Minister Ouk Rabun.
The Senior Minister said that the Royal Government of the 7th legislature of the National Assembly, His Majesty the Prime Minister Hun Manet, the Prime Minister of Cambodia will continue to strengthen cooperation with development partners in countries in the region and the United Nations to promote food security and Strengthen nutrition, resilience to climate change, crises and other challenges by pushing the food system towards green development.
To improve food security and nutrition, Senior Minister Ouk Rabun made the following 10 recommendations:
First, request the General Secretariat of the Council for Agricultural and Rural Development, which is the Secretariat of the Joint Technical Working Group on Food Security and Nutrition, to continue to cooperate with relevant ministries, institutions, sub-national administrations, development partners, civil society and the private sector to find implementation budgets. The priority action plan in the roadmap on the Global Action Plan to respond effectively to children's malnutrition.
Third, request the General Secretariat of the Council for Agricultural and Rural Development to cooperate with relevant ministries, institutions, sub-national administrations, civil society development partners to prepare the third National Strategy on Food Security and Nutrition from 2024 to 2028 in line with the Pentagon strategy. The first phase will raise funds to implement this strategy.
Fourth, Mr. Sok Silo, a key figure in the movement to improve nutrition in Cambodia and convened a national meeting on the food system, must continue to strengthen cooperation with relevant ministries, institutions, donor networks, UN networks, business networks and affiliates. Civil society organizations for nutrition in Cambodia by participating in programs on the food system and nutrition to enhance Cambodia's prestige on the international stage.
Fifth, continue to expand and strengthen access to health and nutrition services through consumer education, lifestyle changes, education, water supply and sanitation, and nutrition and lifestyle changes. By improving sanitation and strengthening the food system, health system, education system and social protection system in response to climate change and rising prices for goods and food.
Sixth, continue to strengthen the governance of the food system at both the national and sub-national levels by cooperating with relevant actors to strengthen a food system that is stronger, smarter, more resilient, provides a healthier and more nutritious diet.
Seventh, continue to strengthen and build the capacity of the working group to coordinate the food security and nutrition of the capital and provinces and integrate food security and nutrition into the development plan and investment plan of the commune.
Eighth: Organize regular meetings of the Joint Technical Working Group on Food Security and Nutrition and Food Security and Nutrition Forum to share experiences and knowledge and discuss technical issues on food security and nutrition, agriculture and rural development.
9th: Participate in the World Food Safety Day on June 7 and the National Nutrition Day on November 6 every year.
10th: Prepare and implement some pilot projects related to agriculture and rural development.
