Financial experts urge young people to increase the production of financial knowledge information content so that citizens are more aware
(Phnom Penh): Financial experts urge young people with financial knowledge to create video content to spread more financial knowledge so that people, especially young people, are interested and gain knowledge related to financial technology, which makes it difficult for them. To lose any scam that leads to loss of money.
Mr. Tith Kamrong, Founder of Rithipol Company and Founder of FECA, said that financial literacy and financial technology are very important for people, especially young people. He manages his finances well and is not easily deceived.
He said that when they do not have financial knowledge, it will make them more vulnerable to fraud from some crooks through the image of investing at high interest rates, borrowing money online or other scams such as asking for a password. And so on. If he has knowledge of financial technology, they will be highly considered without being deceived.
He said that according to a survey report released by the ADB in 2018, only 18% of Cambodians are financial literate, while 85% said they have little financial knowledge.
However, through the encouragement of relevant institutions, both government and private, which have jointly disseminated financial knowledge to the people, he observed a significant increase, especially financial technology.
"I do not have data that measures what percentage of this financial literacy is growing, but we see firsthand that all parties involved have worked hard to make this work, and I think all the means that we have taken will lead to this," he said. For people to increase their knowledge of financial technology, especially young people.
He added that in order to improve this financial knowledge, in addition to creating video content competition programs, Rithip will continue training at various locations throughout the country, and Rithip recently organized curricula to be included in the curriculum at universities. Some, too.
The remarks of Dr. Chheang Vann Monin and Mr. Tith Kamrong were made at the Financial Literacy Competition (FECA) organized in order to disseminate financial knowledge to the Cambodian people more widely. A period of creative, artistic ideas to make educational messages easy to understand and applicable to people of all levels throughout Cambodia.
