Senior Minister Ly Thuch Presides Over a Regional Workshop on Promoting Innovation and Sustainability in Mine Action and UXO
(Phnom Penh): On behalf of the Prime Minister of Cambodia Hun Manet and Chairman of the Mine Authority on September 13, 2023, Dr. Ly Thuch, Senior Minister and First Vice President of the Mine Authority, opened a regional workshop on Promoting innovation and sustainability in mine action and unexploded ordnance, which took place from 12-14 September 2023, Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh.
The regional workshop was organized by the Mine Action Authority and supported by the Demining Project for Outcomes, with partners Australia, New Zealand, the Republic of Korea and UNDP, as well as the participation of Ambassadors, Embassy representatives in Cambodia, institutional representatives and delegations. Cambodia and countries in the region include Laos, the Philippines, Thailand and Vietnam.
Senior Minister Ly Thuch said that regional and global crises and conflicts over the past few years have led to an increase in the use of anti-personnel mines and an increase in landmines, as well as new challenges and risks. Both now and in the future, as well as pushing 60 states and territories to be affected by landmines and explosive remnants of war.
Despite international efforts to ban the use of landmines, landmines continue to be used in conflict situations. Asia is classified as a landmine-affected continent, and some ASEAN countries include Myanmar, Thailand, Cambodia, Laos, Vietnam, and the Philippines, which are heavily affected by landmines and explosive remnants of war.
