The purpose of this inspection was to understand the actual quality situation of the bridge, as well as to show how to use the new technical equipment to the leadership of the Ministry and relevant technical officials to strengthen and expand the capacity to maintain the bridge infrastructure throughout the country.
Prek Kdam Bridge is one of the 13 major bridges across the country that is under survey for 2023. The use of vehicles equipped with bridge surveillance equipment has made it easier and more accurate than inspecting the bottom of the bridge in the past, which can accommodate people to inspect the bottom of the bridge directly.
It should be reminded that the Prek Kdam Bridge, 981 meters long and 13.50 meters wide across the Tonle Sap River, was opened in June 2007 and completed in April 2010 at a cost of more than 28 million US dollars. The 13-year-old bridge was officially inaugurated in May 2010 under the high presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, former Prime Minister of Cambodia.
