"On the other hand, in the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone, he also raised the issue of investors, he was worried, especially the staff were worried because they read the newspaper, some information is not true. He read that he was afraid to come to work in Cambodia. ” This is what Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol said.
In an interview with reporters after the visit to the SEZs, Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol said that this issue requires cooperation between the private sector and the government to disseminate factual information and the government's measures not to To affect the feelings or fears of those who wish to invest and work in Cambodia.
The Deputy Prime Minister also revealed that the Prime Minister of Cambodia, His Excellency Hun Manet, was aware of this issue and also set up a committee to solve and disseminate explanations to wash the face of Cambodia. Mr. Sun Chanthol continued that this issue is a matter that requires the relevant authorities to solve together.
It should be noted that recently, the Cambodian authorities have received information related to online kidnappings and have cracked down on all those crimes as well. All of these issues have been reported by some foreign media as a source that leads investors as well as tourists to worry about their safety in entering Cambodia. Ministry of Interior rejects request to establish "Khmer Puppet Party"
