Minister Net Pheaktra asks the private sector to help improve the living standards of civil servants by providing low-interest loans to buy affordable housing.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Minister of Information, requested the private sector to contribute to improving the living standards of civil servants by providing low-interest loans to some affordable officials to be able to buy affordable housing. .
The request of the Minister of Information was made during a meeting with Mr. Dith Sochol, CEO of Foreign Trade Bank of Cambodia (FTB) on the afternoon of September 12, 2023 at the Ministry of Information.
On that occasion, Minister Neth Pheaktrap added: "Having support" means that civil servants who have their own house, do not rent it, is a part of living comfortably and able to work. Effectively get good results.
In response, the President and CEO of the Foreign Trade Bank of Cambodia (FTB) will jointly discuss to help civil servants of the Ministry of Information who have not yet been able to afford to buy a house through a loan with an interest rate. Low in line with monthly salary.
On this occasion, the management and staff of the Foreign Trade Bank of Cambodia FTB would like to congratulate Mr. Neth Pheaktra on his appointment as Minister of Information for the 7th legislature of the National Assembly.
Meanwhile, Minister Neth Pheaktra confirmed that the priority work to be done as the Minister of Information is to focus on modernizing institutions and modern administration to make the Ministry of Information a public relations institution of the Royal Government of Cambodia. However, to spread the truth of Cambodia to the national and international community as a timely and quality media.
