(Phnom Penh): Dr. Ken Sambath, Deputy Director General of the General Department of Taxation, urged partner commercial banks, as participants in providing tax services, to continue to pay more attention to improving tax payment services. To promote a culture of taxation and fiscal compliance in Cambodia.
This push was made on the occasion of Dr. Ken Sambath, Chairman of the Working Group to discuss the technical work of providing all types of tax collection services through commercial banks, chaired a meeting to monitor the progress and strengthen the implementation of the Memorandum of Understanding between the Ministry of Economy. And finance and partner commercial banks.
Dr. Ken Sambath stated, "The General Department of Taxation, together with partner commercial banks as contributors to the tax service, must continue to pay more attention to improving tax services to improve "Tax culture and fiscal compliance in Cambodia to increase revenue into the national budget."
Dr. Deputy Director General said that in the new turning point of deep reform and stand on the spirit of proactive in the implementation of high responsibility under the leadership of Minister Kong Vibol with the close cooperation of partner commercial banks. The fiscal administration has been modernized, good governance and good governance have been strengthened.
Dr. Ken Sambath stated that tax officials are regularly strengthened and enhanced in terms of tax professionalism, both legal and legal, as well as experience in the field of international practice through the organization and management. To attend training courses, seminars, meetings, forums, conferences at home and abroad.
In addition, Dr. Ken Sambath said that this is because the General Department of Taxation clearly understands that human capital plays an important role and is the core of the success of the institution and, in particular, ensures the sustainability of the institution's growth.
Dr. Ken Sambath said that the results of tax reform in the last decade and the efficiency of providing better tax services have made the General Department of Taxation collect tax revenue in excess of the annual plan. Regularly, most of the annuals exceed two digits.
In addition, in recent years, the General Department of Taxation has become an institution that plays an important role in managing the collection of tax revenue by collecting the most revenue into the national budget. This is the additional confirmation of Dr. Ken Sambath.
(Phnom Penh): The APSARA Authority has been working for about 30 years to preserve the global value of the Angkor resort, raising the value of the local cultural heritage since UNESCO listed the Angkor site as a heritage site in 1992. There are many tasks and problems to be solved.
The Angkor site was removed from the list of endangered heritage sites in 2004 under the auspices of the ICC-Angkor Commission, co-chaired by Japan and India, and the efforts of the Royal Government of Cambodia as well as the APSARA Authority. Which is the executive body. Under this effort, Angkor Resort is continuously promoted to the world tourism market, becoming the most attractive tourism product for Cambodia.
But as tourism grows, some people have illegally settled on the land of the Angkor World Heritage Site. The presence of this illegal location threatens global prominence and destroys the scenic beauty of the region.
Hang Pov, director general of the APSARA Authority, said that there was theft in the Angkor area, which damaged the underground archeology and groundwater, which is also a source of stability for local Khmer temples. As of 2017, there are more than 500 constructions, so UNESCO wrote a letter to the Royal Government of Cambodia to address the problem of construction spread in the Angkor area to prevent affecting the global value of Angkor.
All of these are the ingenious policies of the Royal Government of Cambodia, which maintains values in the Angkor Heritage Protected Area and helps people to obtain affordable housing.
APSARA Authority remains committed to continuing its efforts to protect the heritage value of Angkor and calls for participation in the protection of this magnificent area for the nation of Cambodia as well as for global values under the slogan: "Protection of Heritage "Culture is the duty of every Cambodian child."
