India is committed to implementing a number of projects with the Ministry of Rural Development, focusing on clean water supply, training, model villages, etc.
(Phnom Penh): India is committed to further strengthening its partnership with the Ministry of Rural Development by providing assistance on rural water supply and sanitation, continuing to provide education and training in human resources, providing credit to rural people and cooperating. Experience in creating a model village with a focus on various digital public services.
On that occasion, the Minister thanked the Indian side for always providing close cooperation with Cambodia in all fields, including culture, religion, education, skills training and rural development.
The Minister also briefed the Ambassador on the Pentagon strategy of the Royal Government of Cambodia, the seventh mandate, under the leadership of His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister, which focused on job growth, equity, efficiency and sustainability to build the foundation to achieve the vision. Cambodia 2050. The key priorities of the first phase of the Pentagon strategy include: people, roads, water, electricity and digital technology.
The Minister claimed that in order to be in line with the first phase of the Pentagon strategy of the new government, the Ministry of Rural Development has prepared four priority programs:
1. Develop physical and transportation infrastructure to better expand rural roads to accelerate the provision of essential services to rural areas and boost the people's economy by transporting agricultural products and connecting rural roads everywhere that becomes rural. Integration is getting closer to the city.
2. Improve the living conditions of rural communities so that people have access to clean water, maintain sanitation, have adequate toilets and stop open defecation.
3. Diversify rural economic activities, continue to promote the rural economy by providing skills training to people so that they can engage in other occupations other than agriculture to increase daily income.
4. In connection with the strengthening of administrative support services and general affairs, the Ministry has been working to strengthen institutions at both the national and sub-national levels, especially the implementation of decentralization policies in order to be more effective and responsible in serving the people. Better and faster, more.
In response, the Ambassador of India expressed his appreciation and appreciation for the close partnership between the Government of India and the Royal Government of Cambodia in the past.
The two sides pledged to continue to work for better cooperation, especially between the two countries, to understand Cambodia's need for rural development so that the Indian government can continue to cooperate.
