The Ministry of Commerce is constantly monitoring the increase in the price of rice in the market, if it affects the livelihood of the people will intervene immediately (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): While the price of rice in more than a month has risen steadily. The past has affected the price of rice in the Cambodian market today, with a significant increase, which makes consumers in the market complain about this increase.
However, a senior official of the Ministry of Commerce pointed out that although the price of rice has risen significantly, but at a price that has not yet affected consumers, the Ministry has yet to intervene.
Oknha Kim Savuth, CEO of Khmer Food, confirmed that the current price of rice has increased slightly compared to last year, increasing by an average of about 400 riel per kilogram.
The tycoon supports the increase in the price of rice, which helps our farmers to profit because Cambodia is a country that produces for export, so the export price is good.
According to the report of the Department of Commerce in some provinces such as Siem Reap, Prey Veng, Koh Kong, Banteay Meanchey, Kratie, etc. At the beginning of September, the price of rice in these provinces increased between 100 riel to 700 riel per kilogram. According to different types of rice compared to the beginning of January 2023.
In fact, in Banteay Meanchey province, the price of jasmine rice, which was 3,200 riel per kilogram at the beginning of the year, increased to 3,500 riel in the beginning of September. Aromatic rice costs 2,800 riel to 3,000 riel per kilogram and Neang Khon rice, which used to cost 2,200 riel, has risen to 2,700 riel per kilogram, while mixed rice has risen to 2,500 riel per kilogram.
In Prey Veng province, the price of Rumduol rice at the beginning of the year was 3,500 riel, while the price of jasmine rice was 3,500 riel, while the price of jasmine rice was 3,700 riel per kilogram and the price of rice was 2,000 riel. Per kilogram.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra: "Cambodia's level of knowledge and human resources has improved, so all media outlets need to strengthen the production of quality information to serve their readers."
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Minister of Information, said that "the level of knowledge and human resources of Cambodia has improved, so all media need to strengthen the production of quality information to serve their readers and to contribute to the quality. "Cambodia's human resources through the provision of real, fast and quality information."
This is the statement of Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Minister of Information, on the morning of September 12, 2023, on the occasion that he met with Duke Sok Chamroeun, General Director of Phnom Penh Cable TV Company PPCTV and his colleagues who came to perform. Courtesy and discussion at the Ministry of Information.
The Minister of Information requested the Director General of Phnom Penh Cable TV to participate in the production of news and entertainment programs that serve the interests of understanding and ethical entertainment to the people.
At the same time, he also highlighted the strengthening of the capacity of journalists by opening training courses to improve the capacity of journalists to have a strong foundation in the production and writing of quality news articles.
Neak Oknha Sok Chamroeun, General Director of Phnom Penh Cable Company (PPCTV), confirmed his position to continue to be ready for cooperation and to continue to support the work activities of the Ministry of Information in the past and further, especially cooperation. With the National Television of Cambodia to make the broadcasting of TV in the PPCTV cable TV system with good picture and sound quality without much technical interference.
On this occasion, Duke Sok Chamroeun and the management of Phnom Penh Cable Company (PPCTV) paid tribute to Mr. Neth Pheaktra, who has just been appointed Minister of Information in the seventh mandate of the Royal Government under the leadership of Samdech Moha President Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
In response, Neak Oknha, CEO of Phnom Penh Cable Company, will cooperate with the national TV technicians to ensure that the cable TV broadcasts have a clear sound and picture, and will also be organized by the state television and Private is available next door for convenience, visitors open to Khmer channels who want to watch.
Taking this opportunity, the Minister informed about the priority work to be done as the Minister of Information going forward, focusing on modernizing institutions and modern administration to make the Ministry of Information a public relations institution of the Royal Government. What Cambodia wants to do is to spread the truth about Cambodia to the national and international community as a quality and timely media.
At the same time, it is planned to establish a National Institute of Journalism and Public Relations to train human resources to keep up with the multi-sectoral audio-visual industry, not just news writing, which journalists must learn to strengthen their capacity. Strong. Phnom Penh Mayor Joins Meeting with International Association of Mayors Using French ZOOM to Discuss Aid to Earthquake-Affected Morocco
