Siem Reap Authorities Hold Emergency Meeting to Discuss LDP Rally in Rolous Commune, Prasat Bakong District Without Permission
(Siem Reap): Mr. Nak Neron, Deputy Governor of Siem Reap Province, this morning, September 12, 2023, held an emergency meeting to discuss the case of the League for Democracy Party (LDP), which gathered four times a week to meet in Geography: Rolous Khang Lech village, Rolous commune, Prasat Bakong district, Siem Reap province, without permission or permission from local authority.
The ceremony was attended by the leaders of the relevant departments, the three forces, the district authorities involved at the Siem Reap Provincial Hall.
On that occasion, Mr. Nak Neron also highly appreciated the working group of all institutions stationed in Phnom Kulen, Thmor Choul Village, Tbeng Commune, Banteay Srei District, Siem Reap Province, a gathering place for supporters and activists from the capital-province of the Democratic Party. At the point of Mr. Khem Veasna's plantation, having well controlled all the activities of the entry and exit of those activists.
"After the 7th National Assembly election, LDP supporters and activists gathered in Rolous Khang Lech village, Rolous commune, Prasat Bakong district without seeking permission from the provincial legislature," he said. At the grassroots level, we meet four times a week. ”
"All of these activities are anarchic, causing insecurity at the local and social levels, as well as gatherings at Khem Veasna's plantations in the past," he said.
He confirmed that so far, the remaining 300 people who listened to Mr. Khem Veasna's propaganda refused to leave the 12-hectare plantation, and now the people who are staying on the plantation are also harassing. Invading people's land in the area as well.
In particular, for gatherings without the permission of the authorities, it is strictly forbidden to hold such gatherings, and if the instructions of the authorities are not followed, the law enforcement forces must follow the law.
