Koh Kong Province's Sre Ambel District Police Inspectorate Denies Allegations of Taking Money in Response to Local Illegal Gambling
(Koh Kong): Colonel Doung Vanna, police inspector of Sre Ambel district, Koh Kong province, who has just been in office for 10 days, has denied allegations that he received bribes from the owners of illegal gambling venues in return. And not cracking down on crime, gambling sites, cockfighting and online lotteries locally.
In a statement obtained by Fresh News, it was confirmed that on September 2, 2023, at 19:14, the Sre Ambel District Police Inspectorate reduced the number of intervening forces and specialized forces to ban gambling places. An illegal chicken coop in Trapeang village, Sre Ambel commune, Sre Ambel district, with the company owner not present at the location, only two employees.
Therefore, the inspection force also brought some business related materials with a budget of 1,119,000 Riels and the two employees to the inspectorate to make an education contract to stop their activities in order to promote Implement safe village, commune and sangkat policies.
On the morning of September 3, 2023, the professional force returned all the materials to the company without demanding anything. For the budget of 1,119,000 Riels, Sar Sok Kosal, a representative of the online chicken feeding company, handed over to the inspectorate to build a kitchen in the unit without any demand, with a letter handed over to the competent authorities.
District Police Inspectorate forces, professional forces and administrative forces at administrative police stations signed contracts to steal all kinds of gambling, including online chickens, etc., in 5 active locations in Sre Ambel commune.
