The joint military exercise comes as Armenia increasingly dissatisfied with what it sees as Russia's failure to act as a security guarantor in the face of escalating tensions with Azerbaijan. Armenian long-standing opposition. The Eagle Partner military exercise is small-scale, with the participation of 85 US and 175 Armenian troops, and will run until September 20.
The Armenian Defense Ministry said the exercise was aimed at strengthening the United States' ability to operate jointly in international peacekeeping missions. The United States has said Washington has been cooperating with Armenia since 2003 and considers the exercise a normal military exercise that has nothing to do with other events.
However, a Kremlin spokesman said that Armenia's decision not to engage in military exercises with Moscow-led CSTO security and to return to military exercises with the United States requires Russia to analyze. Eat a depth. Last week, Russia also summoned the Armenian ambassador to express dissatisfaction with some of the seemingly unfriendly actions that Yerevan has been carrying out.
