After the order of the Prime Minister! Stoung district police chief who robbed Tou Meas was fired while the district inspector was temporarily removed from his job at the provincial police commission.
(Kampong Thom): A police officer who was appointed as the Chief of Administrative Police Station in Samprouch Commune, Stong District, Kampong Thom Province, who had committed the robbery of Tou Meas, was fired from the National Police while the Stong District Police Inspector was fired. At the provincial police station temporarily after finding irregularities in this appointment, especially the post chief had a bad history related to the robbery case.
The search for this action took place after receiving a strict order from the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Hun Manet, on the morning of September 10, 2023, ordered General Sar Thet, General Commissioner of the National Police and Major General. Men Ly, Kampong Thom Provincial Police Commissioner, examines the appointment of a police chief in Samprouch commune, Stong district, Kampong Thom province, after it was reported that the police chief had committed a crime.
Speaking to Fresh News on the evening of September 10, a senior police officer of the National Police General Commission confirmed that "After receiving this high order, the Kampong Thom Provincial Police immediately conducted an immediate investigation and took action. The law is in force, the post chief was fired and the inspector was temporarily removed to work at the provincial police commission.
Starting from this case, Samdech Hun Sen introduced a thorough examination and evaluation of the personality of each individual before making appointments in state institutions, both civil and armed forces at the national level and Sub-national. According to the media, the man who has just been appointed as the post chief is Hong Sarom.
Sources said that the man had a bad history involved in the robbery of a gold seller in the middle of the day in Stong Market on March 8, 2015, with a total of more than 150 pieces of jewelry, a motorcycle and money. A large number, too.
Please be reminded that on March 24, 2015, the police force of Kampong Thom province investigated and broke the case of robbery of gold in Stong market, Stong district, and then arrested two suspects as the target of robbery and confiscated exhibits such as guns and motorcycles. How to commit 3 robberies. The robbery happened on March 8, 2015.
The two suspects are Hong Sarom, 40, and Mean Ren, 47, both of Chum II Village, Thnaot Chum Commune, Baray District. After arresting the suspects, the police confiscated three motorcycles, including the motorcycle of In Siphan, a female, which was stolen during the robbery, and the other two motorcycles were robbed.
