Minister of Cults and Religions Resolves Dispute Between Monks and People at Wat Sak Sampov
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chay Borin, Minister of Cult and Religion, this morning, September 10, 2023, presided over a meeting to mediate disputes, roadblocks and the demolition of fences for monks and their families at Wat Sak Sampov. With the invitation and participation of the representatives of the sub-committee of Dangkor district, the chief abbot of the pagoda, the monks, local authorities and Buddhists at the foot of the pagoda in Sak Sampov village, Sangkat Sak Sampov, Khan Dangkor, Phnom Penh.
Mr. Chay Borin stated that in accordance with the high recommendation of His Excellency Hun Manet, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, the first phase of the Pentagon Strategy for the seventh mandate has been set out for the growth of employment, equity, efficiency and sustainability in building the foundation to achieve Cambodia's vision for 2050.
In that, the Minister of Cults and Religions listened to the orders of the monks and the people in the clarification and some requests of the monks and the people.
The Minister also asked the local authorities, led by the Deputy Governor of Dangkor District, to clarify the above disputes in order to better understand the disputes in order to resolve them in a targeted and transparent manner.
Through this, the Minister accepted the requests and suggestions to be considered in a transparent, fair and effective manner for both the people and the monks not to lose the interests of both parties, especially the property of the pagoda, which is the place of obedience of the people in Basic.
The Minister asked the people to be open-minded in accepting the solution, considering that we, the same Cambodian Buddhists, live in the same community, solve it together effectively and smoothly. As a result, he pointed out that both parties should accept the solution as agreed in the minutes of the meeting.
Mr. Chay Borin stated that the dispute will be resolved peacefully only with the participation of both parties, and if there is no agreement between the two parties, he will stand by the legal authorities and local authorities. Practical legal letter in settlement. Therefore, he still hopes that the dispute will be resolved peacefully and with the consent of both parties.
