US Secretary of Commerce Gina Raimondo said on Tuesday she did not expect any changes to US tariffs on Chinese imports until the US Trade Representative Office completed its review. .
Former US President Donald Trump lifted tariffs in 2018 and 2019 on thousands of goods worth about $ 370 billion from China at the time, after an investigation under Article 301 found that China had Is using US intellectual property unfairly and dishonestly and forcing US companies to transfer sensitive technology to do business in China.
Tariffs currently range from 7.5 percent on a wide range of consumer goods to 25 percent on vehicles, industrial equipment, electronics and other electronics. Among the main types of goods that escaped duty were mobile phones, laptops and video game consoles.
To remove tariffs on goods imported from China, the Trump administration used Article 301 of the 1974 Trade Law, which aims to combat the unfair practices of trading partners. According to Reuters.
