Minister Tho Chetha Inspects Water Condition and Irrigation System in Siem Reap and Kampong Thom Provinces
(Siem Reap): Mr. Tho Chetha, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, accompanied by Permanent Secretary of State, Secretary of State, Under Secretary of State, Director of the Cabinet, Director of the Department and professional officers, on the morning of September 9, 2023, inspected the water situation and met with the farming community. Water at Makak Irrigation System, located in Chi Kreng District, Siem Reap Province.
On that occasion, the Minister and his team, with the participation of Deputy Provincial Governor, Chi Kreng District Governor and Commune Chief, met with 35 people from three water user farmers' communities, including Makak community, Area 1 community and local community. 2. After that, the Minister and his team inspected the dams and the potential of the reservoir and canal system for irrigation.
The Minister instructed to continue to strengthen the existing water farmers 'communities and requested all water farmers' communities to continue to help maintain the existing achievements so that they can be used for a long time in the future.
In the afternoon of the same day, the Minister also continued to inspect the water condition and inspect the Tang Krasang irrigation system in Santuk district, Kampong Thom province.
Deputy Prime Minister Hang Chuon Naron: Eight core priorities set out will help improve education reform
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, stated that the eight core priorities set by His Majesty the King Hun Manet and the Ministry of Education will be the driving force for the education sector in Cambodia in the new mandate. Improved.
He said this on the occasion of his speech on the priority of education, youth and sports reform of the Royal Government of the 7th legislature under the leadership of His Majesty Hun Manet on the morning of September 9, 2023.
