The Ministry of Agriculture announces the postponement of the entrance examination within the Ministry for 2023
The following is the announcement of the Ministry of Agriculture: Business Awareness: Businessmen suggest that at a time when the world is experiencing food shortages, it is an opportunity for the rich to invest in agro-industry.
(Phnom Penh): Two well-known businessmen in Cambodia said that those with large investment capital should look for investment opportunities in the agro-industrial sector in Cambodia to produce and process agricultural products for domestic supply and export while the world He is having food problems.
A well-known businesswoman, Oknha Keo Mom, President of Cambodian Entrepreneurship, spoke in support of and encouraged those who have a lot of capital or investors who have real skills related to agriculture to examine the possibility of investing in this sector, because this situation may be the time. Which is best to start investing at a time when the world is short of food. Therefore, investing in agricultural crops is a right and good investment.
She noted that although Cambodia is an agricultural country, it is on a small scale that can not compete with them.
She added that Cambodia is a country with favorable conditions and potential for agriculture because the land is of good quality, fertile and free from major natural disasters, which provides opportunities for investment in agro-industrial crops. At the same time, a number of Cambodian agricultural products are considered to be of high quality, such as rice ranked No. 1, cashew No. 1, pepper and many other agricultural products that we can compete in the world market.
Neak Oknha Lim Heng, Vice President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, said that in this situation, it is an opportunity for local investors to turn to investing in agriculture as the Royal Government in this mandate sets out policies to support the economy. After Kovid 19, focusing on agriculture and established the Fourth Special Economic Pole in the Northwest.
He observed that in the past, investors were more interested in the real estate sector. However, when the real estate sector is not doing well, if the capitalists can turn to agricultural investment opportunities, it is a good opportunity to contribute to the national economic growth through agriculture.
He emphasized that through free trade agreements such as agreements with China, Korea, the United Arab Emirates, as well as the RCEP agreement, it would boost Cambodia's exports, while those countries also have demand for Cambodian agricultural products.
