Singapore was a commercial port of the Champa Empire from the beginning. When the Cham people were influenced by Hinduism from Indian businessmen from the 4th century, Singapore became a center of Hinduism and became the capital of Champa Empire from the 4th-8th centuries.
Businessmen from China, Cambodia, Vietnam, India, Persia, Arabia, etc. trade in and out of this Singapore international port. By colonial times, although much of Champa was under the control of the Annamite Empire, Singapore remained an important international trading port for traders from parts of the world.
