Please be reminded that Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet pointed out 6 priority tasks to the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training to be implemented effectively in 2023, including
First, try to facilitate the discussion of the minimum wage well based on the scientific characteristics and criteria set out in the law on the minimum wage before the upcoming Pchum Ben holiday.
Second: Prepare urgent legal documents to prepare for the implementation of the social security system for voluntary health care for those in charge of the members of the Social Welfare Party. To help ease the burden of health care costs for workers and their families quickly and to be widely disseminated to workers, as well as to create a convenient mechanism for workers to participate in this program.
Third, to launch vocational training programs for approximately 1.5 million young people from poor and vulnerable families across the country, and to coordinate with stakeholders to allow workers to learn vocational skills. Also, to increase productivity and efficiency in the workplace by organizing training courses at night or on weekends.
Fourth, to promote the full implementation of apprenticeship obligations in accordance with the Labor Law, including internships, internships, skills development and skills reorganization, encouraging the private sector to participate in the training of workers and provide Additional training for working workers to improve their skills, productivity and affordability.
Fifth, pay attention to the implementation of cash support programs for pregnant women, both before, during and after childbirth, better and more convenient. Also ensure that pregnant women and people with disabilities leave work 15 minutes early.
And 6: Establish a competition program on the theme of workplace harmony to turn an enterprise into a peaceful community from 2024 onwards.
Second, cooperate with stakeholders to promote the improvement of the dining area or canteen in the factory that is operating in a way that is suitable for the workers and requires the preparation of the canteen or canteen for the new factory to be established.
Third, cooperate with stakeholders to study mechanisms to support and encourage the gradual change of means of transportation of workers in accordance with technical standards and more comfortable by 2027.
And 4: Promote the skills recognition test program, which is an opportunity for both domestic and foreign workers to have a skills certification certificate to demonstrate their abilities and skill levels.
