According to a release from the Japanese Ministry of Foreign Affairs, during the meeting, Prime Minister Kishida congratulated Prime Minister Hun Manet on receiving the support of the people and the National Assembly to lead the new government.
The Prime Minister of Japan also expressed his willingness to work more closely with the Prime Minister to strengthen the "comprehensive strategic partnership", which was launched in 2023.
In addition to strengthening bilateral relations, the Japanese Prime Minister also wants to work closely with President Hun Manet to maintain and strengthen freedom and openness of international order based on international law.
During the meeting, Prime Minister Kishida expressed Japan's willingness to strengthen security cooperation through dialogue between the Japanese Self-Defense Forces and the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, including a visit by the Japanese Self-Defense Forces to a naval base. Ream and so on.
Mr. Kishida also expressed Japan's willingness to continue to cooperate for the economic and social development of Cambodia, especially in the digital sector, where Cambodia is currently using Japanese technology.
The Japanese Prime Minister said that Japan will continue to support the development of Cambodia's democracy.
In response, President Hun Manet thanked and thanked Japan for its contribution to Cambodia's peace, as well as Cambodia's reconstruction and economic development.
Regarding security issues, the Prime Minister emphasized that the security sector is an important part of bilateral cooperation. He affirmed that he would develop this cooperation not only with the Japanese Self-Defense Forces, but also with the Japanese Self-Defense Forces, and that Cambodia would continue to open the Ream Sea port to welcome Japan.
He also expressed his willingness to continue cooperating with Japan in various fields, including the digital sector, which the Cambodian government is focusing on.
The two leaders also agreed to work more closely on regional and international issues, including tackling the missile and nuclear weapons programs.
According to the Japanese Ministry of Foreign Affairs, during the meeting, Prime Minister Kishida mentioned the recently announced "ASEAN-Japan Comprehensive Integration Initiative" and hoped that the new vision would work. More comprehensive cooperation on the occasion of the 50th anniversary of ASEAN-Japan friendly relations in December 2023.
Driving across the spill dam accidentally turned off the engine and was hit by a whirlpool in Oddar Meanchey province, no one was injured
(Oddar Meanchey): A car was swept down the road while driving through a spillway with high water flow. This case happened on September 7, 2023 in Tumnup Thmey village, Trapeang Tao commune, Anlong Veng district, Oddar Meanchey province.
Colonel Su Nou, Anlong Veng district police chief, said that prior to the incident, a Star Rich water truck was crossing a 300-meter-long spillway in a north-south direction where the water level was rising. 50 meters above the back of the dam, while the car was driving across the dam, the engine suddenly turned off, causing the car wash water to fall from the dam, with two car owners and their spouses getting off without any danger.
Anlong Veng District Inspector confirmed that the driver of the car was Him Meng Hour, 24 years old, and his wife was Rith Srina, 21 years old. Holy.
