This morning, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet continued to visit nearly 20,000 workers in Kampong Speu province
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Saturday, September 9, 2023, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, continued to meet with a total of 18,265 workers. From various factories in Kampong Speu province.
Dr. Heng Sour, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, said that the workers who participated in the ceremony tomorrow from 14 factories. These 14 factories have 3 garment factories, 7 travel products and bags, 2 sewing shoes, 1 garment printing and 1 electronics factory.
According to Dr. Heng Sour, among the workers who participated in the ceremony, there were 638 pregnant workers.
According to the Minister of Alumni from Japan, Kampong Speu currently has more than 150,000 workers, earning a total of 470 million US dollars a year in 385 factories. . Of these, 191 garment factories employ a total of 140,000 workers, earning more than $ 430 million a year.
Mr. Heng Sour said that Kampong Speu is the second most developed province after Phnom Penh. Currently, Kampong Speu province also has a high demand for labor. As of September 6, the province needs about 4,000 workers.
Samdech President Hun Manet has already met with workers twice. The first one was held on August 29 in Prey Speu area, Phnom Penh, with 18,013 workers participating. The second time was held on September 1, 2023 in Takhmao City, Kandal Province, with 18,289 workers participating.
In the last two meetings, His Excellency Hun Manet presented the policy of the Royal Government in the new legislature, especially the Pentagon strategy - the first phase, which is a strategy to focus on job growth and improve people's lives. Citizens for the better.
The issuance of the order came shortly after the Prime Minister received a request from three ministries through the Ministry of Public Works to prepare for the 2023 civil service examination procedure.
Through this voicemail, His Excellency Hun Manet said:
"Since the recruitment of civil servants is an important task related to the reform of our public functions in the new mandate, I would like to suspend the recruitment of civil servants in the remaining 2023 plans for later preparation.
