Minister Tho Chetha Inspects Water and Irrigation Situation in Pursat and Battambang Provinces
(Battambang): Mr. Tho Chetha, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, accompanied by the Permanent Secretary of State, Secretary of State, Undersecretary of State, Director of the Cabinet, Director of the Department and professional officers, on September 8, 2023, inspected the water and irrigation conditions at two locations: The first is in Pursat province and the second is in Battambang province.
In the morning, the Minister inspected the water condition and had a face-to-face meeting with the community of farmers using water at Damnak Ampil Irrigation System in Bakan District, Pursat Province. The Minister instructed the farming community to take care of the existing achievements and supported the Pursat Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology's proposal for the Damnak Ampil Irrigation and Dam Project.
Please be informed that Damnak Ampil Irrigation System is a complete irrigation system capable of supplying irrigation water to about 27,000 hectares of wet paddy and 9,000 hectares of dry paddy. Damnak Ampil Irrigation System has the potential to provide a source of water for the rainy season to nearly 40,000 farmers.
In the afternoon, Minister Tho Chetha continued to inspect the Dontry Dam in Rukkiri District, Battambang Province, a project that received a concessional loan from the Republic of Korea. The construction company also informed the Minister and the working group that the progress of the construction of the Dountry Dam has reached 71% so far and is scheduled to be completed by the end of 2025.
