(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chhay Rithi Sen, Minister of Rural Development, announced the strategy of four priority programs to support the policy of further development of rural areas and encourage civil servants at all levels under the Ministry of Rural Development as well. The directors of the 25 capital-provincial rural development departments participated effectively.
The launch of these priority strategies during the Minister's meeting with the leaders of the Ministry, leaders and civil servants at all levels in the units under the Ministry and the Director of the 25 Departments of Rural Development on the morning of September 8, 2023 At the Ministry.
The Minister expressed his appreciation and appreciation for the efforts of the management and subordinates, as well as congratulations on the achievements made in the past legislation in improving the quality and value of living. Of rural people with economic, social and cultural conditions.
On that occasion, he stated that in the 7th legislature of the National Assembly, based on the above vision, the Ministry of Rural Development will continue to strive to build new achievements by setting out strategies as four priority programs to support rural development policies. Further progress as follows:
Program 1: Development of physical infrastructure and cellular communication, ensuring integrated rural areas and to promote the arteries of economic growth to rural areas.
Program 2: Improve the living conditions of rural communities in order for rural people to live in a good, healthy and hygienic manner and comfortable.
Program 3: Diversify rural economic activities through basic skills training to create jobs and employment with the aim of increasing household income in rural areas.
Program 4: Strengthen administrative support services and general affairs to strengthen institutions to serve rural people with integrity and high responsibility.
