(Phnom Penh): On the evening of September 7, 2023, Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Minister of Information, High Representative of the Royal Government of Cambodia, attended the celebration of the 75th Anniversary of the Establishment of the Democratic People's Republic of Korea (DPRK) organized by Mr. Jan Yun Gon, Ambassador of the Democratic People's Republic of Korea to Cambodia at the Cambodiana Hotel.
The ceremony was also attended by senior ministers, ministers, secretaries of state, undersecretaries of state, government leaders, diplomats in Cambodia.
Cambodia will always remember the difficult times of the past when King Norodom Sihanouk received the warmest and warmest welcome from the great leader Kim Il Sung during his stay in Pyongyang. And the relationship between Cambodia and the Democratic People's Republic of Korea has steadily strengthened and linked traditional ties and good cooperation.
In addition, Mr. Pheaktra added that next year is the 60th anniversary of our diplomatic relations (December 20, 1964 - December 20, 2024), he hoped that Cambodia and the Democratic People's Republic of Korea will continue to maintain friendly relations and promote Strengthen good bilateral and multilateral cooperation for the common benefit of our two peoples under the umbrella of peace, stability and common prosperity in the region.
Finally, Minister Net Pheaktra wished Kim Jong Un, Leader of the Democratic People's Republic of Korea, good health and long life.
