BEIJING, Sept. 7 (Xinhua) - A Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesman answered a reporter's question on US unreasonable accusations against China at the East Asia Summit.
At the East Asia Summit on September 7, the US envoy made unreasonable accusations against China over the Taiwan and South China Sea issues, the media reported. How does China respond to this?
A Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesman said the US envoy had ignored the facts and made unreasonable allegations against China. For the US side.
The spokesman stressed that the Taiwan issue is purely an internal affair of China, which does not allow outside interference. The separatist activities of the separatist forces that want "Taiwan independence" and the indulgence by external forces are the biggest threat to the peace of the Taiwan Straits.
Analysis: Destroying the reputation of others can not only improve itself, China can only develop the world to another level of prosperity.
BEIJING, Sept. 6 (Xinhua) - The China International Services Trade Fair 2023 closed in Beijing on September 6. Over the past five days, countless products of all kinds, crowds and remarkable business data have shown real confidence.
At the same time, the certainty of China's policy of relentless expansion has boosted the confidence of foreign traders to do business in China. China has basically eased restrictions on allowing foreign capital to enter China's manufacturing industry, and is opening up to all aspects and orderly service industries.
