(Siem Reap): Police from Prasat Bakong District Police Inspectorate in Siem Reap Province arrested three suspects in connection with a case of violence against others by riding a motorcycle, beating and kicking the victim's motorcycle, causing him to fall and injure himself.
According to the report of Prasat Bakong District Police Inspectorate obtained by Fresh News on September 08, 2023, on the night of September 3, 2023, along National Road 6 in Ta Trav village, Kantraing commune, Prasat district Bakong, Siem Reap Province A group of five victims rode two motorbikes from a movie theater in Siem Reap City to return home in Prasat Bakong District.
After receiving information and complaints from the victims, on September 4, 2023, the local police force cooperated with the police of the Serious Crimes Police to open an investigation and arrest 3 suspects. People were brought for questioning at the Prasat Bakong District Police Inspectorate.
The first suspect: Ley Samnang, 21 years old, blacksmith, place of birth and current address: Kantraing village, Kantraing commune, Prasat Bakong district, Second: Chung Sith, 15 years old, Occupation (None) Kantraing, Prasat Bakong district, Siem Reap province;
After questioning, the suspects confessed that they had committed the crime, with Khean Thai, 22, a motorcyclist, Chung Sith, 15, sitting in the middle, and Ley Samnang, 21. Chhnang, who was sitting in the back, attacked Rith Toei with one hand and removed the spare belt, but the victim fled on a motorcycle to the bridge. The reason is that the suspect was angry with the victim, who was driving a motorcycle with a flashlight.
According to the victims' complaints and with the guidance of Major General Teng Channath, Siem Reap Provincial Police Commissioner and Deputy Commissioner for Criminal Planning, the specialized force prepared a case file and sent the suspects and exhibits to the Serious Crime Police Office for transfer. Proceed to court proceedings.
Interior Ministry spokesman: 115 people arrested for criminal and drug offenses on September 7 yesterday
