The Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia has licensed 30 companies to conduct joint venture projects.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sou Socheat, Delegate of the Royal Government in Charge of the Director General of the Securities Regulator of Cambodia, on September 08, 2023, presided over a workshop on "Public Dissemination on the Implementation of the Prakas on Issuance of fund units of joint ventures at the Office of the Non-Banking Financial Services Authority.
He said that the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia has launched another financial instrument called the Joint Venture Fund through the official implementation of the Prakas on the Issuance of Joint Venture Units dated July 20, 2023 ago, in which the terms and conditions of the issuance of the fund unit of the joint investment project and the operation of the fund after the issuance.
The Director General stated that the publication of fund units of investment projects allows fund management companies to create investment projects to raise funds or cash from joint ventures to invest in defined projects and distribute profits or benefits back to investors. Rejoined.
In addition, he said that to date, the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia has issued licenses, permits and / or recognition to companies operating in joint ventures, about 30 companies, including: fund management companies, maintenance companies. Assets on behalf of the distributor, repurchase or repayment companies and fund managers are key players in this joint venture market.
In order to develop the market and promote the securities sector of Cambodia, the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia not only conducts research, develops new regulations and financial products, but also disseminates and disseminates a broad and in-depth public awareness. Also for the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia to attract and receive investment from the public and investors on the securities market in Cambodia.
This statement was made by the President of the National Assembly of Korea during a working meeting with Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, Acting Head of State of Cambodia. The meeting took place on the morning of September 8, 2023 at the Senate.
On that occasion, Mr. Kim Jin-poo hoped that this bridge will contribute to the development of Cambodia and a symbol of Cambodia-Korea friendship. The two countries will continue to expand cooperation to attract Korean companies to invest in Cambodia and continue to expand in various fields, and strong cooperation between the two countries will contribute to peace, stability and development in ASEAN. Like the Mekong region.
At the same time, the President of the Korean National Assembly reaffirmed the intention of the Government and the Korean Parliament to further strengthen good relations and cooperation with Cambodia, considering Cambodia as an important partner in the ASEAN-Korea framework and an important ODA partner. . To achieve these goals, the two countries must deepen relations and operations through exchanges of visits between the leaders of the two countries.
At the same time, Mr. Kim Jin-poo thanked Cambodia for supporting the Republic of Korea to host the 2030 World Expo in Busan. Cambodia is the first country in ASEAN to support the Republic of Korea, and the decision to host the World Expo will take place in the first week of November this year.
In response, Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, Acting Head of State, expressed his satisfaction by seeing the relationship between the two countries continue to grow. This progress is reflected in people-to-people exchanges, mutual support for international cooperation aimed at contributing to peace, security, stability, regional and global development.
The presentation of the position to continue to help develop Cambodia, as Korea has done many times, was made during a courtesy meeting and work discussion between Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Chairman of the Supreme Council of the King and President of the Cambodian People's Party. With Mr. Kim Jin Pyu at the Palace of January 7 this morning, Friday, September 8, 2023.
According to a press release issued by the Cambodian People's Party, Samdech Techo Hun Sen warmly welcomed Kim Jin-poo, an old friend, during his first official visit as Speaker of the National Assembly of the Republic of Cambodia. Korea.
As the founder of the resumption of Cambodia-Korea relations in 1997, Samdech Techo thanked the National Assembly, the Government and the people of Korea, especially Kim Jin-poo, for his contribution to the launch of the Development Cooperation Project. Economy through EDCF concessional lending since 2001.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also mentioned the historically good relations and thanked the Republic of Korea for helping Cambodia in difficult times, including socio-economic recovery after a long civil war. Road infrastructure, special technical training school, Cambodia-Korea Friendship Bridge, planned to be built across the Tonle Sap and Mekong rivers, a symbol of great unity.
The President of the National Assembly praised Samdech Techo for his wise diplomatic leadership and requested Samdech Techo to continue to think about lasting peace in the region and the world.
