Trade officials and exporters claim that Cambodia has high potential to export 250,000 tons of rice per year to Indonesia
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia has agreed to supply about 250,000 tons of rice per year to Indonesia to maintain food security and consumption in this country.
Both Ministry of Commerce officials and rice exporters believe that Cambodia has the potential to achieve 250,000 tonnes of rice exports per year to Indonesia.
Speaking to Fresh News on the afternoon of September 8, 2023, Mr. Pen Sovicheat, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Commerce, confirmed that the companies of the two countries and stakeholders have discussed rice exports, so the productivity of The export of 250,000 tons to Indonesia, Cambodia could be done if we had already signed an agreement with Indonesia in the near future.
He said that of the 250,000 tonnes exported, it was not certain that it would be exported, as the quantification was a sign of a trade agreement, but the actual price negotiations depended on market conditions. .
Mr. Pen Sovichet stated, "As for the actual possibilities based on the production based on the capabilities of the rice mill, the current procurement, so the exporters believe that they will make every effort to export in full."
Oknha Song Saran, chairman of the board of the Cambodian Rice Federation and chairman of the rice exporter Amru Rice, said that Cambodia has enough rice to export to Indonesia 250,000 tons per year without shortage.
"Cambodia's export of 250,000 tonnes of rice a year to Indonesia is not a concern because Cambodia has enough rice, but what matters is the price we are concerned about," he said. "Prices are likely to fluctuate in other countries, such as Pakistan or Burma."
He said that if the rice exports were carried out in accordance with the set terms and conditions, plus the price did not change, the export of 250,000 tons to Indonesia could be achieved without any obstacles.
Indonesian President Joko Widodo has expressed satisfaction that Cambodia has agreed to supply 250,000 tonnes of rice a year to Indonesia. At the same time, Indonesia will support Cambodia's food security program through the supply of agricultural fertilizers.
The agreement to import 250,000 tonnes of rice a year from Cambodia comes after India stopped exporting rice to Indonesia. Indonesia initially planned to import 1 million tonnes of rice from India, but the proposal was rejected.
Senior officials of the Ministry of Education call for continued attention to the literacy work that is the foundation of education
(Preah Vihear): Mr. Nou Sles, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, called on relevant institutions, national and international organizations, community development partners and all citizens to pay more attention to literacy as well as education in Systematic and informal in the spirit to continue to contribute to the promotion of literacy in Cambodia to be even better.
Mr. Nou Sles made this call on the morning of September 8, 2023, on the occasion of his visit to represent Mr. Hang Chuon Naron, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Education, Youth and Sports on the 23rd National Literacy Day, September 8, which was celebrated. Held under the theme "Basic Literacy of Entrepreneurship and Socio-Economics" in Sihanoukville.
The event was also attended by Mr. Prak Sovann, Chairman of Preah Vihear Provincial Council, Mr. Kim Rithy, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, as well as the accompanying delegates and Deputy Governors, Heads of Departments around the province, teachers and students. Crowds.
Mr. Kim Rithy, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, said that on behalf of the Provincial Council, he would like to express his great pleasure and warmly welcome the presence of Mr. Nou Sles, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and the accompanying delegation. Join this event in Preah Vihear province.
Mr. Nou Sles read out the message of the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Mani Hun Manet, on the occasion of the National Literacy Day 2023, that the Royal Government has been continuing its historically great mission with a strong commitment to serve the people and accelerate development. Socio-economic will promote the implementation of deeper and more comprehensive reforms in all areas.
The Secretary of State stated that this year's theme emphasizes the importance of promoting literacy in all its forms and providing renewed opportunities for students, especially those with a weak economy, the disadvantaged, the poor, children, youth and ethnic groups. Indigenous peoples to be able to read, write, calculate and solve some problems in life better.
The message goes on to say that literacy is, of course, the foundation of knowledge and education that enables everyone to understand common types of information and gain new knowledge, as well as increase opportunities for improving the quality of life. And as a foundation of lifelong learning.
He also called on relevant institutions, national and international organizations, community development partners and all citizens to continue to pay more attention to literacy as well as all formal and informal education in this spirit. To continue to contribute to the promotion of literacy in Cambodia to be even better.
Kampong Cham Provincial Governor Holds a Discussion Meeting Before Signing a Contract Between Cintri Company and Kampong Cham Municipal Administration Representative to Clean and Collect Garbage
