Singapore to send 22 ambulances to Ukraine in response to humanitarian crisis
SINGAPORE, Sept. 7 (Xinhua) - Singapore will send a humanitarian aid package of 22 ambulances to Ukraine, the Foreign Ministry said on Tuesday. This is according to the release by the CNA news agency on Thursday, September 7, 2023.
The ministry added that the aid was made in response to Ukraine's request to support international efforts to resolve the country's humanitarian crisis.
The last time Singapore sent aid to Ukraine was in June 2022. The aid package included nine ambulances, two fire engines, a variety of firefighting equipment, first aid kits, mine detectors and medical supplies.
In April last year, the Singapore Red Cross also donated a third donation of S $ 3.66 million to support Ukrainian refugees. And in December 2022, the Singapore Red Cross further supported the construction of 10 modular houses to help communities in Ukraine facing a severe winter.
