(Phnom Penh): The Criminal Police Department of the General Commission of the National Police on September 7, 2023, came out to completely reject the false information shared on Facebook regarding the implementation of the duties and responsibilities of professional forces to maintain law and order. And avoid the use of violence.
The following is the full text of the Criminal Police Department:
"The Information and Quick Reaction Team of the Criminal Police Department is honored to inform the media and the public that: At 9 pm on August 17, 2023, the Criminal Police Department received information from the people in case of attempted use of an act. Violent and armed at Borey Niroth Meanchey, Ta Ngov Village, Sangkat Niroth, Khan Chbar Ampov, Phnom Penh.
After receiving this information, the specialized force of the Criminal Police Department, which is working at the local level, especially monitoring the fugitives from the Siem Reap Provincial Prison, went to the scene to coordinate the intervention to avoid any possible violence. There is up.
At the scene, the victim claimed that Srey Meas Chantara, a male, had insulted and attempted to use violence against the other party, Nang Srey Mech and Kuy Kim Thea. Not wanting to get into an argument, Nang Srey Mech and Kuy Kim Thea drove home from the scene and suddenly Meas Srey Chantara drove to their house at Borey Peng Huoth, Boeung Snor.
When the specialized force arrived and reported and cooperated with the locals to the scene, the police arrested both parties who were fighting and the police stopped both parties from arguing, but Meas Srey Chantara and his family Insulting the authorities, "Come to the other side." We then explained to him that they should coordinate to go home separately.
As mentioned above, the Criminal Police Department would like to completely reject the false information shared on social media that the Criminal Police Department forces go to one side and use violence against the other party. "This accusation has seriously damaged the reputation of the law enforcement forces, which are performing their legal duties."
