Police Arrest 3 Suspects in Beheading Case in Por Sen Chey District
(Phnom Penh): The criminal police force of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police in cooperation with the police force of Po Sen Chey district investigated and arrested three gangsters from two factions who started a fight and cut a guard, causing serious injuries in Trapeang Thleung 3 village, Sangkat Choam Chao I, Khan Por Sen Chey.
The incident happened at 2:30 AM on September 7, 2023 in Trapeang Thleung 3 Village, Sangkat Choam Chao I, Khan Por Sen Chey.
Prior to the incident, two groups of suspects had been drinking and then arguing with each other. There is a conflict with each other. While cutting and fighting, the perpetrators cut each other, causing the left finger to be amputated, three fingers to be amputated.
The suspects then tried to escape and took their accomplices to the rescue and treatment. At that time, the village guards who were the victims intervened and arrested the suspects, but the suspects acted with a machete. The victim was seriously injured.
Lt. Col. Leng Veasna confirmed that the three suspects are: First: Sok Chhlang, male, 18 years old, living in Thmor Koul 1 village, Sangkat Choam Chao, second: Hun Samnang, male, 18 years old, occupation: Real address: Thmor Koul village, Sangkat Choam Chao II and 3rd: Name: Chea Tola, Male, 18 years old, Occupation: Uncertain, Residence: Thmor Koul village, Sangkat Choam Chao II.
The victim, Thon Raksmey, male, 35 years old, resident of Trapeang Thleung 3 village, Sangkat Choam Chao I, was injured in the left chest, 1 knife in the back and 1 knife in the left finger and was hospitalized.
The three suspects are currently being held for questioning at the Po Sen Chey District Police Inspectorate to prepare for the procedure to be sent to court for legal action.
