The Minister of Rural Development makes some recommendations to officials under the Department of Administration and Personnel and the Department of Training and Research
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chhay Rithi Sen, Minister of Rural Development, on September 7, 2023, met with leaders and civil servants of the Department of Administration and Personnel and the Department of Training and Research at the Ministry of Rural Development.
On that occasion, Mr. Phal Sok Samnang, Director of the Department of Administration and Personnel and Mr. Dy Sarath, Director of the Department of Training and Research reported on the progress and achievements of the two departments for the first half of 2023 on Personnel Administration and Research. The human resource development work that has achieved results should be a source of pride.
With this, the Minister expressed his appreciation and appreciation for the efforts of the management and professional officers of both departments who fulfill their duties in improving the efficiency of work, capacity building of civil servants and basic skills training necessary for the people. People in rural areas.
In response to the leaders' issues and requests, the Minister agreed with the leaders in charge and provided recommendations, guidance and advice to the leaders in charge and Civil servants under the supervision of both departments:
1. The Department of Administration and Personnel must strengthen and promote the flow of documents in a timely and prompt manner, especially the minutes of the meeting must be completed no later than one day after the meeting.
2. The storytelling schedule is prepared by consulting all the leaders in charge and has one day for each leader.
3. The Department of Administration and Personnel must prepare a unified form of minutes of meetings and clear reports so that the units under the Ministry can easily implement the summary.
4. The Department of Training and Research shall organize the training work in a package, starting from the training of basic skills, job creation, career orientation, monitoring and evaluation of the beneficiaries who have been trained to ensure that the training has helped To join the poverty alleviation card.
5. Strengthen advertising, including print, digital media, and promotional video production.
6. Need to update training programs for the development of civil servants and the training of new basic skills to the people, especially mobile skills training.
7. Arrange for the awarding of medals and equipments at the annual general meeting of the Ministry to retired civil servants.
8. The management and officials of both departments must adhere to the rules and regulations of the system, set the regular monitoring and inspection monthly, quarterly and semi-regular meetings and must report and ask for advice in a timely manner.
9. Strengthen internal unity to work more effectively by paying attention to the well-being of sick and disabled civil servants, especially pregnant civil servants through encouragement and favorable working hours. .
10. Both departments must prepare a report on the achievements of the department for the meeting to summarize the work results for 2023 and the work direction for the next year, which is scheduled to be held on December 22, 2023.
