An active thief was cracked down on in Prasat village, Por Reach commune, Svay Chrum district
(Svay Rieng): An active thief was chased by the police of Svay Chrum district in Prasat village, Por Reach commune, Svay Chrum district, Svay Rieng province, on the afternoon of September 5, 2023, under the act of stealing people's property.
According to the source, at 2:30 pm on September 5, 2023, at Prasat village, Por Reach commune, Svay Chrum district, two thieves on a motorcycle broke into the house of Neang Sovisal, male, 40 years old, ethnic Khmer Occupation Teacher. When the thieves acted, the villagers saw the thieves and shouted and arrested one person named Pov Vayu to the Por Reach Administrative Police Station for questioning.
In front of the police, the suspect confessed that he had another party member named Yang Poeun and that he had ridden a motorbike to steal the property of an unknown person in Prasat village, Por Reach commune, Svay Chrum district twice. .
Police added that the seized items included a Viva motorcycle without a license plate, a solar lamp and some locks. The suspect is currently being held at the Svay Chrum District Police Inspectorate for legal action.
General knowledge: Which colony came to Asia first?
(Phnom Penh): Many events have taken place in the history of the world, including the event that the European powers colonized the kingdoms in Asia is also an important historical turning point, but do you know which colonies? Who arrived in Asia first?
In 1498, the Portuguese navy invaded the Indian state of Goa and crossed the Indian Ocean into Southeast Asia to invade the Malacca peninsula in 1511 AD. Portuguese troops also continued to travel across the South China Sea to the southern shores of the Great Meng to seize Macau in 1557 AD.
In 1565, the Spanish Empire raised a navy to conquer the Cebu Empire and later established the capital Manila in 1571 under Portuguese rule.
Meanwhile, French troops arrived in Indochina in 1858 and colonized the Kingdom of Cambodia, the Kingdom of Tonkin, the Kingdom of Annam, and the territory of Kampuchea Krom, Vientiane, Laos, and part of China.
