Authorities continue to inspect the "Miss Ex" entertainment club in Daun Penh district after frequent incidents disrupted people's lives, after inspecting the owner of the location without a business license
(Phnom Penh): As pointed out by Mr. Chea Khema, Governor of Daun Penh District, on the night of September 6, 2023, Mr. Chap Dina, Deputy Governor of Daun Penh District, led the Khan Administrative Unity Command to inspect the Miss Ex Club to check the law. Business and guide the owner of the location related to security, order and public order.
According to the investigation, Miss Ex Club does not have a license to open a club business. This is the second visit to the site and the first visit was made on September 1, 2013. The team recently advised the site owner:
1: Must be organized, orderly, hygienic, clean and proper environment can not be used as a parking lot for motorcycles. 2. Business must have a business license. 3: Do not make loud noises to disturb neighbors. Absolutely. 4: Prohibit sexual services. 5: In case the location owner does not follow the above instructions, the location owner will be responsible before the law.
On behalf of Daun Penh District Administration, Mr. Chap Dina, Deputy Governor of Daun Penh District, requested the people to provide information through the Daun Penh District Administration Pack or by calling 017 884 888,081 368 999, 088 2333339 to facilitate your work.
