The following is a message from the President of the European Council: The Deputy Governor of Preah Vihear Province recommends inspiring people to build and use latrines so that Preah Vihear Province can become a province by the end of open defecation by 2025
(Preah Vihear): Mr. Ouk Kem San, Deputy Governor of Preah Vihear Province, called on local authorities and all stakeholders to disseminate to local people to participate in the construction and use of latrines in their localities. For every family to make our Preah Vihear province a province to get rid of open defecation by 2025.
Ms. Chhay Sovanna, Deputy Director of the Department, Mr. Mop Thirith, Director of the Department of Rural Development of Preah Vihear Province, said that as of August 2023, the sanitation coverage rate in the whole province was 68%, of which 46 villages and communes had completed open defecation. In 232 villages and communes, there are 4 out of 51 communes in Preah Vihear province.
On this occasion, Mr. Ouk Kimsan thanked UNICEF for cooperating with the Provincial Department of Rural Development, as well as a number of relevant departments, as well as local authorities at all levels, to conduct training "on accelerating the situation to end defecation. In the open field ”today.
On behalf of Mr. Kim Rithy, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, Mr. Ouk Kimsan also expressed his hope that today's training is an important input to provide good experience and knowledge, as well as important tips to all participants. Attend this course.
He also urged all participants to pay attention to listen to and follow the explanations of trainers who have experience in inspiring people on the construction and use of toilets.
The expression of gratitude as well as the gratitude was made during the Prime Minister of Timor-Leste's meeting with His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia in Jakarta, Indonesia on September 6, 2023. This.
In this meeting, the Prime Minister of East Timor expressed his deep congratulations to Samdech Hun Sen Manet for the support of the people and the National Assembly to lead the new Royal Government of Cambodia. The Prime Minister also sent a message of greetings to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Supreme Council of the King, whom he always considered a respected brother.
The Prime Minister expressed his deep gratitude to the Royal Government and Samdech Techo Hun Sen for their continued support and encouragement to Timor-Leste in regional and global integration.
"Assisting East Timor to become an ASEAN observer country as Cambodia chairs ASEAN in 2022, as well as supporting and sharing Cambodia's experience in becoming an ASEAN member in 1999, are respectable gestures. "And it is an important way for Timor-Leste to learn and prepare for ASEAN membership in the near future." This is the emphasis of Mr. Kaira Lazana Nagosmao.
Samdech President Hun Manet expressed his deep gratitude for the congratulations and thanks to the Royal Government of Cambodia and Samdech Techo. He also said that helping Timor-Leste is also a source of pride for Cambodia.
He added that Cambodia, as a country that has gone through 1,000 chapters of destruction, clearly understands the situation and the situation that East Timor is facing today. The President of the Royal Government of Cambodia has strongly stated that he will continue to support and assist Timor-Leste, especially in the upcoming preparations for ASEAN membership.
During the meeting, the two leaders also discussed potential areas for enhancing cooperation between the two countries, especially in trade, education, agriculture, and tourism. The two leaders hope that these good cooperation will be of great benefit to both nations.
