Minister of Rural Development makes some recommendations to subordinates to expand community development and continue to help indigenous peoples
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chhay Rithi Sen, Minister of Rural Development, on September 6, 2023, met with the leaders in charge of the Department and civil servants of the Department of Community Development and the Department of Ethnic Development and made some recommendations focusing on Expanding community development and continuing to assist indigenous peoples.
On that occasion, Mr. Oeun Thearith, Advisor to the Ministry and Director of the Department of Community Development, and Ms. Nuon Monichenda, Director of the Department of Ethnic Development, reported on the progress, achievements, as well as challenges and directions of the two departments for the first half. 2023 on community and indigenous development.
The Minister expressed his appreciation and appreciation for the efforts of the management and professional officers of both departments, which achieved proud results.
He considers these two departments to play an important role in improving the lives of people in rural areas. He said that these are the sacrifices of all civil servants to get overwhelming support from people across the country through the past parliamentary elections.
During the meeting, the Minister also gave recommendations and instructions to the leaders in charge and civil servants under the supervision of the two departments as follows:
1. Based on the existing achievements, both departments must strive to create more new achievements and achievements to contribute to the further development of rural areas in accordance with the Pentagon Strategy of the Royal Government of the 7th legislature to achieve the vision of Cambodia 2030 as a revenue country. High average and 2050 as a high income country.
3. The Department of Indigenous Peoples' Development shall strive to strengthen the capacity of the Indigenous Community Development Committees and shall finalize the location maps of the indigenous communities.
4. Study to create model villages by selecting villages that have potential and favorable in terms of economy, tourism or other agricultural products according to the geographical situation, especially in indigenous communities.
5. Provide training on life skills or necessary skills to the community in accordance with the needs and circumstances.
6. Training soft skills related to changing attitudes, changing the moral mindset of living with high cooperation and solidarity.
7. The leaders and officials of both departments must adhere to the rules and regulations of the system, set the regular monitoring and inspection monthly, quarterly and semi-regular meetings, and report and ask for advice in a timely manner.
8. The two departments must prepare their achievements report for the meeting to review the work results for the year 2023 and the work direction for the next year, which is scheduled to be held on December 22, 2023.
9. Strengthen internal unity to work more effectively by paying attention to the well-being of sick and disabled civil servants, especially pregnant civil servants through encouragement and favorable working hours. .
