PM Hun Sen Attends ASEAN-Canada Summit
(Phnom Penh): In Jakarta, Indonesia, on Wednesday afternoon, September 6, 2023, His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, attended the ASEAN-Canada Summit.
The ASEAN-Canada Summit is chaired by Indonesian President Joko Widodo and chair of ASEAN and Canadian Prime Minister Justin Trudeau.
The ASEAN-Canada Dialogue was established in February 1977 after the first official meeting between the Canadian Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs and the ASEAN Standing Committee. In 1981, the ASEAN-Canada Economic Cooperation Agreement (ACECA) was signed, laying the groundwork for industrial, commercial and technical cooperation between the two sides.
By 2020, trade between ASEAN and Canada will reach $ 16.2 billion, and foreign direct investment (FDI) from Canada to ASEAN will reach $ 5.1 billion. Gen. Sar Thet Appoints Lt. Gen. E Sok Khi as Closing Representative of the 52nd Private Security Agency Training Course of the Private Security Management Department
(Phnom Penh): General Sar Thet, General Commissioner of the National Police, appointed Lt. Gen. E Sok Khi, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police, to preside over the closing ceremony of the 52nd Private Security Agency Training Course of the Private Security Administration Department this afternoon. This September 06, 2023.
Speaking on the occasion, Lt. Gen. Ey Sok Khi praised the leadership of the Department of Private Security Management, Trainers, Team for Organizing the 52nd Private Security Agency Training Course with 145 participants (2 females) and a trainer who Highly experienced as a judicial police officer and professional leader of the National Police Force.
Lt. Gen. Ey Sok Khi encouraged all private security agencies stationed at the targets to continue to cooperate and report to law enforcement or local authorities in the event of a crime or suspected location nearby. There will be various offenses. Private security agencies must act as good citizens and good people and be an important support force to the competent authorities and must cooperate well and respond in a timely manner.
According to Lt. Gen. E Sok Khi, when a private security agent sees or suspects any illegal activity, whether in his standing position or immediately, he must immediately report it to the competent authority or to the department directly via Phone provided to jointly prevent, prevent and crack down on crime in a timely manner. In addition, we must continue to work together to implement the policies of the Royal Government, especially the policy of safe villages, communes and sangkats.
Lt. Gen. Ey Sok Khi advised that private security agents must have a proper attitude to participate in the work by adhering to what is right after receiving training to respect the qualifications of private security agents, that is, discipline, ethics, Use adequate private security uniforms and equipment.
In addition, he urged the directors of private security companies and institutions (to continue to support the training) by sending private security agents to attend the course, and all participants must apply the knowledge gained from this study and continue. Expand knowledge, intelligence, creativity and high responsibility in fulfilling their role.
At the same time, Lt. Gen. Ey Sok Khi also asked private security service providers and enterprises to consider applying for the National Social Security Fund (NSSF) to their agencies that do not yet have access to government support. .
He added that the training is aimed at meeting the need to increase the capacity to become a qualified and qualified private security agent for participation in the maintenance and protection of stability, security, safety, order and age. People's lives as well as improve the policy of safe villages, communes and sangkats.
