President Hun Manet highlighted China's importance for ASEAN at the 26th ASEAN-China Summit on Wednesday morning, September 6, 2023 in Jakarta, Indonesia, where ASEAN leaders and leaders of dialogue partners Are meeting.
The ASEAN-China Summit was chaired by Indonesian President Joko Widodo and chaired by ASEAN and Chinese Premier Li Keqiang.
At the beginning of the ASEAN-China Summit, Chairman Joko Widodo delivered the opening remarks and invited Chinese Premier Li Chiang to deliver speeches and remarks. Prior to the start of the closed-door talks, Joko Widodo asked the media to leave the meeting room. Joko Widodo then invited the leaders of ASEAN countries in a series of speeches and also invited the East Timorese Prime Minister.
In his keynote address at the meeting, President Hun Manet highlighted some of China's important roles for ASEAN.
President Hun Manet stated that Cambodia recognizes the common interests of good relations during the nearly three decades between China and ASEAN. As for Cambodia, the Belt and Road Initiative (BRI) has provided many benefits to Cambodia, especially in the areas of transportation and logistics, such as the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway, which is an example of the achievements of this initiative.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia also noted the importance of the tourism sector, which is the main engine of economic growth, still low compared to the pre-Kovid-19 crisis. In this regard, the President stressed the need for ASEAN to promote the effective implementation of the ASEAN-China Declaration on Tourism Cooperation.
In addition, President Hun Manet also briefed the ASEAN-China Summit on the President's visit to Nanning to attend the 20th China-ASEAN Expo (CAEXPO) and the visit to Beijing to attend the meeting. Top on Belt and Road Initiative (BRI).
