Prey Veng Provincial Police Commissioner Takes Action to Collect Students Who Avoid School
(Prey Veng): Major General Chhoeun Bunchon, Prey Veng Provincial Police Commissioner, took action to gather students who evaded school to gather, play games, play phone games, and gather in groups to educate, guide, make contracts at the police inspectorate, and invite their parents to guarantee. Go home with the knowledge of teachers and principals as well.
The commissioner-general stated that such practices at first glance seemed a bit out of place for the police and could be criticized for infringing on the rights and freedoms of the students, but the commissioner stressed that if the police did not participate Then many children may drop out of school due to not studying well or not having an exam name, etc. Because the current curriculum is very strict.
The commissioner said that most of the children who are dressed in such a crowd will soon form a group of big and small brothers to commit inappropriate acts or may lead to committing a crime that society hates this and avoid the police to intervene. Already.
He added that if teachers, guardians, parents, the people or the police do not participate in correcting this problem, the future of these children could become a social disease that requires unlimited treatment. On the other hand, the development of the nation will also be difficult because the school children we see today, the future, are also contributors to the national destiny.
After receiving instructions from the Provincial Police Commissioner, the police force of the 13 city-district police inspectorates started to hold outreach forums in schools and started collecting children who evaded school for many cases.
Phnom Penh Police Crack Down on Four Suspects in Siem Reap and Prey Veng Provinces Involving Victims in Daun Penh District
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner's Office of Minor Crimes searched all the way to Siem Reap and Prey Veng provinces to crack down on and arrest four suspects in a row in connection with the intentional violence against the victims. Together, they used their hands and feet to kick and hit the victim on the head with a bottle of beer, causing him to bleed and suffer serious injuries, fainting) from September 3-5, 2023.
According to the report of Lieutenant Colonel Mam Savon, Director of the Bureau of Minor Offenses of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police on September 6, 2023, this operation was carried out under the direct command of Lieutenant General Chuon Narin, Deputy Commissioner and Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner.
Please note that the case of a group of people kicking and hitting the victim on the head with a bottle of beer, causing fainting, occurred in front of a nightclub (Miss-EX) along the corner of Street 55 and Street 242, Village 5, Sangkat Chaktomuk, Khan Daun Penh, Phnom Penh. Phnom Penh. The suspects were arrested at the Kampong Kdei bridge in Chi Kreng district, Siem Reap province, and in Bum Chay Mear district, Prey Veng province.
Lt. Col. Mam Savon said that the four suspects who were detained by the authorities include:
While smoking, the suspects saw a group of women arguing with each other. Suddenly, the victim walked out of the club and in front of the suspect, Wa, with a beer bottle in his hand, hit the victim on the head. The accident caused the beer bottle to explode and the victim fell on the road.
Another suspect, Da, did not take part in the beating. After beating the victim, causing him to lose his head and faint, the suspects escaped. The victim was rescued and taken to hospital.
Lt. Col. Mam Savon added that for the four suspects, the specialized office has been preparing to build a case to send to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court to proceed with the procedure.
