Despite being busy in Indonesia, President Hun Manet solves the request of monks and people to build a road to Tuol Preah Theat (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Despite being busy with the ASEAN Summit in Indonesia, Samdech Hun Sen The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia also took action to solve the problem that was the request of the monks and the people related to the entrance to Tuol Preah Theat in Ta Ben village, Prek Anchanh commune, Muk Kampoul district, Kandal province.
Tuol Preah Theat is an ancient hill, a place of worship, religion and belief of the people in Prek Anchanh commune, which has a long history. This ancient hill has a huge Po tree, which is estimated to be about 1,000 years old. This Po tree splits its branches and begs for shade. In addition, the monks also set up shrines for worship in both Buddhism and Hinduism.
Mr. Leng Bunlim also said that Tuol Preah Theat is also a meeting place for people to celebrate festivals and other traditional ceremonies.
Tuol Preah Theat is not far from Phnom Penh. Tuol, the people's shrine, is located on the 12th bridge and is only about two kilometers down from National Road 6A. But what is difficult to get to this ancient hill is the road. At present, Tuol Preah Theat is surrounded by land that is privately owned, so if people want to enter this hill, they have to ask to travel.
Faced with such difficulties, Venerable Pov Piseth, who was taking care of the ancient hill above, sought the intervention of the authorities many times because it did not work. Recently, Venerable Pov Piseth, who has been invited to stay at Tuol Preah Theat 5 Preah Vossa, decided to make a video calling on Samdech Hun Sen to help find a solution and build a road to this ancient hill. .
The message of the request of Venerable Pov Piseth was posted only for one day and one night to reach Samdech Hun Manet. Despite being busy at the ASEAN Summit and related summits in Indonesia, the Prime Minister instructed the Governor of Kandal Province, Mr. Kong Sophoan, to study and facilitate the construction of a road for the people to enter the sacred hill. On this.
On September 4, Kong Sophoan visited Tuol Preah Theat and met with landowners around Tuol and discussed with the district authorities to build the road.
According to the authorities, the access road to Tuol Preah Theat is nearly 2 kilometers long. Nearly 1 km of land is an existing state road, while more than 1 km of land is privately owned by 3 owners, including Mr. Nguon Seang, Ms. Ngov Pok and Ms. Sreng Pek Keang. Under the coordination of the Governor of Kandal Province, the three landowners agreed to donate land to the authorities to build a road for people to travel to Tuol Preah Theat.
After coordinating, Mr. Kong Sophoan also instructed and arranged for the equipment to pioneer and pour the construction soil soon. This road will be built with a width of up to 7 meters.
Mr. Som Phalla, Deputy Governor of Muk Kampul District, as the district authority, expressed his happiness and joy when he received the direct intervention of the head of the Royal Government in building roads for people to travel like this. According to Mr. Phalla, the provincial governor will build a concrete road and install electricity for the people.
After receiving such quick intervention from the head of the Royal Government, both Venerable Pov Piseth and the people who always go out to worship and worship at Tuol Preah Theat expressed their hearts and minds very happy. Venerable Pov Piseth and the people highly appreciated the consideration of Samdech Mani Hun Manet on the well-being as well as the needs of the people.
