Samdech Hun Manet and His Majesty the Sultan Aim to Increase Cooperation in Defense, Security, Education, Training, Human Resources and Agriculture (Video inside) (Jakarta, Indonesia) The King of Brunei Darussalam Bolkiah Mujahideen Vadula intends to increase cooperation in areas such as defense, security, education, training, human resources and agriculture.
This intention was expressed in a courtesy meeting and discussion between Samdech Hun Manet and the Sultan on Wednesday morning, September 6, 2023 in Jakarta, Indonesia.
In the above meeting, Samdech Thepdey welcomed and brought a warm welcome from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Supreme Council of the King to the Sultan.
The Prime Minister spoke about the good relations between Cambodia and Brunei, especially in the field of defense, which he visited in Brunei when he was the Commander-in-Chief of the Army.
The Sultan expressed his deep gratitude to the President and reminded of the close friendship between him and Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Supreme Council of the King.
During the meeting, the President and the Sultan discussed the future direction of enhancing cooperation between Cambodia and Brunei, focusing on defense, security, education and training of human resources, agriculture, as well as linkages. Between the people and the people of the two countries.
President Hun Manet and the Sultan agreed to increase cooperation on cross-border crime prevention, private sector integration through the Chamber of Commerce, and support for the implementation of bilateral dialogue mechanisms between the two countries' foreign ministers.
During the meeting, the Sultan invited the President to pay an official visit to Brunei at an appropriate time. The Prime Minister accepted the invitation and returned to the Sultan to pay a royal visit to Cambodia. Police crack down on more than 5,000 drug cases and arrest 12,356 people, confiscate more than 2.5 tons of drugs in 8 months this year
