Minister of Rural Development instructs officials of the Department of Rural Roads to pay more attention to the construction of quality and durable roads
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chhay Rithi Sen, Minister of Rural Development, instructed the civil servants of the Department of Rural Roads to study the technical and legal standards clearly before constructing the road to make sure that the built road is of good quality and usable. Long lasting.
This introduction was made on the occasion of Mr. Chhay Rithi Sen's meeting with the leaders and officials of the Department of Rural Roads on September 6, 2023 at the Ministry of Rural Development.
Mr. Kong Phoeun, Advisor to the Ministry of Rural Development and Head of the Department, reported to the Minister on the progress report and achievements and directions of the Department to the Minister. According to the report, the Minister expressed his appreciation and appreciation for the efforts of the management and professional staff of the department.
Minister Chhay Rithi Sen also gave the following recommendations and instructions to the leadership of civil servants under the Department of Rural Roads:
1. Based on the existing achievements and directions, the Department must strive to create and increase new achievements and achievements in order to build Cambodia in the field of rural development to further develop in line with the Pentagon strategy of the Royal Government of the seventh mandate and to strengthen the control campaign. Examine ongoing projects for greater efficiency.
2. Must study the technical and legal standards clearly before building the road to make sure that the road is built quality and durable.
3. According to the new policy by Samdech Hun Manet, development must be promoted to areas with high potential, areas with high need for development.
4. Procurement must be transparent and in accordance with procedures.
5. Provide training for professional officers to monitor additional technical skills for officers to make their work more effective.
6. Examine the possibility of delegating work to build, maintain and repair roads to provinces that have the capacity and have sufficient professional officers to manage.
7. Let the department study the placement of existing rural roads under construction.
8. Strengthen the laboratory work to control the raw materials to be used to build roads and artistic constructions in accordance with technical standards and study to find new quality raw materials to be used in the future.
10. Prepare annual summary report and work direction for the next year, which the Ministry of Rural Development is scheduled to prepare on December 22, 2023.
11. Strengthen internal solidarity to work more effectively and achieve better results in the new 7th legislature of the Royal Government and to contribute to promote the vision of Cambodia 2030 as a high middle income country and 2050 as a country High income.
12. Pay attention to civil servants under the supervision of special officers who are sick, pregnant women, retired officials and encourage by appreciating the awarding of medals to officials who have worked in the Ministry in the past.
The Minister also took the initiative to establish the "Association of Civil Servants of the Ministry of Rural Development" in order to maintain solidarity and internal friendship.
Samdech Hun Sen Presides Over the 26th ASEAN-Japan Summit
(Jakarta, Indonesia): On the morning of Wednesday, September 6, 2023, Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Manet attended the 26th ASEAN-Japan Summit in Jakarta, Indonesia.
The ASEAN-Japan Summit was chaired by Indonesian President Joko Widodo and chair of ASEAN and Japanese Prime Minister Fumio Kishida.
Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Secretary-General of ASEAN, was also invited to attend the meeting.
It should be noted that ASEAN and Japan established the first informal dialogue in 1973, then formalized in March 1977 with the convening of the ASEAN-Japan Forum.
Since then, significant progress has been made in all areas, including political security, economic, financial and socio-cultural cooperation.
Japan joined the Treaty of Amity and Cooperation in Southeast Asia (TAC) in July 2004 and became a dialogue partner, appointing its ambassador to ASEAN at the ASEAN Secretariat in Jakarta. The Japan Mission to ASEAN was established on May 26, 2011.
Bilateral trade between ASEAN and Japan reached 240.2 billion US dollars, up 17.2 percent year on year, according to ASEAN data for 2021. Foreign direct investment (FDI) inflows from Japan in 2021 will reach 12.0 billion US dollars, up 3.5 percent year on year, making Japan its third largest trading partner. ASEAN among ASEAN dialogue partners in 2021 as well.
Deputy Prime Minister Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of the Kingdom of Cambodia, and other ASEAN Foreign Ministers witnessed the signing ceremony of the TAC. According to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, the signing of the instruments of the three countries has increased the number of TAC parties to 54.
Meanwhile, the ASEAN Foreign Ministers look forward to the signing of the TAC by Spain, Mexico, Algeria and Luxembourg soon.
Please be informed that at the invitation of Ms. Reth No Masudi, Minister of Foreign Affairs of the Republic of Indonesia, Deputy Prime Minister Sok Chenda Sophea attended the 27th ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting (AMM) and the ASEAN Political-Security Council (APSC) Meeting. And the 34th ASEAN Coordinating Council (ACC) Meeting on September 4, 2023 in Jakarta, Republic of Indonesia.
