The new Director General of the General Department of Prisons has set out five priority tasks for all leaders and officials to continue their efforts to perform their duties and maintain internal unity.
(Phnom Penh): Chief of General Staff No. 1 Chhorn Sanath, Director General of the General Department of Prisons, who just took office last week, this morning, September 6, 2023, met with the leaders and officials of the General Department of Prisons. . The meeting was held at the Ministry of Interior.
Speaking on the occasion, Mr. Chhorn Sanath reminded about the achievements of the previous generation of leaders for the officials of the General Department of Prisons, especially good recommendations that all officials must continue to implement in order to continue to strengthen work efficiency and responsibility. According to its function, role, duties.
At the same time, His Excellency Chhorn Sanath, the 1st Class Conservation Building Officer, issued 5 additional instructions as a reminder to all officials, including:
* First: Strengthen the implementation of the law, continue to pay attention to increase awareness of the law and the legal documents in force to focus on leadership and skills.
* Second: Harmonization of work, strengthening professional ethics, sense of responsibility, ownership of their duties and internal unity for the benefit of the organization as a whole.
* Third: Take strict action against the inactivity of the officers to evaluate the qualifications based on the truth, transparency and rewards policy.
* Fifth: Strengthen and expand the capacity to perform the functions of correctional centers to promote rehabilitation programs, vocational training programs, and the integration of detainees back into the community.
