The following is the full text of the decision: The Prime Minister of Cambodia expresses his desire to learn from Singapore on the implementation of military service of the people (Video inside) (Jakarta, Indonesia): The Prime Minister of Cambodia, His Excellency Hun Manet, expressed interest in Singapore Citizens' military service and intends to learn from this experience from Singapore as well.
On the evening of September 5, 2023, Prime Minister Hun Manet met with Singaporean Prime Minister Lee Hsien Loong in Jakarta, Indonesia, where the two leaders attended the ASEAN Summit and related summits.
During the meeting, Mr. Ly Xianlong expressed his warm congratulations to Samdech Hun Sen, who was elected Prime Minister of Cambodia. The Prime Minister also reminded with emotion when he met with Samdech in 2018.
Samdech Thibodi Hun Manet expressed his deep gratitude for this celebration. In particular, Singapore was the first country to send a congratulatory letter to the President.
During the meeting, Samdech Hun Sen expressed his pleasure for the long-term relations and cooperation in all fields between the two countries. In particular, the defense and education sectors, where Singapore has always provided technical assistance as well as training to Cambodia.
Samdech Hun Sen expressed Cambodia's intention to learn from Singapore's experience in the field of national defense, especially in the implementation of the people's military service.
Mr. Lee Hsien Loong agreed to explore the possibility of continuing to provide technical support and training to Cambodia in both the civil and military fields, and he also invited the Prime Minister to visit Singapore in the near future.
The two leaders discussed ways to further strengthen existing cooperation and expand cooperation in areas such as trade, investment, tourism, education, security, energy, health, digital, agriculture and defense.
The two heads of government also discussed the possibility of importing rice and other agricultural products from Cambodia to the Singapore market, as well as plans to build an underwater power transmission line from Laos to Singapore. President of An Huy Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia: believes that under the leadership of Samdech Hun Manet, Cambodia will enter the golden age of rapid development
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Liu Yin, President of the Anhui Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia, believes that under the leadership of the next generation of Cambodian leaders, Samdech Thep Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, with the joint efforts of all RCEP members in Cambodia. Will enter the golden age of rapid development.
The President of the Anhui Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia expressed his confidence in the morning of September 5, 2023, when he attended a roundtable discussion on the President of the Anhui Provincial Chinese Federation outside. RCEP countries organized by the Chinese Federation of Anhui Overseas and Anhui Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia.
The President of the Anhui Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia pointed out that looking back at the past since the establishment of the RCEP has led to an era of higher, stronger and faster development. Today, the world is undergoing rapid change, difficulties and uncertainties are increasing, and Cambodia's nation-building process has also entered a new phase.
Mr. Liu Yin emphasized that in addition, the new government led by Prime Minister Hun Manet, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has begun to implement the "Phase 1 Pentagon Strategy", including: 1: human capital development, 2: economic diversification, 3: Private Sector and Employment Development, 4: Sustainable and Environmental Development, and 5: Digital Economic and Social Development.
He said the "Pentagon Strategy" is based on peace and development established by the Cambodian government over the past 25 years and guides the country and its people to achieve the development vision to become a high-income country in the long run. The next 25 years.
In addition, Mr. Liu Yin also announced to welcome An Huy compatriots to visit Cambodia to share their memories and seek common development.
For more than a year, under Liu Yin's leadership, there has been strong support from all member organizations and has played an active role in promoting economic, trade and cultural exchanges and cooperation. Between Anhui Province and RCEP countries. These related works have also received strong support from Anhui provincial government leaders and overseas Chinese federations.
