(Phnom Penh): A young Chinese student studying in Singapore was rescued by the Ministry of Interior's Intelligence Department in cooperation with Chinese embassy officials in Cambodia after he became convinced of the machinations of a rogue group. Fraudulent Singapore authorities and prosecutors persuaded victims to imitate the victims of the kidnapping and sent a video clip to their guardians to demand $ 710,000.
The victim, a Chinese student, is pursuing a first-year bachelor's degree in stock marketing at the University of Management, Singapore.
Based on the description of the victim in the press conference on the afternoon of August 31, 2023, when the Cambodian authorities allowed him to tell the story, said that on August 3, 2023, there was an unidentified man. One called himself claiming to be Singapore's immigration police in a Chinese conversation, stating that the victim was involved in several scams.
According to the source, the scammers used words of intimidation and consolation until the victim was afraid of being punished and followed the instructions of the suspects. The victim arrived in Cambodia on On August 10, they were instructed to find a hotel room to stay in temporarily and made several short video clips of themselves acting as victims of the kidnapping and sent the video to the suspects.
After receiving several video clips from the victim, the suspects forwarded the video to the victim's parents (residing in China), threatening to pay $ 710,000, but were sent by the victim's parents. For only $ 5,000 and also complained to the authorities of Singapore and the Chinese Embassy to intervene.
After receiving the complaint, the Singapore authorities investigated and found that the victim had entered Cambodia, so the victim's parents and Chinese embassy officials cooperated with the Cambodian police to search for the victim. Found on August 15, 2023 in Aeon Mall 2 in Sen Sok district, while the victim was filming his activities to report to the suspects.
Cambodia, China jointly review the results of cooperation and mutual support in the fight against drugs
(China): General Meas Virith, Secretary-General of the National Anti-Drug Authority, confirmed that the Cambodian and Chinese authorities have jointly reviewed the results of cooperation and mutual support in the fight against drugs in Beijing.
This statement was made by General Meas Virith on the occasion that he led the Cambodian delegation to the 10th Cambodia-China Bilateral Meeting on Drug Control Cooperation on the afternoon of September 4, 2023. At the Ministry of Public Security of the People's Republic of China in Beijing.
(Kampot): Mr. Chhay Rithi Sen, Minister of Rural Development, on September 5, 2023, inspected 2 water supply sources and 1 public toilet with 4 rooms in Chhuk District, Kampot Province.
This activity was accompanied by delegates and technical officers of the Ministry of Rural Development, Provincial Department of Rural Development, as well as the participation of Mr. Khieu Rithiphorn, Deputy Governor of Kampot and many other relevant officials.
The sites inspected included:
Location 1: Atmospheric water pumping station is located in Srakaneak village, Taken commune, Chhuk district, Kampot province, with a maximum capacity of 800-2000 liters per day under the budget of the Asian Development Bank (ADB) and the Royal contribution. The Cambodian government provides the people for use and management by the community. This water pump is powered by a solar system.
Location 2: 10,000 liters public rainwater filter tank and 1 public toilet with 4 rooms, located in Boeung village, Boeung Nimol commune, Chhuk district, Kampot province, in the area of Boeung Nimol health center for public benefit.
During the meeting with the people, the Minister brought greetings from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
In the afternoon of the same day, Mr. Chhay Rithi Sen and the accompanying delegation continued to meet and greet the leaders of civil servants of Kampot Provincial Department of Rural Development.
After listening to the welcome report of Mr. Hor Sorin, Director of the Department of Rural Development of Kampot Province, the Minister expressed his appreciation and appreciation for the efforts of the leaders and civil servants of the Provincial Department of Rural Development and gave the following recommendations. This:
1. Continue to work hard to participate in rural development work to improve the living conditions of the people in rural areas in an economic, social and cultural environment in line with the vision and strategy of the Royal Government of the 7th legislature.
2. Cooperate with relevant departments, institutions and local authorities at all levels by fulfilling the role of technical staff to provincial governors and provincial councils in the field of rural development.
3. Adhere to the rules and regulations of the meeting system, monitor and inspect monthly, quarterly, semi-regular meetings to jointly address the requests of the people.
4. Prepare annual summary report and work direction for the next year, which the Ministry of Rural Development plans to prepare on December 22, 2023.
5. Strengthen internal solidarity to work more effectively and achieve better results in the new 7th legislature of the Royal Government and to contribute to promote the vision of Cambodia 2030 as a high middle income country and 2050 as a country High income.
6. Establish a spokesperson for the Department to provide information and coordinate with the spokesperson of the provincial hall and the spokesperson of the Ministry of Rural Development in order to participate in disseminating the achievements of the Royal Government widely.
