Kratie Provincial Department of Education, Youth and Sports Holds National Literacy Day
(Kratie): Mr. Hang Chandy, Deputy Governor of Kratie Province, on September 5, 2023, presided over the National Literacy Day on September 8 under the theme "Literacy as the Foundation of Entrepreneurship and Socio-Economics" in Wat Po Rainsy, Wat Phum Thmey I. Located in Khsach Andet Commune, Chhlong District, Kratie Province.
He said that the national policy on lifelong learning to develop all Cambodians to have lifelong learning opportunities in all contexts and everywhere with skills, skills, fitness, behavior, fitness and fitness to contribute to economic growth and harmony. Of life.
He went on to recall that after the day of liberation on January 7, 1979, Cambodia was left with very few intellectuals and scholars, this principle is an important way to promote the development of our people to this day. Literacy is a key means and starting point of education and also the basis of development in all fields.
He said that for the National Literacy Day 2023, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports has set the theme "Literacy as the foundation of entrepreneurship and socio-economic". This policy aims to provide non-formal and informal education services to all citizens and use the knowledge gained to enhance efficiency, quality, productivity and income in line with the age of information technology and Buddhist society.
