On the occasion of presiding over the 33rd Anniversary of the 24th Anniversary of the Establishment of the 246th Battalion and the 14th Anniversary of the Establishment of the Bodyguard Command on the morning of September 5, 2023, Dr. Neth Savoeun He pointed out that drugs are now flowing into the countryside, which is a matter of concern for the future of Cambodian youth in the future.
In addition, the Acting Prime Minister emphasized that there are two main measures to be taken:
First, it is the role of the Royal Government, the authorities and the law enforcement forces to make more efforts to fight drugs. The government will set up a national commission to lead a joint force in the fight against drugs.
Second, it is an educational work, which calls on the people and civil servants of the Armed Forces, with a family, a village, a commune or an institution to help monitor and warn not to get involved in drugs, which is a movement that needs to participate. Practice together.
The Acting Prime Minister hopes that under the leadership of the National Commission will develop strategies to increase the effectiveness of drug prevention.
Please be informed that according to the Acting Prime Minister, starting from the poor management of chemicals, some crooks seize the opportunity to secretly produce and process drugs, which the forces cracked down on a lot. In fact, in 2022, Cambodia cracked down on more than 16 tons of drugs and nearly 400 tons of chemical compounds. Samdech President Hun Manet and ASEAN Leaders Hold a Closer Meeting
(Jakarta, Indonesia): On the afternoon of September 5, 2023, Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Manet, together with other ASEAN leaders, began a closed-door meeting under the chairmanship of Indonesian President Joko Widodo and chair of ASEAN. .
It should be noted that the 43rd ASEAN Summit officially opened this morning, September 5, 2023 in Jakarta, Indonesia, as the rotating chair. Indonesia, as chair of ASEAN, has set the theme of the ASEAN Summit "ASEAN Importance: Core of Growth".
The leaders of the ASEAN member countries present at the meeting included the President of Indonesia, the King of Brunei, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, the Prime Minister of Vietnam, the Prime Minister of Laos, the Prime Minister of Malaysia, the Prime Minister of Singapore and the President of the Philippines. Thailand, meanwhile, sends only high-ranking officials because the Thai prime minister is busy completing other procedures to become a full-fledged prime minister.
The meeting was also attended by East Timorese leaders as observers.
