During a meeting between Indonesian President Joko Widodo and Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Manet in Jakarta, Joko Widodo expressed satisfaction that Cambodia had agreed to supply 250,000 tonnes of rice a year to Indonesia. At the same time, Indonesia will support Cambodia's food security program through the supply of agricultural fertilizers.
"I appreciate the positive response from Cambodia regarding the import of 250,000 tonnes of rice from our neighbors," Joko Widodo said.
Pen Sovicheat, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Commerce, told Fresh News on September 5, 2023 that the agreement to supply 250,000 tonnes of rice a year to Indonesia is for four years, which will begin. Implemented from 2024 onwards.
Separately, the agreement to supply 12,500 tons of rice, including 100,000 tons of white rice using the mechanism of Bullock and Green Trade, and another 2,500 tons of luxury rice between ID food and members of the Cambodian Rice Federation will be implemented. 2023.
He said the two sides would revise a memorandum of understanding between the Cambodian Ministry of Commerce and the Indonesian Ministry of Commerce on a rice trade of up to 250,000 tonnes per year for four years.
He added that the price will be negotiated depending on the fluctuations of the actual market.
The agreement to import 250,000 tonnes of rice a year from Cambodia comes after India stopped exporting rice to Indonesia. Indonesia initially planned to import 1 million tonnes of rice from India, but the proposal was rejected. This is according to Indonesian Trade Minister Zulkifli Hasan.
According to Indonesian government data, the national rice stockpile at Bulog has reached nearly 1.6 million tonnes as of Monday, September 4, in addition to the supply of 400,000 tonnes of rice from neighboring countries. Will be delivered later this year based on previous agreement.
