Minister of Environment Instructs the Department of Environment to Start a Campaign to Reduce Plastics in Schools
(Koh Kong): Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Minister of Environment, urged the Department of Environment to launch a campaign to reduce the use of plastic in schools so that Cambodia can reduce plastic waste for sustainable development.
In the meeting with leaders, civil servants and park rangers of Koh Kong Provincial Department of Environment on the afternoon of September 3, 2023. The Minister encouraged the Department of Environment of Koh Kong Province to start outreach, especially with teachers and students in schools, starting from all schools in the district or municipality to be committed to participating in the campaign "Today I do not use plastic.
At the same time, the Minister stressed that the contribution of students and teachers to reduce and stop using plastic from one day or two days a week, Cambodia participated in protecting and maintaining the environment to reduce the use of plastic. Millions of bags. At the same time, the campaign will support the welfare of the people, the quality of the environment, the beauty of the city and the village to be beautiful and make Cambodia sustainable development.
The campaign to reduce the use of plastic was launched by the Minister of Environment with students in schools starting from September 1, 2023 from 44 schools with a total of more than 18,000 students across Ou Raing Ov district, Tbong Khmum province. In the main purpose "for the good of our environment."
Reuters, based on sources familiar with Suu Kyi and the shadow government, said the 78-year-old Nobel Peace Prize winner was receiving medical treatment from a prison doctor. The source, who asked not to be named, said Suu Kyi had swollen gums and could not eat easily and was dizzy and nauseous. However, a spokesman for the Myanmar military junta did not respond to a request for comment.
Suu Kyi faces up to 27 years in prison on 19 charges ranging from incitement and electoral fraud to corruption. In July, she was transferred from prison to house arrest in the capital, Nay Pyi Taw. She has denied the allegations against her and is appealing.
Meeting with ASEAN Secretary-General, Cambodian Head of Diplomacy emphasizes the importance of promoting ASEAN Community Building Efforts (Video inside) (Jakarta): Ahead of the 43rd ASEAN Summit and Related Summits in Jakarta, Deputy Prime Minister Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, pays a courtesy call on Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Secretary-General of ASEAN, on September 4, 2023.
On that occasion, Deputy Prime Minister Sok Chenda Sophea emphasized the importance of accelerating efforts to build the ASEAN Community in line with the vision of "ASEAN: One Community, One Destiny." ASEAN Secretary-General Kao Kim Hourn also reaffirmed the full support of the ASEAN Secretariat to Cambodia and other ASEAN Member States towards achieving the ASEAN Community Vision 2025 and beyond 2025.
Kandal Provincial Governor Builds New Road to Tuol Preah Theatny Ashram, Muk Kampoul District, After Request from Citizens
(Kandal): Monks at Tuol Preah Theat Ashram and the people thanked Mr. Kong Sophoan, Governor of Kandal Province for facilitating the opening of roads and concrete roads for Buddhist monks and people to travel to and from Tuol Preah Theat Ashram. In Prek Ta Ben village, Prek Anchanh commune, Muk Kampoul district.
It should be informed that on September 4, 2023, the Governor of Kandal Province visited the site in order to coordinate with the landowners, with good results, which was well received by the people. Landowner Sreng Keang (wife of Mr. Hay) agreed to donate 3.5 meters of land and Nguon Seang donated 3.5 meters of land to pave the way to Tuol Preah Theat hermitage.
Along with agreeing to open the road, Mr. Kong Sophoan instructed the team and the authorities of Muk Kampul district to pioneer to open the road, raise the land above the water and pave the stones to make it easier to travel temporarily. When paving stones, solar lights must be installed to illuminate the sidewalks to illuminate the people as well. Once this road has a solid foundation, this road needs to be concreted for the people.
It should be noted that in the past, Buddhists and people came to pay their respects at Tuol Preah Theat hermitage, passing through their land without a road before, then the landowner raised a dam around the border and the people there Have traveled through that dam so far.
Recently, the landowners built a fence around their land to make it impossible for people to enter and exit the Tuol Preah Theat hermitage, so they asked the Muk Kampul district authority, especially Kong Sophorn, to solve and open the road for them. For the alms-giving ceremony at the Tuol Preah Theat hermitage.
