(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia, His Excellency Hun Manet, this morning, September 5, 2023, attended the opening ceremony of the 43rd ASEAN Summit in Jakarta, Republic of Indonesia.
It should be noted that Samdech Hun Sen and Lok Chumteav led a high-level delegation from Cambodia to attend the 43rd ASEAN Summit and related summits in Jakarta from September 4 to 7, 2023.
The ASEAN Summit in Indonesia was held under the theme "ASEAN Importance: Core of Growth" and will focus on promoting the ASEAN Community Vision 2025, which provides an important roadmap for strengthening ASEAN influence through institutional enhancement. In order to seek benefits for its people on the international stage.
In addition, the discussions will focus on building an ASEAN community with a long-term vision and people-centeredness, which is a key force for achieving ASEAN 2045.
The Prime Ministers of Cambodia, Vietnam and Laos agree to complete the demarcation mechanism between the three countries in the near future and promote stronger cooperation (Video inside) (Indonesia): Samdech Hun Sen The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Mr. Pham Minh Chinh, Prime Minister of Vietnam and Mr. Son Sai Siphandon, Prime Minister of Laos agreed to continue to implement five points of cooperation for the benefit of the people of the three countries.
Among the five points, the leaders of the three countries also agreed to continue the demarcation mechanism between the three countries to be completed soon.
The consensus of the Prime Ministers of the three neighboring countries took place during a breakfast meeting and a tripartite working meeting in Jakarta, the capital of the Republic of Indonesia.
The breakfast meeting is a continuation of the tradition that the leaders of the three countries have always practiced before the opening of major regional summits.
In this meeting, the leaders of the three countries discussed and agreed on the following principles:
First, continue to maintain the tradition of having breakfast and discussing trilateral work before the opening of major regional summits, which have always benefited the three countries.
Second, continue to solve together and push to achieve results for the remaining issues.
Third, continue to implement the mechanism of demarcation between the three countries to complete soon.
Fourth, to continue the cooperation between the three countries in the socio-economic aspects, security, people-to-people links, culture and traditions.
Fifth, to further strengthen the relationship and connection between the three countries in all means, including infrastructure such as bridges, roads, railways and ports, supply chains, and tourism.
In this meeting, the Prime Minister of Vietnam sent greetings and condolences to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Chairman of the Supreme Council of the King and expressed his desire to meet with Samdech Techo in person at some point. Face.
The Prime Minister of Laos also invited His Majesty to pay an official visit to Laos in 2024.
