Pursat Governor Urges Parents and Residents to Awaken Their Children to Help Them Avoid Drugs
The provincial governor made this appeal on September 4, 2023 at Pursat High School on the International Day Against Drug Abuse, June 26, 2023, under the theme "Drug burning is the first step to help them grow." Health and Safety ”with nearly 2,000 participants.
Colonel Hem Mony, Deputy Commissioner of the Provincial Police Commissioner in charge of the Anti-Drug Work Plan, said that in 2022, the Anti-Drug Police of the Provincial Police Commission cracked down on 120 drug crimes and arrested 180 suspects and confiscated drugs. 293 packs of drugs, 162 pills, 8 drug scales, 6 cars, 25 motorcycles, 57 mobile phones, 57 small arms and some other criminal materials.
For legal action, 98 suspects were sent to prisons, 17 were sent to correctional centers and 65 were sent to basic education. All of these, compared to the capitals / provinces, see that the crime is light, small-scale and transit.
However, we continue to pay attention to the implementation of the Royal Government's Plan No. 01 to reduce the crime rate to a low level by implementing the slogan "Do not be involved, do not intervene, do not make exceptions and report" .
