Residents report that many species of wildlife are for sale on the sidewalk of Phsar Kon Damrey near O'Chrov Forestry Administration Sangkat
(Banteay Meanchey): According to reports from residents, many species of wild animals such as snakes, turtles, birds, etc. are for sale on the side of Kon Damrey Market, near Ochrov Forestry Administration Sangkat, located in Kon Damrey Village, Sangkat Nimit, Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province and Request to the competent authorities to prevent effectively.
Residents said that when they traveled along National Road 5 to Malai district at the point of the Elephant Market, they saw wild animals, dead snakes, birds, turtles and some other wild animals were sold regularly. Every evening, travelers passing through Poipet to Malai and Serei Sophorn are shopping for your favorite wildlife.
These snakes include rattlesnakes, rattlesnakes weighing 2 to 3 kilograms, some weighing 4 to 5 kilograms, while traders sell them for 30,000 to 50,000 riel per kilogram. The seller also buys from the people earning money by placing an hour.
Residents said that when he passed the Elephant Market, which sells wildlife such as dead snakes and birds that were killed and sold, he was saddened by the wildlife.
Citizens ask the officials of Banteay Meanchey Provincial Forestry Administration and Sangkat State Forestry District / Municipality to have rules to crack down on wildlife sellers at Ko Damrey Market, Poipet City to prevent wildlife crime and conservation and to stop wildlife sales. Banlung municipal authorities continue to instruct traders to stop selling on public roads in front of Banlung market before taking legal action
