The five guidelines set out by General Sar Thet during a meeting with the leadership of the General Commission of the National Police on the morning of September 5, 2023 include:
* First: to continue to work together as a group, have a strong internal unity to fulfill the roles and responsibilities in accordance with the skills, respect the hierarchy and relevant laws and regulations. In that, I would like to request all of you to provide support and close cooperation between the leadership and the police force under the supervision and between units and units for efficiency.
* Second, continue to promote the reform of the National Police Force by developing institutions and building human resources, paying close attention to the well-being of the police force, promoting the implementation of policies for retired police officers and the incapacity of disabled people due to causes. National security.
* Third: Continue to monitor and manage the forces accurately and regularly, both in terms of quantity, presence and memory to improve the efficiency and quality of work. In case of shortage of force or any force is difficult to report according to the hierarchy.
* Fourth, continue to strengthen the discipline of the police force to ensure the dignity, honor and morality of the National Police Force, along with efforts to strengthen the capacity, training, skills and technology. Information and digital to improve the maintenance of national security, order and social security in all circumstances.
* Fifth: Strengthen the efficiency and mode of work according to the competent skills and hierarchy, along with thinking, encouraging the police force that has done well and disciplining the police force that commits wrongdoing with accuracy and transparency.
At the same time, we must jointly protect the Royal Government for the 7th legislature of the National Assembly, which is the Royal Government formed in accordance with the will of the people.
