The political crisis in Myanmar has lasted for about three years. Myanmar's military leader has not been allowed to attend the ASEAN summit for three years. Russia proposes joint naval exercises with North Korea and China
SEOUL: Russia's defense minister has asked North Korean leader Kim Jong Un to hold joint naval exercises with China, according to South Korea's Yonhap news agency. Monday, September 4, 2023.
Yonhap reported that Shoigu made a request for a trilateral naval exercise to Kim during his visit, but gave no details.
The agency also reported that South Korea's National Intelligence Service informed the National Assembly that Shoigu had actually met privately with Kim to approve a large-scale military expansion.
Russia and North Korea have recently called for closer military ties, but North Korea has rejected any "arms deal" with Russia.
The United States has recently sanctioned three entities it accuses of having links to an arms deal between North Korea and Russia.
North Korea has conducted six nuclear tests since 2006 and has been testing several missiles in recent years, but has rarely held military exercises with neighboring countries.
The United States and its ally South Korea hold regular military exercises that North Korea has denounced as preparations for war.
