New Delhi: India has increased the use of coal to generate electricity in order to stop power outages due to low hydropower and to meet demand. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Monday, September 4, 2023.
In general, electricity consumption in India increased significantly during the dry months of May. It is not uncommon for India to have high demand for electricity in August, which usually has an annual monsoon between June and September. However, in August 2023, the dry weather caused the power generation to reach a record 162.7 billion kilowatt hours.
Coal consumption in India rose to 66.7 percent in August, the highest level in six years.
Low rainfall has reduced India's total hydropower output by 14.8 percent from 18.1 percent in the same period in 2022. Minister Chhay Rithy Sen Inspects 2 Water Supply Sources and 1 Pump Well in Phnom Sruoch District, Kampong Speu Province
(Kampong Speu): Mr. Chhay Rithy Sen, Minister of Rural Development, on September 4, 2023, led a delegation and technical officers of the Ministry and attended by Mr. Kao Sovanrith, Deputy Governor of Kampong Speu Province and relevant officials to inspect water supply sources. For use at 2 locations and 1 Aridephe pump well located in Phnom Sruoch district, Kampong Speu province.
Location 1: Water distribution system through a small community pipeline in Doung village, Choam Sangke commune, using both electricity and sunlight, with a capacity to produce a maximum of 200 cubic meters of clean water per day. Currently, the water distribution system has 182 houses out of a total of 401 houses in Doung and Seila villages.
Location 2: Community pond located in Sre Chrov village, Taing Samrong commune, with a maximum capacity of 40 cubic meters of clean water during the day using solar energy.
Location 3: Afridef pump well in Damnak Trach Primary School, Dambok Rong commune for students to use.
The Minister instructed and instructed the technical officers and officers of the Department of Rural Development, authorities at all levels to strive to maintain all these achievements so that people can use them for a long time and continue to sustain the water supply to the people.
In the afternoon of the same day, Mr. Chhay Rithi Sen and his accompanying delegation met and greeted the leaders and civil servants of the Department of Rural Development of Kampong Speu Province.
After listening to the detailed welcome report of the Director of the Department, the Minister expressed his appreciation and appreciation for the efforts of the leaders and civil servants of the Department of Rural Development and provided the following guidelines and recommendations:
1. Continue to strive to participate in the implementation of rural development to improve the value of life of rural people in a comprehensive environment, both economically, socially and culturally, in line with the vision and strategy of the Royal Government of the 7th legislature.
3. Respect the rules and regulations of the meeting system, monitor and inspect the monthly, quarterly, semi-regular meetings to jointly address the requests of the people.
4. Prepare the annual summary report and work direction for the next year, which the Ministry of Rural Development plans to prepare on December 22, 2023.
