(Kampong Cham): Mr. Un Chanda, President of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Kampong Cham Province and his colleagues and monks on the morning of September 4, 2023, handed over the 15th and 16th humanitarian houses at two different locations. There are 2 poor families, 1 family in Kokor 2 village, Kokor commune, Kampong Siem district and another family in Anlong Okkeut village, Sokong commune, Kang Meas district.
The second family: Lum Srey Touch, a resident of Anlong Akkeut village, So Kong commune, Kang Meas district, is a blind widow with a 3-year-old daughter, living on the generosity of neighbors, with the support of the commune and village authorities. Help from the Royal Government through the Equity Card 1. And this poor widow has only a small hut on the ground that the commune administration provides on a plot of land measuring 8 meters by 12 meters in the above village.
At the same time, to help ease the living standard, Mr. Un Chanda provided food items to both families for this new house, each family received 50 kg of rice, 20 cans of fish, 12 bottles of fish sauce, 12 bottles of soy sauce. , 2 boxes of noodles, 2 kits for 12 T-shirts, soap, some kitchen equipment and a budget of 200,000 riels.
Separately, grandparents who witnessed the handover ceremony of the two new houses, each received rice, fish, noodles, fish sauce, soy sauce, soap, T-shirt and 20,000 Riels.
