The following is the press release of Angkor Institute: Cambodian Youth Movement Association, Group 157 and philanthropists bring donations to students of Poisonous Crocodile Primary School in Rolea Bier District
(Kampong Chhnang): A lot of study materials and food items were distributed by 100 students of the Cambodian Youth Movement Association, Group 157 in Kampong Chhnang Province and 100 students at Krapeul Poul Primary School in Krapeul Poul Village, Kraing Dey Meas Commune, Rolea Bier District. In the morning of September 3, 2023.
Mr. Soy Phoury, a philanthropist who has always been involved in humanitarian work with various organizations in Kampong Chhnang province, said that after he received the news that at the Poor Crocodile Primary School, the students were in need, he decided to cook a healthy meal. Soup, curry, bread and buy school supplies to give to students now, and this is not the first time, it is done every year.
After the dispute was over, the 157 Cambodian Youth Movement Association, which took place at the time, turned its attention back to humanitarian activities, and this humanitarian activity was everywhere to help the people, orphans, the elderly and the homeless. People face accidents and other natural disasters.
Mr. Phon Seiha, Deputy Governor of Rolea Bier District, expressed his gratitude to the Cambodian Youth Movement Association Group 157 and all the benefactors who have worked in the past to do humanitarian work in Rolea Bier District as well as in Kampong Chhnang Province. At the Poisonous Crocodile Primary School, they received school supplies and ate delicious food in a very happy and friendly atmosphere.
