Cambodia seeks Japanese assistance for three additional projects related to water resources and meteorological development (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Through its commitment to continue cooperation in water resources and meteorology, the Cambodian side requested Japan to assist Three more projects to promote the water resources and meteorology sector for the present and future.
It should be noted that under the cooperation between Cambodia and Japan, the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology is in the process of implementing the National Irrigation Standards Development Project, which started in 2022 and was completed in 2024, and the Irrigation and Irrigation Rehabilitation Project. Southwest of Phnom Penh, which started construction in 2023 and completed in 2026.
During the meeting, the Cambodian side requested the Japanese side:
Second. Provide heavy machinery for the construction and repair of irrigation systems and for intervention in the event of natural disasters such as floods and droughts.
Third. Help train more technical officers on water resources management and development.
At the same time, the Japanese side also requested the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology to hold a groundbreaking ceremony for a project to rehabilitate Phnom Penh's southwest irrigation and drainage system (CP-P14) to present new achievements of cooperation. Between Cambodia and Japan of the Royal Government of Cambodia, the 7th legislature of the National Assembly.
The Cambodian and Japanese sides have expressed their high commitment to further enhance cooperation in the field of water resources to make the sector more prosperous for the present and future.
It should be reminded that 2023 is the 70th anniversary of diplomatic relations between Cambodia and Japan. Since 1953, the two countries have built a trusting and strong relationship through cooperation during the peace process and the period of national reconstruction in Cambodia. The level of bilateral relations between the two countries has risen from a strategic partnership in 2013 to a comprehensive strategic partnership in 2023.
