Peamrok police said that a buffalo chased people, injuring three people.
First, Nguyen Young Wei, a 69-year-old Vietnamese man, suffered a cut on his left forearm. Second: Lu Bun Nhe, a 58-year-old Vietnamese man, suffered a broken left buttock, a broken arm and a child. Left leg. Third: Kim Phuong, male, 62 years old, Vietnamese, injured left arm. All three of them live in Village 5, Prek Khsay Commune (B), Peam Ro District, Prey Veng Province.
Authorities confirmed that prior to the incident, a buffalo named Ana (ownerless Anatha) came to chase the victim who was exercising and drinking coffee at the house of a person named Tabi, causing a surprise.
Two of the victims' relatives are currently being treated at Neak Leung Referral Hospital, and one of the victims was sent to Vietnam for treatment of buffaloes after being chased by villagers and fled into the forest of the former Banteay Abi. Surrounded.
Authorities also appealed to people raising livestock not to release cattle in the open, which could lead to traffic accidents as well as harm to local people as it climbed.
