MADRID (Reuters) - Several subways in Madrid and high-speed trains connecting to the southern cities were closed Monday morning and two men went missing after heavy rains hit central Spain. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Monday, September 4, 2023.
Rain continued to fall in most parts of Spain, but the National Meteorological Agency on Monday lowered the orange alert level to yellow. A union supports the government in speeding up wages for workers and improving transportation
(Phnom Penh): The President of the National Union Coalition, Mr. Fasali, expressed his support for the recommendation of the Prime Minister of Cambodia, His Excellency Hun Manet, on speeding up wage negotiations and adjusting the transportation of workers.
This support was made after His Excellency Hun Manet on August 29, 2023 in Prey Speu, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh, instructed the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training to make good efforts to facilitate the discussion of the minimum wage based on Scientific characteristics and criteria set out in the law on the minimum wage before the upcoming Pchum Ben holiday.
Mr. Fasali said he was happy to expedite the workers' pay raise meeting because it was a positive message for workers waiting for news of wage negotiations.
"However, although Cambodia is affected by the global economic order, the government has also tried to increase the wages of workers, more or less," he said.
At the same time, His Excellency Hun Manet also instructed the Ministry of Labor to cooperate with stakeholders to study mechanisms to support and encourage the gradual change of means of transportation of workers in accordance with technical standards and more comfortable by 2027. .
At this point, Mr. Ban Fasali believes that at present, the movement of workers is still a big problem, not a small one, each car is loaded with up to 70 workers, and the driver of the car does not obey the traffic rules. Although officials from the Ministry of Labor and unions explain and guide them.
"I would like to encourage car drivers to go back to driving lessons and, secondly, to check for drivers who use drugs, which is detrimental to the safety of workers," he said.
The union president also called on the government to provide buses to transport workers to provinces across the country to ensure the safety of workers' travel.
Please be informed that on September 4, 2023, the National Minimum Wage Council continued its third meeting to discuss the minimum wage in textiles, garments, footwear and travel products and bags for 2024.
The third minimum wage negotiation meeting was chaired by Mr. Heng Sour, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, and was attended by unions representing workers, employers and the government.
According to a press release from the Ministry of Labor, as a result, representatives of the workers 'side raised the figure by 215 US dollars and representatives of the employers' party raised the figure by 201 US dollars.
The meeting also agreed to resume the talks on September 11, 2023.
The minister said that the ministry will strive to release the minimum wage figure for 2024 before Pchum Ben to facilitate the lives of workers.
