To date, PSE provides education and vocational training and food to more than 6,000 poor students while trying to raise funds to continue their activities.
(Phnom Penh): Founded in 1996, the Organization for the Smile of Children (PSE), an organization that helps orphans and the poor, has been providing vocational education and training and providing food to more than 6,000 poor students. The organization is also trying to raise funds to continue its activities. The main mission of this organization is to help children get out of misery towards a career.
Ms. Leakena, Director of the Organization for the Smile of Children, said that this is an NGO that was established in 1996 with the aim of helping children, youth and poor families in Phnom Penh, Sihanoukville and Siem Reap, focusing on providing Food, treatment, protection and accommodation, general education, vocational training, family support and facilitation to find a suitable job for them.
"Today, the organization is providing education and vocational training and providing food to 6,500 poor students in Phnom Penh and other public schools in Phnom Penh, Sihanoukville and Siem Reap," she said. About 4,500 students have graduated and are working in the job market. I myself am also an alumnus of the organization for the smile of a child.
In response to the needs of the organization for the smiles of children as well as all children, in March, the management of the organization for the smiles of children launched two fundraising campaigns: the Food Supply Aid Campaign and the Campaign. Find study materials.
She thanked for the support from many major partners in Cambodia, including Hanuman Beverage Company, Okulen Pure Water Company, Westline Education Group, Lihua Lixing Company, Talias Company, Forte Insurance Company, Sofitel Phnom Penh Hospital and Hospital. Cambodia who helped for the charity birthday night event.
