UPDATE: Tomorrow, the court will hear the case of the criminals who detained the Chinese hostage for up to 10 million dollars for "illegal detention, torture to extort money and possession of weapons without permission"
(Phnom Penh): The Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court has already investigated the criminals who detained the Chinese hostage for up to 10 million dollars for "illegally detaining people, torturing them to extort money And Possession of Weapons Without Permission ”The case will be heard on September 5, 2023 tomorrow.
The victims expressed hope that the court would help them find justice.
Please be informed that the representative of the Phnom Penh Municipal Prosecutor's Office has decided to formally charge 5 Chinese criminals who detained a Chinese man for extorting up to 10 million dollars for "illegally detaining people "Torture to extort money and possess weapons without permission."
Speaking to Fresh News on the evening of April 19, 2023, Mr. Plang Sophal, Spokesman for the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, stated, "Illegal torture to extort money and possession of weapons without permission."
The five Chinese criminals were arrested in connection with the same Chinese detention case for extorting about $ 10 million at the Sky Villa building in Sangkat Veal Vong, Khan 7 Makara, Phnom Penh.
