When questioned, one of the suspects, Kong Vannak, said that he and his accomplices actually threw stones at the victim's motorbike, causing it to break. Another suspect, Chham Vanda, alias Boom, denied that he had thrown stones at the victim's motorcycle, but had been drinking with the suspects and driving to the scene.
At the invitation of the Cambodian People's Party, Mr. Li Jianchao, Minister of International Relations of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China, led a delegation to visit the Kingdom of Cambodia from September 3 to 4, 2023.
During the visit, Mr. Liu Cheanchao paid a courtesy call on Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) and Samdech Moha Bovathi Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Youth Chairman of the Central Cambodian People's Party (CPP). Mr. Prak Sokhon, Member of the Standing Committee of the Central Committee and Chairman of the Foreign Relations Committee.
Discussions focused on a number of mutually beneficial bilateral issues, including the post-election situation in Cambodia, the celebration of the 65th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations and the year of Cambodia-China friendship and inter-party cooperation. Hold both powers.
On the occasion of the 65th Anniversary of Diplomatic Relations and the Year of Cambodia-China Friendship, the two sides discussed action plans to further promote multifaceted cooperation, including political relations, diplomacy, trade expansion, investment facilitation. Promoting tourism, exchanges in education, infrastructure development and security cooperation.
Liu Jianchao reaffirmed China's unwavering commitment to respecting Cambodia's sovereignty and brought the full support of Xi Jinping to the CPP-led government. Select the development path in accordance with the national conditions of Cambodia.
The Cambodian People's Party (CPP) has reaffirmed its strong commitment to continue to strengthen and expand cooperation to build a high-quality, high-standard and high-standard Cambodian-Chinese community of common destiny, as well as to enhance the framework for diamond cooperation. In the mutual interest of the party, the country and the people.
The Cambodian People's Party (CPP) is deeply grateful for China's support and development assistance, including the provision of the Kovid-19 vaccine and scholarships, which have made significant contributions to Cambodia's socio-economic and infrastructure development. Helped to strengthen nation building and contribute to poverty reduction.
Both parties expressed satisfaction over the strong and dynamic momentum of the strategic partnership in all aspects of cooperation between the two countries for prosperity, peace and development in all fields.
Both parties are committed to enhancing relations at all levels, especially mass organizations and youth, as well as working together to make the "Youth House for Cambodia-China Friendship" project work better.
Both parties praised the consistent implementation of the Memorandum of Understanding on Cooperation and Exchange between the two parties, which was signed under the chairmanship of Samdech Techo, President of the party.
The two parties are committed to continuing communication, exchange visits and mutual support in regional and international forums. Neak Oknha Kith Meng Leads a Delegation of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce to Accompany Hun Manet to the 43rd ASEAN Summit and Related Summits in Indonesia
