(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pheav Sovuthy, Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Environment, said that Cambodia is a country vulnerable to climate change and Cambodia has often been affected by floods, droughts and typhoons.
Mr. Pheav Sovuthy made this remark during a seminar on "Building Media-Journalist Relations on Climate Change" on August 4, 2023, Cambodiana Hotel, Phnom Penh.
At this point, a senior official of the Ministry of Environment added that Cambodia's main priority is to build resilience in the economic and social sectors to reduce the impact of climate change on health, infrastructure and agricultural productivity.
He said that since 2000, the Royal Government of Cambodia has taken care and taken the lead in implementing climate change adaptation measures and has made great progress in organizing activities and plans to address climate change.
In fact, climate change is being integrated into the first phase of the National Strategic Development Plan (NSDP), National Strategic Plan and Action Plan (NESAP) 2016-2023, and other relevant development strategies and policies. Include climate change in development plans and budgets at both the national and sub-national levels.
