Minister Eang Sophalleth Urges People to Plant Trees, Reforest to Increase Forest Cover and Increase Income through Carbon Sales
(Koh Kong): Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Minister of Environment, urged people to plant trees, restore forests and participate in forest conservation to increase forest cover and sell carbon to increase income in the community.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth said this during a visit to the community of Ta Tai Krom Protected Area on Sunday morning, September 3, 2023.
The head of the Tatai Krom Protected Area Community, Mr. Tep Mala, asserted that the community was involved in protecting and conserving natural resources without further deforestation or deforestation. The area is attracting a lot of national and international tourists to visit natural resources, including waterfalls, scenic canals, ancient villages and boating, and the community is earning income through eco-tourism.
But with the support of tourists on natural resources, roads, parking lots, water and information centers for tourists is also a need for further development of the community.
At the same time, Mr. Eang Sophalleth said that in order to ensure the sustainability of the environment and the livelihood of the community, the community must plant more trees because trees are a source of income by generating income from carbon sales and sales revenue. Bon will help develop infrastructure and give people more income than today through tourism.
It should be recalled that the promotion of tree planting so that communities can earn income from the sale of carbon is a strategy of the Ministry of Environment, which implements the first phase of the Royal Government of Cambodia's Pentagon strategy in the five strategic goals. The first point is to ensure economic growth at an average annual rate of around 7% with resilience and crisis.
It should be noted that the community of Ta Tai Krom Protected Area is officially recognized by the Ministry of Environment according to Prakas No. 290 dated 19 July 2023 and has 177 families living in Anlong Vak village and Koh Andet village, Ta Tai Krom commune, Koh Kong district. Natural potentials such as forests, mangroves, waterfalls, canals, ancient villages, as well as sea fishing are attracting tourists.
