ASEAN Secretary-General delivers welcoming speech at ASEAN Business and Investment Summit
On the morning of Sunday, September 3, 2023, in Jakarta, Republic of Indonesia, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Secretary-General of ASEAN, delivered a welcome address at the ASEAN Business and Investment Summit.
On that occasion, the ASEAN Secretary-General encouraged greater participation from the private sector in the business community to make ASEAN economic growth more sustainable and inclusive, as well as provide opportunities for all businesses, small and large.
On the same Sunday morning, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn also attended the 23rd ASEAN Economic Community Council Meeting. The meeting focused on the review of progress in the implementation of the ASEAN Economic Community 2025 Roadmap, discussing the achievements of 2023 economic priorities under the leadership of Indonesia, as well as initiatives related to sustainability and digital transformation. .
This is the first time that the ASEAN Economic Community (AEC) Meeting has held a special closed session before the Plenary Session on the post-2025 AEC agenda.
On Sunday afternoon, September 3, 2023, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Secretary-General of ASEAN, attended the launching ceremony of the ASEAN Digital Economic Framework (DEFA) Negotiations on the occasion of the 23rd ASEAN Economic Community Council Meeting. The main purpose of DEFA is to enhance the digital transformation in ASEAN supported by modern technology.
The two sides discussed efforts to strengthen the ASEAN Dialogue Partnership with the United Arab Emirates, as well as possible cooperation under the economic pillars, especially in the areas of trade and investment.
