Khmer Civilization Expert: How does the awarding of the title "Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet" reflect the Khmer tradition?
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia is the territory of the ancient empire in our Southeast Asia and has a rich civilization that makes the world very respectful.
How does the conferment of the title "Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet" reflect the Khmer tradition?
Thus, for the title "Samdech Moha Bovar Dhipati" means: * Moha Moha Prasert * Bovor is a golden song of the warlord *, and the word "Samdech Moha Bovar Dhipati" means that for the title "Samdech Moha Bovar Dhipati" is one of the highest ranks. In the time of the Angkorian Empire, those who had sufficient qualifications and ability to rule the war went to all parts of the country to protect the great peace.
Mr. Rath heard that the bestowal of the highest honors is a reward for the patriotic spirit that has worked hard to protect and build a prosperous nation to preserve for future generations. Which is a beautiful tradition of our Khmer people since ancient times.
On the other hand, in the Angkorian period, when it comes to warlords, the title of "Great General of the War" was one of the great generals who served during the reign of King Udaya Titvarman II in 1050-1066 and also wrote a memorial. To the story that his ancestors, who sacrificed everything to serve the nation since the reign of Jayavarman II, was the first king of the Angkor Empire in 802.
Therefore, for the honor of "Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet" in modern times, it is an honor that connects the past, the present and the future in the management of war in all parts of Cambodia to maintain peace, harmony and development of the whole nation. To be even more beautiful.
