(Phnom Penh): Two separate cases of gangsters stabbing and intimidating people in Sangkat Boeung Tumpun I, Khan Meanchey and Khan Por Sen Chey were investigated by the Phnom Penh Municipal Police and led to a series of crackdowns. .
Speaking to Fresh News on September 2, 2023, Major General Chuon Narin, Deputy Commissioner General and Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner, said that the crackdown took place in two different cases, including:
Case 1: On August 31, 2023, the competent authorities of Meanchey District Police Inspectorate conducted a search and arrested 4 suspects in connection with a case of intentional violence (using a machete, a stone, cutting and beating) at 12 Beta Street Group 4, Sansom Kosal 4 Village, Sangkat Boeung Tumpun I, Khan Meanchey, Phnom Penh, on August 30, 2023.
Four suspects were arrested: First, Sem Ponleu, living in a rented house in Kampoul Meas village, Sangkat Dangkor, Khan Dangkor, student occupation, Second: Phon Soeng, living in a house with no number, Sonsom Kosal 1 village, Sangkat Boeung Tumpun I, Khan Meanchey, student , 3: Sam Ang Reaksa, living in a house with no number, Sonsom Kosal 3 village, Sangkat Boeung Tumpun I, Khan Meanchey, Occupation: Student
Case 2: Violence, vandalism of other people's property on public roads (using stones and helmets) on September 1, 2023 at Prey Chisak village, Sangkat Choam Chao 3, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
The first suspect: Chhem Sa, 23 years old, living in a rented room in Prey Pring North Village, Sangkat Choam Chao III, Khan Por Sen Chey, the second suspect: Horn Visal, 17 years old, working in a rented room in Prey Pring North Village One, Sangkat Choam Chao III, Khan Por Sen Chey. The victim is Kim Veasna, 23 years old, living in Prey Chisak village, Sangkat Choam Chao III, Khan Por Sen Chey. The victim's motorcycle was damaged and the victim was not injured.
The two suspects are currently building a case to send to court.
