(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ieng Sotheara, a Buddhist trader and a well-known businessman in Cambodia, shared three tips to keep the enterprise stable even in difficult circumstances.
The three tips include:
First, the fitness or intellect: as a businessman or owner of an enterprise, only the intellect to solve on the right path. Wisdom comes from listening, learning, and so on. After all, this intelligence is different from studying for a degree. Having a degree but no intelligence will not solve the problem.
Second: Fitness or cash: The current problem of some companies or some employees is only assets (houses or land) but can not be used because all those assets are related to the sale or bank. Therefore, business owners need to strengthen their ability to cope with problems and spend properly.
3: Solidarity means that in the company must have understanding, work together, love each other, regardless of position, that makes the company run smoothly.
Ieng Sotheara's speech was made at the Cambodia-Japan Business and Investment Association (CJBI) Network Meeting 2023, during which many business people discussed issues facing small and medium enterprises to overcome. Challenge and seize opportunities to strengthen more business owners.
