Plastic bags are a worrying issue that is spreading around the world. Every year, 300 million tons of plastic waste are generated and take 1,000 years to decompose. This problem is also happening in Cambodia. Population growth and rapid economic growth have led to a significant increase in the amount of waste. In Phnom Penh, more than 3,500 tonnes of waste is generated daily, of which 20 percent is plastic.
