Phnom Penh Municipal Commissioner Conducts First Meeting to Strengthen Prevention of Robbery, Robbery and Gangs and Prohibit Traffic Police Officers from Hiding and Intercepting Citizens
(Phnom Penh): Major General Chuon Narin, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police and the newly-appointed Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner, chaired the first meeting to strengthen the main work to prevent and suppress criminal offenses, robberies and gangs. And traffic order work.
In a meeting held on the morning of September 2, 2023 at the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, Major General Chuon Narin forbade traffic police officers from hiding and intercepting people traveling on the streets, which is the main task. The Commissioner must take care to maintain security, maintain order and bring safety to the people with warmth and trust in the leadership of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Deputy General Commissioner of the National Police and Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner raised the issue of crime prevention by urging the 14 Khan Criminal Police Force and the Criminal Expert Office to pay more attention to the prevention of theft. Robbery and gangs are crimes that scare people.
Regarding the traffic order work, Major General Chuon Narin also introduced to the Deputy Commissioner for Traffic Order and the Director of the Office of Traffic Order and Traffic, the Deputy Inspector General, the Chief of Traffic Order of the 14 Khan Police Inspectorates. In order to enforce traffic laws, it is necessary to eliminate theft, ambush and arrest people traveling on the streets.
He claimed that the hiding of people was a phenomenon that has a negative impact on the national police force and especially advised traffic police officers to strictly prohibit the use of violence against people and to use gentle verbal gestures. To the people and be serious about their duties. Citizens, on the other hand, should adhere to the law rather than fear the authorities' fines.
He stressed that traffic police officers must change their attitude in performing their duties by using gentle, disciplined behavior in law enforcement and must stop any activities that adversely affect law enforcement and eliminate negativity. Everything that has ever happened has led to criticism from the people.
It should be noted that the meeting was held for one separate day in the morning of the same day, the Commissioner chaired the meeting with the Deputy Commissioner for Criminal Affairs, Mr. and Mrs. Deputy Chief of the Office of Criminal Affairs, Mr. Criminal skills in the 14 district police inspectorates.
