Leakage of Almonia gas pipe at "Chheang Mu" ice factory in Russey Keo district, injuring 23 people
(Phnom Penh): On the night of September 1, 2023, there was a case of leaking ammonia gas pipe in the ice factory of "Mrs. Chheang Mu" brand, located on Concrete Road, Group 5, Village K1, Sangkat Chrang Chamres II, Khan Russey Keo Phnom Penh.
According to a report by Major General Chuon Narin, Deputy Commissioner General and Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner, the owner of the location, Chheang Por, 56, was at the scene.
In this incident, affecting the health of 23 people living near the scene, 17 women were sent to Calmette Hospital and Samdech Ov Samdech Mey Referral Hospital. Among them, 4 Calmette Hospital, 3 women (severe condition) and Samdech Ov Samdech Mey Referral Hospital, 19 patients (mild condition). Doctors are now rescuing and treating.
On the morning of September 2, 2023, Mr. Ek Khun Doeun, Governor of Russey Keo District, led professional officers and authorities to inspect the location of the original ice and sanitary ice factory and make notes with the owners of the above locations, including:
* The owner of the site is looking for another water plant location without allowing it to be near the people. * The owner of the location must pay for the treatment of the victim who is being treated at the hospital.
After the inspection, the relevant authorities decided to temporarily suspend the location of the original ice and sanitary ice factory for the owner to prepare and meet the technical standards of the technical officials. Campaign to give equity cards to individuals working in tourism services continues in Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province
(Banteay Meanchey): The inter-ministerial working group, including the National Council for Social Protection, the Ministry of Planning, and relevant authorities, jointly disseminated and continued the campaign to give equity cards to individuals working in the informal economy tourism services. Life difficulties in Poipet city, Banteay Meanchey province.
The Equity Card Campaign for Individuals in Tourism Services was held on September 1, 2023, led by Dr. John Narith, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Economy and Finance and Secretary General of the National Council for Social Protection. Leaders of the Ministry of Planning and representatives of other relevant institutions.
The campaign aims to give individuals working in the informal economy tourism services, especially women working in bars, discos, karaoke, beer gardens, massage parlors and spas, access health care coverage. Free of charge at public health facilities and other social protection benefits from the Royal Government based on the principle of "do not abandon any citizen".
Mr. Theng Panhathorn, Government Delegate in charge of Planning Director of the Ministry of Planning, said that this is the second campaign organized by Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province, organized by the Inter-Institutional Working Group, the first at Wat Phnom. Phnom Penh. The decision to campaign in Poipet was due to the significant number of employees in the entertainment industry.
He said that for those who came to be interviewed in this campaign, they immediately received a card to receive free medical treatment at public hospitals. However, for those who are busy and do not come to the interview can also be done in the commune to interview for this card. At the same time, he confirmed that for those who are already named in the equity card can not come once No more.
In order to receive health services, individuals working in the tourism sector of the informal economy must use public health facilities, following the system of providing services from primary to lower health facilities to higher health facilities, except in emergencies.
