According to the AFP news agency, on Friday, September 1, 2023, King Bhumibol Adulyadej decided to commute the sentence of former Thai Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra. Eight years in prison, only one year.
The commutation comes after the 74-year-old former Thai leader formally filed for a royal pardon on Thursday. The statement said the former Thai prime minister had confessed to his crimes and expressed deep regret. The statement also said Thaksin was ill.
Thaksin has been sentenced to eight years in prison for abuse of power and conflicts of interest after returning to Thailand last week after a 15-year exile. Thaksin served as Thai Prime Minister from 2001 to 2006.
Thaksin returned to his home country on August 22 and reunited with his family shortly afterwards, was taken to court by police and sent to prison.
Before returning home on August 5, Thaksin and his sister Yingluck flew to celebrate Hun Sen's birthday in Takhmao City, Kandal Province.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Thaksin have been close brothers since 1992, before Thaksin became Thai Prime Minister.
