(Phnom Penh): At the invitation of Mr. Ngo Van Tuan, Auditor General of the State Audit Office of Vietnam, Dr. Som Kim Sour, Auditor General of the National Audit Authority, led a delegation of the National Audit Authority to attend the 10th Tripartite Meeting and Relevant meeting between the audit institutions of Cambodia, Laos and Vietnam from 27 to 31 August 2023 in Da Nang, Vietnam.
The meeting proceeded with the intervention on the progress after the 9th tripartite meeting, especially the update on the achievements of each institution and the audit of tax revenue through information technology, with the meeting highly appreciating the results of this audit. And the contribution of each audit body to the development of the policy framework, in particular the revenue collection strategy of each country.
The three parties discussed and shared their experiences on conducting audit work in a new normal way, focusing on:
1: General situation in preventing Kovid-19 to maintain socio-economic resilience 2: The process of carrying out audit work in the new normal trajectory 3: Achievements achieved during the crisis 4: Challenges faced and 5 : Solutions and directions.
The 10th Tripartite Meeting raised the topic of "Monitoring the Implementation of Audit Recommendations" for discussion and sharing, focusing on:
1: Legal framework and mandate of the institution on monitoring the implementation of audit recommendations 2: Standards, guidelines and procedures for monitoring the implementation of audit recommendations 3: Practice, challenges and further directions to improve monitoring recommendations Audit to bring the highest benefits for the development of the country by strengthening transparency, accountability, efficiency and effectiveness of the use of public resources.
In addition, a delegation of the top three audit institutions, Cambodia, Laos and Vietnam, paid a working visit and met with HE Chairman of the People's Council and leaders of Da Nang.
The meeting also praised the Vietnamese side for successfully hosting the 10th Tripartite Meeting and related meetings, and said that the meeting was not just a forum for sharing knowledge, know-how and relevant work experience. In the field of public audit between the three institutions, it has also contributed to strengthening, expanding and promoting the bonds of solidarity, friendship and cooperation between the three countries.
