* Security related: Positive consequences for managing and reducing risks related to aviation security (illegal interference activities).
* Socially relevant: created 1,400 direct, professional and approximately 600 indirect jobs for the initial phase.
* Economically relevant: By complying with ICAO and IATA standards and requirements, Cambodia will gain opportunities and advantages to attract new airlines and increase passenger and freight flights, including Tourism, business and trust activities in line with the five mottos of the Royal Government's Pentagon Strategy of the Seventh Mandate, including growth, employment, equity, efficiency and sustainability.
