(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC), through commune councils and village chiefs across the country, has begun issuing invitations to 2022 official voter lists to serve as a review of the voter list and Register to vote in 2023.
According to the NEC, the issuance of invitations in villages in communes is for 30 days from September 1 to September 30, 2023.
The purpose of issuing this invitation is to inform the citizens whose names are on the voter list as follows:
* Citizens whose names are on the official voter list in 2022 and who have used an expired Khmer Nationality (AK) ID card or identification document used to provide past voter registration to verify and update voter list data. According to the AEC, which was valid during the 2023 voter list review and registration
* Citizens whose names are on the official voter list in 2022 and who have used the valid AK in the past voter registration to verify their names and data on the voter list if they find that there is an incorrect record. According to the valid AK, corrections can be requested during the 2023 voter list review and registration.
