Mr. Vy Samnang said that on the occasion of the National Independence Day on November 9, the provincial administration requested the commutation of the sentences of 12 prisoners (no women) on the occasion of the Water Festival, worshiping the moon, Ok Ambok and floating lanterns on November 26. In 2023, 9 people (3 women) applied and on the occasion of January 7, 2024 Victory Day, 5 people (no women).
The provincial governor confirmed that of the 26 prisoners, the sentences were commuted from three months and one of them was pardoned.
The governor of Kampong Speu province said that requests for commutation and pardon for prisoners serving their sentences in Kampong Speu Provincial Prison are always made every year.
With the pardon conditions, 25 prisoners were asked to be pardoned from 3 to 6 months and one prisoner was asked to be pardoned.
