(Phnom Penh): As planned, on the morning of September 1, 2023, Mr. Keo Rattanak, Minister of Mines and Energy, will preside over the inauguration ceremony of the new Director General of Electricite du Cambodge, Mr. Prang Chulsa. The King issued a recent Royal Decree appointing him.
The inauguration ceremony was attended by dignitaries and leaders from the Ministry of Mines and Energy, the Ministry of Economy and Finance, the Electricity Authority of Cambodia and Electricite du Cambodge. The ceremony will be held at the office of Electricite du Cambodge.
Please be reminded that the new General Director of Electricite du Cambodge, Mr. Prang Chulsa, was born in 1974 in Phnom Penh. After the genocidal regime of Pol Pot was overthrown, he returned from a four-year evacuation to Phnom Penh, attended Russey Keo School and graduated from Phnom Penh Daun Penh School in 1990.
Mr. Prang Chulsa continued his studies at the Cambodia-Soviet Friendship High Technical Institute through a rigorous examination and graduated in 1995 with a degree in Electrical Engineering.
He also received training in political education for young people, Level 1 in the 25th generation and Level 2 in the first generation at the CPP headquarters.
Mr. Prang Chulsa joined EDC in 1996 and has been working consistently since the beginning of 2001 after graduating from France.
He continued to work in various ranks, from ordinary officers until he was appointed as the Director General of Electricite du Cambodge on August 25, 2023, with experience as a leading technician in solving various tasks as well as urgent challenges, as well as A long-term strategy, focusing on the national interest and building the electricity system, including cooperation with foreign institutions, brings fruits of national pride.
In addition to his professional work, Mr. Prang Chulsa has always been actively involved in social, humanitarian and political work in support of the Royal Government's policies, which have achieved remarkable results. Leading officials at all levels in the energy sector as well as the general public, especially directly from Mr. Keo Rattanak and Mr. Suy Sem.
