Articles and photos by Cambodia-China Friendship Radio General Knowledge: Used to hear the Silk Road on land, now know the Silk Road
(Phnom Penh): The Silk Road is a network of ancient trade routes that first flourished from 100 BC to 1500 AD. The silk trade extends from eastern China to Central Asia, the Middle East and the Mediterranean. This is the Silk Road on land, but there is still the Silk Road.
The Silk Road refers to the ancient trade route between the East and the West, and is also associated with the Silk Road trade route on land. Unlike the Silk Road on land, the Silk Road on the sea trades a wide variety of goods. In addition to silk fabrics, porcelain, incense, and tea are also the most traded commodities, so the Sea Silk Road is also known as the Porcelain Road or the Perfume Road.
After the 16th century, with the arrival of Europeans, the Pacific Silk Road was established and became a trade route from China to the Philippines and then across the Pacific Ocean to the Americas.
