Recently, at a location in the South China Sea, Chinese anti-submarine patrol aircraft flew non-stop flights for more than 40 hours, focusing on the East China Sea Command, the Chinese military said in a statement. Find out the presence of submarines and rehearse as if launching an attack on them.
The Chinese military said the drills helped refine anti-submarine capabilities in the air, and that drills were held late at night and low-light to enhance the operation experience at different times. However, the statement did not say whether any non-Chinese submarines had been found in the area.
The exercise is one of a number of similar exercises held this year and is part of a broader military exercise by the Chinese military in the Indo-Pacific region. The United States and its allies have also increased their military activities, especially in the South China Sea, where China has territorial disputes with other countries bordering the sea.
