General knowledge: When did the first Silk Road come into being?
(World): The Chinese were the first to produce silk and also became the only source of silk products to Central Asia, the Middle East and Europe. Do you know when the first silk business started and when it ended?
The Silk Road was an ancient trade network that first flourished from 100 BC to 1500 AD. It is famous for its large number of silks, which are exported from China via long distances to many regions.
The silk trade stretches for more than 8,000 kilometers through the highlands, mountains, deserts, rivers, seas and cities from eastern China to Central Asia, the Middle East and the Mediterranean.
By 800 CE, the Silk Road began to decline and maritime trade began to flourish. By the 13th and 14th centuries, when the Mongol Empire ruled Central Asia and China, the Silk Road trade network was completely cut off.
Until the modern era, the President of the People's Republic of China, Xi Jinping, has developed a new Silk Road policy, the Belt and Road Policy, to link diplomacy, politics, economy and trade with many countries. As in Southeast Asia, Southeast Asia, Africa and beyond to Europe, the new era of the Silk Road is much larger than the ancient Silk Road.
