The wildfires that killed 20 people in Greece last week were the largest in the European Union since 2000.
The fire department said six planes and four helicopters were assisting 475 firefighters on the ground, backed by an additional 100 vehicles. And 260 firefighters and a helicopter are working to fight another massive fire that has been burning for days in a forest on the southern slopes of Mount Parnitha on the outskirts of the Greek capital. .
Authorities are investigating the cause of the blaze, which has been raging for weeks, burning homes and displacing thousands.
