(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of August 29, 2023, the National Bank of Cambodia issued a notification on the preparation of measures to maintain exchange rate stability.
According to the announcement, the prepared measures include intervention in the foreign exchange market and the use of other monetary and political instruments to maintain the value of the riel in order to maintain the purchasing power of the Cambodian people.
According to the National Bank of Cambodia, in recent days, the riel exchange rate against the US dollar has increased significantly, mainly due to seasonal factors and the pressure of the US dollar appreciation in international markets. .
As for the seasonal factors, the demand for the riel has slowed down during the agricultural season and the low season. The US dollar as a whole continued to appreciate against other world currencies after the US Federal Reserve continued to raise benchmark interest rates, attracting capital inflows to the United States and boosting demand for the US dollar in international markets.
(Phnom Penh): The National Assembly of Cambodia will continue the first session of the National Assembly of the 7th legislature with two agendas on August 31, 2023 under the high presidency of Mrs. Kittisangkho Dr. Khuon Sodary, President of the National Assembly.
According to the announcement of the National Assembly, the two agendas include:
1: Decision on the validity of the mandate of 29 elected members of the 7th National Assembly to replace the deposed MPs.
2: Election of Mr. Youk Ngoy as a member of the Constitutional Council to replace Mr. Sam Prohmna, a member of the Constitutional Council who died elected by the National Assembly of the 7th legislature.
