According to the Bor Seth District Working Group, in the past, the district administration has worked hard to provide care, visit and provide food to poor children living with poor aunts.
Due to the lack of a working group, as pointed out by Mr. Sam Oeun Sopanha, Governor of the District Board of Governors, the Office of Social Affairs and Welfare, in cooperation with the village and commune authorities, sent seven children, including five girls. With the consent of the aunt and with the consent of the children themselves, they volunteered to live and study at the Kampong Speu Orphanage.
