Minister Chhay Rithy Sen Initiates the Establishment of the "Civil Servants Association of the Ministry of Rural Development" to Strengthen Solidarity and Friendship
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chhay Rithi Sen, Minister of Rural Development, initiated the idea of establishing the "Association of Civil Servants of the Ministry of Rural Development" in order to maintain and strengthen the bonds of solidarity and friendship between civil servants of this Ministry.
This statement was made on the occasion of Mr. Chhay Rithi Sen's meeting and meeting with the leaders and civil servants of the Department of Supply and Finance and the Department of Planning and Public Relations at the Ministry of Rural Development on the afternoon of August 29, 2023.
Mr. Ban Somara, Advisor to the Ministry, Director of Supply and Finance Department and Mr. Pheng Sambo, Director of Planning and Public Relations Department, reported to the Minister on the Department's first half 2023 Progress Report. According to the report, the Minister praised and appreciated the efforts of the leadership of the department, especially the achievements of both departments in the past.
On that occasion, Minister Chhay Rithi Sen recommended and instructed the civil servants under the guidance of the two departments above that based on the existing achievements must continue to work harder to increase new achievements. The two departments must also prepare to summarize the annual report to hold a meeting to review the work results for 2023 and work directions for 2024, which will take place on December 22, 2023.
He further suggested that the two departments should work hard to complete the formulation of national policies, rural development and necessary legal standards to promote rural development in line with the vision of Cambodia as a high-middle-income country by 2030 and a high-income country. High in 2050.
The Minister further advised that the leadership must be pious and fair in leading and allocating responsibilities to all officials. Officials at all levels in the department must respect the discipline, respect the assignment, respect the code of ethics, respect the discipline of the meeting (monthly, quarterly meeting) and strive to perform their duties better.
The Department of Supply and Finance must strive to promote the provision of materials to various departments in a timely manner. On the other hand, attention must be paid to women, especially pregnant women, sick civil servants and retirees.
