Banteay Meanchey Military sends Thai national to court over drug case
(Banteay Meanchey): On August 28, 2023, the Poipet Municipal Gendarmerie Local Force, led by Brigadier General Nuon Ninaro, the Commander of the Poipet Municipal Gendarmerie, arrested a Thai national for illegal possession and use. Drugs at Teuk Pou Night Market in Kbal Spean 1 Village, Sangkat O'Chrov, Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province.
Exhibits seized included: 7 packets of white crystalline powder (ketamine) weighing 6.25 grams, 1 passport, 1 Thai identity card and 1 backpack.
Colonel Nuon Ninaro said that before the crackdown, the Municipal Gendarmerie received information from security guards that there was a case of storing and distributing drugs. Immediately, the Municipal Gendarmerie arrived at the location to detain the suspects and exhibits and brought them to the Municipal Gendarmerie for processing.
After being arrested and questioned, the suspect confessed that he had actually stored and used illegal drugs. Based on the confession and the actual evidence, the Poipet Municipal Gendarmerie has prepared a case file and sent it to the Provincial Gendarmerie Command to proceed with the procedure.
Colonel Chea Dara, Deputy Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie in charge of anti-drug work, said that the crackdown was also authorized by Brigadier General Born Bin, Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie and coordinated the procedure. From Mr. Keut Vannareth, Prosecutor of the Provincial Court.
Currently, the suspect and the exhibits were sent by the Provincial Anti-Drug Office of the Provincial Gendarmerie to the Provincial Court on the afternoon of August 29, 2023 to follow the procedure.
