European Council President: EU needs to be ready by 2030 for new members
Speaking at a forum in Slovenia, Michel said: "In my personal belief, we must be ready by 2030 to expand our membership. This goal is a big ambition, but it is a necessary thing. "It shows that we are very clear."
Currently, six countries in the Western Balkans, including Albania, Bosnia, Kosovo, Montenegro, Northern Macedonia and Serbia, are at different stages of the EU membership process. In 2022, Moldova and Ukraine also received EU candidate status, while Georgia is still waiting for that status.
Michel said that in order to join the EU, future member states must implement reforms to ensure an independent judiciary, systematically fight crime and corruption, and streamline their foreign policy. In line with EU member states. He also urged countries that want to become members to resolve bilateral disputes before joining the EU.
The EU currently has 27 member states, including Austria, Belgium, Bulgaria, Croatia, the Czech Republic, Denmark, Finland, France, Germany, Greece, Hungary, Italy, Italy, Lithuania, Luxembourg, Poland and Poland. Nha Trang and Sweden. Ministry of Social Affairs Continues Meeting on Standard Operating Procedures for Identification and Repatriation of Trafficking Victims
