The re-announcement of these six priority policies was made on the occasion of His Excellency Dr. Hun Manet's visit to nearly 20,000 workers in Prey Speu, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh, the first public forum as Prime Minister.
His Excellency stated the six policies, including:
2: Skills training for young people from poor families with a target of 1.5 million people. This vocational training consists of short courses, medium courses, long courses, and the young people who study not only do not pay, but also receive a stipend.
3: Expanding the coverage of the National Social Assistance Program and all social protection districts to about 4.5 million people through the first: National Social Assistance Program as a family package to provide subsidies to help more than 700,000 poor and vulnerable families. A total of more than 2.8 million households. Second, expand the protection framework to respond to emergencies to support and provide support to people with systematic conditions for sustainability.
4. Introduce strategies on informal economic development, such as motodup riders, tricycle riders, construction workers, vendors, etc. to be able to participate in the economy in the system and be able to benefit from the formal social protection system.
5. Establish a specific budget to support the agricultural sector. The Prime Minister stated that the Royal Government has prepared 100 million US dollars to intervene in agricultural products, rice, vegetables, etc. through the necessary programs of the Royal Government.
