Minister Chheang Ra Visits Health Care Centers and Hospitals in Kampong Thom Province (Video inside) (Kampong Thom): Minister of Health Prof. Chheang Ra on August 28, 2023 Visiting people who come to receive health services at Canal Health Center, Kampong Thom Provincial Hospital and Baray and Santuk Referral Hospital in Kampong Thom Province.
On that occasion, Professor Chheang Ra also personally examined the patient's condition and provided guidance to patients and their families on health care and prevention and control of infectious and non-communicable diseases.
At the same time, the professor also showed how to care for and treat patients, especially how to provide quality and effective emergency care to doctors at health centers, referral hospitals and provincial hospitals.
Around this visit, the people who came to receive medical treatment expressed their great satisfaction with the attention of the Minister of Health.
In addition, the people were very happy to hear that the Minister of Health in the seventh mandate will strive to improve the health sector, including infrastructure, medical facilities, especially to improve the quality and effectiveness of treatment. The disease gets better.
Minister Chheang Ra also stressed that the local health sector will be strengthened to have sufficient capacity for medical examination and treatment. If the patient is in a very serious condition, our health center must be competent enough to provide first aid in a timely and safe manner before transferring to another location.
However, at the referral hospital level and at the provincial level, the capacity to provide emergency treatment is greatly strengthened to reduce the transfer of patients from remote provinces to Phnom Penh.
Please be informed that after assuming the position of Minister of Health in the 7th mandate, Prof. Chheang Ra led a health delegation to inspect the condition of health facilities in the provinces around Tonle Sap Lake from 25-28 August. 2023, visiting health centers, referral hospitals and provincial hospitals in six provinces, including: Kampong Chhnang, Pursat, Battambang, Banteay Meanchey, Siem Reap and Kampong Thom.
During the first mission, the Minister also met with leaders and health officials, highlighting strategies to provide effective care and treatment of patients, including:
1: Increase health education activities for the people to improve the health of the people.
3. Prevent the spread of infectious diseases worldwide.
4: Fight non-communicable diseases such as cancer, diabetes, heart disease, etc.
5: Fight the effects on health caused by climate change.
6. Improve comprehensive community outreach as well as improve social protection programs such as the ESS, Equity Fund.
7: Improve the quality of care in both public and private services.
8. Develop health and human resources throughout the country to send experts to the grassroots, that is, to bring services closer to the people.
9: Digital health development.
He added that one of the priorities for the seventh term is the maintenance services, which will be further improved. In the future, the Ministry will implement three action plans, including:
* Strengthen health centers by improving the building with additional facilities, including the supply of medicines, strengthen staff capacity to ensure 24-hour service
* Strengthen the quality, efficiency, safety and equity of services in both district and provincial referral hospitals and national hospitals, as well as improve the regulation of private services and to take private services in partnership with public services.
* Strengthen the organization through continuous training on leadership skills to leaders at all levels.
