"If there is a serious incident, whether on the Polish or Lithuanian border, we will retaliate immediately and all border crossings will be closed," Kaminsky added.
EU and NATO members such as Latvia, Lithuania and Poland have been concerned about the escalation of security threats since Russian mercenaries Wagner arrived in Belarus. By 2023, Poland has closed all border crossings, leaving only one crossing after the arrest and imprisonment of Polish-born journalists and the expulsion of Polish diplomats from Belarus.
