The public meeting program that HE Honorary Governor Dr. Hun Manet met on Tuesday, August 13, 2023, is the workers who are working in the factories. Enterprises in Phnom Penh, a total of nearly 20,000 people. The meeting will be held in Prey Speu, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
Heng Sour, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, told Fresh News that 18,013 workers from 13 factories in 12 Po Sen Chey districts and Khans met with His Excellency Dr. Hun Manet. One top. Of these, 844 were pregnant.
In the textile, garment, footwear and travel products and bags industries, one of the most labor-intensive industries in Cambodia. The Royal Government of Cambodia in the old mandate, headed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, paid high attention to this sector, especially the well-being of the workers who are active operators.
For the new legislature of the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by His Excellency the Honorary Governor, Dr. HUN Manet still pays high attention to the textile, garment, footwear and travel products and bags industries.
In the Pentagon Strategy - Phase 1, announced by His Excellency Dr. Hun Manet during the First Cabinet Meeting on August 24, 2023, also set strategic goals to create more jobs in both quantity and quality to the people. Cambodians, especially young people.
In addition, in the third pentagonal strategic angle, the Royal Government has also shown its focus on private sector development and employment. In the third corner of the Pentagon Strategy, the Royal Government continues to focus on five priorities, including:
1: Development of the labor market with strategic goals, focusing on promoting the development of the labor market by creating, maintaining and increasing employment for workers, both in the system and outside the system, aimed at increasing income, sustaining a decent living and Reduce people's poverty.
2: Promoting small and medium enterprises, new businesses, entrepreneurship and informal economic development, with strategic goals focused on continuing to promote the development of a favorable environment for small and medium enterprises and new businesses to grow, resilient Crisis and innovation that contribute to economic growth and job creation, as well as the development of the informal economy, the transition into the system economy.
3. Strengthening Public-Private Partnerships with Strategic Goals Focusing on Continuing to Strengthen Public-Private Partnerships as an Indispensable and Effective Mechanism to Support Diversity and Growth, and Continuing to Strengthen Debt risk management eventually to the implementation of public investment projects under the public-private partnership mechanism.
4: Strengthening the competition with strategic goals, focusing on continuing to promote fair competition by continuing to create a fair, non-discriminatory business environment, fair procedures and in line with the "character of the system" A »aims to contribute to the creation of new goods and services and increase productivity and economic efficiency in Cambodia.
5: Strengthening the banking system and the non-banking financial sector with strategic goals, focusing on continuing to strengthen the banking system and the non-banking financial sector to be more efficient, crisis resilience, environment, diversity and modernity through Continue to develop the legal framework, promote financial depth, strengthen institutional capacity and financial literacy, and promote digitalization in the financial sector.
By capturing the first conversations with workers in the public forum on the agenda of His Excellency Dr. Hun Manet, it is clear that the new government continues to pay high attention to the industrial sector. Textiles, garments, footwear and travel products and bags, which provide a lot of jobs for Cambodians.
It should be noted that the first appearance of His Excellency Dr. Hun Manet as the Prime Minister of Cambodia on this public forum will be broadcast live on Fresh News as well as many other national and private media.
Permanent Deputy Prime Minister Vongsey Visoth, Minister in charge of the Office of the Council of Ministers, presides over the first internal meeting of the Council of Ministers.
(Phnom Penh): On August 28, 2023, Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Permanent Deputy Prime Minister in charge of the Office of the Council of Ministers, chaired the first internal meeting of the Office of the Council of Ministers in the Royal Government of the seventh mandate of the National Assembly. Attended by Lok Chumteav, Secretary of State and Under Secretary of State and Director General of all General Departments under the Office of the Council of Ministers.
However, he stressed that the leadership of the country for the next 25 years is different from the service of 25 years ago, due to changes in regional and global trends, such as geopolitics. Polar to polar, changing global trade trends from globalization to regionalization and bilateralism, climate change and so on. Therefore, it is necessary to have new methods, new work methods, new working methods.
Therefore, the journey forward in the development of the country for the next 25 years is on a more difficult and complicated path, however, this journey is also a necessary national mission and of great value. The next generation of leaders to build on the existing foundations, as well as the determination to maintain the absolute peace that our ancestors inherited hard work.
The main priorities are to continue to reform public institutions and governance in order to achieve a highly capable, strong, intelligent and clean public administration, as well as human resource development, which are key to development and building. Long-term nation and modernization of the Cambodian economy.
