BEIJING: China has urged the United States to stop persecuting its students living in the United States for national security reasons. This is according to the release by the Xinhua news agency on August 28, 2023.
Wang made the remarks when asked to comment on reports that the FBI had recently stolen the personal information of a Chinese student from his curriculum documents, arrested him and charged him with felony criminal mischief. "Visa fraud." Three Chinese students were also detained, interrogated and deported by US customs and border guards without proper evidence or grounds.
He added that exchanges in education, science and technology are an important part of people-to-people contacts between the two countries. The US side has always said that it supports the exchange of education and people between the two countries and welcomes Chinese students, but in fact it continues to implement discriminatory restrictions and expand the concept of excessive national security.
"This seriously affects the legitimate rights and interests of Chinese students and undermines people-to-people exchanges and educational cooperation between the two countries," Wang said.
