The Minister has strong faith and commitment, with the common hope that we will unite as a whole to fulfill the main mission that the Royal Government of the seventh mandate has entrusted to the Ministry of Inspection. Deputy Prime Minister Sokha Introduce legal aspects, requiring motorcyclists from 60 cc to have a driver's license to reduce traffic accidents
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Sar Sokha, Minister of Interior, has instructed to study the legal aspects to require motorcyclists from 60 cc to have a driver's license, and such requirements to reduce traffic accidents.
The introduction of Deputy Prime Minister Sar Sokha was made on the occasion of the inauguration of General Sar Thet as the National Police Commissioner General on the afternoon of August 28, 2023 at the Ministry of Interior.
"Currently, 120cc motorcycles do not need a driver's license, but in the future, I think it should be," said Dr. Abhisandibandi Sar Sokha. Because motorcycles are 120 cc, but some counters 120-130, if we drive at 80-90, hitting cows and buffaloes can also be dangerous, so this is an additional consideration as a measure to prevent future traffic accidents may be less than 60 cc is not necessary. Yes, but 60 cc or more must have a driver's license.
In this regard, Deputy Prime Minister Sar Sokha instructed Dr. Mao Chandara, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Interior, to study the legal aspects and find arguments to discuss with the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, which is a key player in organizing this work.
It should be noted that this work can be said to be the message of the first reform when he took office as Deputy Prime Minister of the Ministry of Interior of Mr. Abhisand Bandit Sar Sokha and is also considered an important work to participate. Reduce traffic accidents in Cambodia. Dr. Aphisandit Dr. Sar Sokha, a former police officer, was well aware of some of the challenges involved in this traffic incident.
Currently, motorcyclists in Cambodia under 125 cc are not required to have a driver's license, from 126 cc onwards, a "A" driver's license is required.
Deputy Prime Minister Sar Sokha sets out some priority work guidelines for the newly-appointed National Police Commissioner General
(Phnom Penh): The Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Ministry of Interior, Mr. Abhisandibandi Sar Sokha, has issued a number of instructions to General Sar Thet, who was announced as the new National Police Commissioner on the afternoon of August 28, 2023.
The priority tasks as well as the guidance of Deputy Prime Minister Sar Sokha on that occasion include:
* First, we must work together to maintain peace, political stability, independence, democracy, and territorial integrity from interference in Cambodia's internal affairs, and to prevent any attempt to overthrow the legitimate government and Any incitement to cause political instability or social unrest
* Second: Increase peacekeeping by increasing cooperation between the authorities, law enforcement forces of countries bordering Cambodia and countries in the region and the world to exchange information, cooperate in preventing terrorism, transnational crime, with a clear organization of That group of crimes and human trafficking and other acts that could affect Cambodia's development
* Third: Continue to strengthen the work and community in order to promote the implementation of the policy of safe villages, communes, sangkats, mobilize and mobilize all sectors at all levels, especially to increase the participation of the people in order to prevent and suppress crimes in the community and maintain Order the environment and join the Royal Government to implement this policy of safe villages, communes and sangkats
* Fourth: Illegal drugs are the most complex and dangerous challenges, especially the mechanism of production, traffic, trafficking and distribution of illegal drugs in the region and the world has not decreased. In 2022, the Cambodian National Police confiscated about 16 tons of drugs and 344 tons of chemicals.
In this regard, the National Police Force must be further strengthened between the relevant ministries, institutions and authorities to implement mechanisms to combat illegal drugs and to promote educational measures, research measures, repression and increase cooperation between countries and relevant international organizations. Region and world. Learn from the experience of cracking down on and rehabilitating drug addicts.
* Fifth: Continue to develop education measures, administrative measures and legal measures to strengthen road traffic safety, order on the city streets to solve congestion and reduce traffic accidents.
* Sixth: For the reform of the National Police Force, attention must be paid to the training of the National Police to have clear skills, adhere to the discipline of the Armed Forces, and strengthen the selection of the National Police to be accurate and transparent. Awarded positions, promotions and awards, rewarded based on qualifications and work experience, as well as the strict implementation of force discipline and improve work efficiency.
* 7th: Request the leadership of all National Police officers to provide support to General Sar Thet, General Commissioner of the National Police, to continue to lead and manage in new tasks, especially to maintain public peace and social security to be more quality and effective. .
