On that occasion, Mr. Sok Soken and Mr. Francis Calbodilay pledged to expedite the signing of a Memorandum of Understanding on Tourism Cooperation between Cambodia and East Timor in order to enhance cooperation in this field. Economy and culture build stronger people-to-people ties and help boost mutual trust and mutual benefit for both countries.
Minister Sok Soken reaffirmed his readiness to work with East Timor on organizing tourism activities as well as exchanging tourism officials to enhance tourism cooperation.
The Minister thanked the Government of East Timor for continuing to maintain and strengthen the good bilateral relations since the government led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the former Prime Minister of Cambodia and the Royal Government led by His Excellency the Governor. Dr. Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, 7th legislature.
Mr. Francois Calderley expressed his appreciation for the good relations between the two countries and also reminded of the Royal Government of Cambodia's efforts to strengthen and deepen the cooperative relations between the two nations.
The Deputy Prime Minister of East Timor also reminded of the importance of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's official visit to the Democratic Republic of East Timor on 19-20 August 2016 that has boosted cooperation in many important areas, including Tourism as well.
The Deputy Prime Minister also reiterated the intention of the people of Timor-Leste to visit Cambodia, so strengthening tourism cooperation between the two countries is very important to achieve this goal. German Ministry of Telecommunications and GIZ sign cooperation agreement to establish first phase of "Digital Development Center of Cambodia"
On that occasion, the Minister said that under the leadership of His Excellency Dr. Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, the first phase of the Pentagon Strategy has been set, with priority given to the transformation and building of the digital economy and society in Cambodia. Defined in the fifth pentagon.
Today's agreement is an important part of supporting the implementation of the Pentagon strategy, especially the priority tasks of building digital government and digital citizens, digital startup, building and developing digital infrastructure, and Build digital trust.
On that occasion, the Minister highly appreciated GIZ for participating in the implementation of the Royal Government's initiatives in the digital revolution, especially the implementation of the digital government policy 2022-2035.
