Minister of Interior Announces the Inauguration of General Sar Thet as National Police Commissioner
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of August 28, 2023, Dr. Ab Sokha, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, announced the inauguration of General Sar Thet, General Commissioner of the National Police, to replace General Dr. Neth Savoeun. Deputy Prime Minister for the 7th term.
The inauguration ceremony of the new Commissioner General of the National Police was held at the Ministry of Interior with the participation of the Deputy Commissioner of the National Police, the Director of the Central Department, the Deputy Director of the Department, the Director of the Department and the Commissioner of the Police Commission. Capital - Province.
It should be informed that from 2008 until August 22, 2023, the General Commission of the National Police led by General Dr. Neth Savoeun as the Chief Commissioner, but when the Royal Government of the 7th legislature led by HE Honorary Governor Dr. Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia took office, and General Neth Savoeun was appointed Deputy Prime Minister.
For more than 15 years, the General Commission of the National Police under the leadership of General Dr. Neth Savoeun has built many remarkable achievements and achievements, especially in maintaining peace, ensuring political stability, especially internal security. Normalize the top institutions, including the monarchy.
More importantly, prevent and prevent any attempt to destroy Cambodia by extremist extremists, that is, any action that seeks to destroy peace and the legitimate government resulting from this election can not take place. It is noteworthy that the capacity of all national police forces has also been continuously strengthened and upgraded to keep pace with the evolving global situation.
Separately, for the new General Commissioner of the National Police General Commission, who has been appointed to this position, is General Sar Thet. Mr. Sar Thet is currently serving as the Deputy Commissioner General and Commissioner of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police and was promoted by the King in a Royal Decree to the rank of General and National Police Commissioner on August 23, 2023.
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Ru Adal Hach, Representative of the Office of the High Commissioner for Human Rights in Cambodia, congratulated Cambodia on being the first country to take action to mark the 75th anniversary by appointing a focal point to mark the day. This, as well as other activities, demonstrates the Royal Government's willingness to promote and respect human rights.
On that occasion, Senior Minister Keo Remy thanked the OHCHR Representative who has always cooperated in the field of human rights in the past and we will continue to cooperate with each other.
Senior Minister Keo Remy said that in celebration of the 75th anniversary, the Cambodian Human Rights Committee has already conducted two summits: two workshops, a 365-day campaign, and a seminar on civil rights. And politics in Battambang province and disseminate the national report on the implementation of the International Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Racial Discrimination in Banteay Meanchey Province.
In addition to discussions for the 75th anniversary celebrations, the two sides discussed the priorities of the Human Rights Committee:
First, the filing of complaints by the Human Rights Committee in prisons in Phnom Penh, which is an effective mechanism for inmates to report human rights abuses in prisons.
2: Introduction of Mobile Complaints Receipt System (CHRC Apps) of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee to facilitate the filing of complaints by citizens in the provincial capitals.
4. The establishment of an independent National Human Rights Committee in accordance with the principles of the Paris Convention, which is planned to be established in the near future.
The representative of the Office of the High Commissioner for Human Rights in Cambodia hopes to request the retention of the current Cambodian Human Rights Committee, as necessary, despite the establishment of the National Human Rights Committee.
She hoped that the two institutions would work together to improve and strengthen the human rights situation in Cambodia.
It should also be noted that the Cambodian Human Rights Committee and the Office of the High Commissioner for Human Rights in Cambodia will hold workshops to disseminate the report on economic, social and cultural rights, as well as consultations on the Universal Periodic Review (UPR) report. Coming soon.
Finally, the Senior Minister informed the representative of the Office of the High Commissioner for Human Rights in Cambodia that he believed in the composition of the Royal Government because he believed in the leadership of His Excellency Dr. Hun Manet in leading the Royal Government, especially on This field of human rights. Delegation of Ottawa Convention Supports the Vision and Commitment of HE Dr. HUN Manet in Resolving Mine Action in Cambodia
