The following is the Royal Decree of the King: Chinese Ambassador: China will continue to closely cooperate with Cambodia in the fields of economy, culture, education and other fields.
Mr. Oum Vuthy, Founder and Chairman of the Board of the Cambodian Students Association in the People's Republic of China and Assistant to Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate of Cambodia, said that it is an honor for the Students Association to have the opportunity to celebrate this year. Cambodia-China friendship and send students to study in China.
The event was organized to strengthen the Cambodian-Chinese youth friendship on the occasion of the 65th anniversary of the establishment of Cambodia-China diplomatic relations, as well as to encourage and provide warmth to Chinese government scholarship students for the 2023-2024 academic year who are ready to fly to study. In China at the end of August, planning to study in Beijing, Shanghai, Tianjin and other provinces of China.
On that occasion, the Chairman of the Board also thanked the two heads of government through the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia and the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports for always paying attention to Cambodian students studying in China. The student association is committed to helping more young people to study in China through the mission of organizing seminars, promoting local scholarships and seeking scholarships in China.
At the same time, the Chairman of the Board also instructed the students who have to continue their studies in China to make efforts to study in order to contribute their knowledge to contribute to the development of the country and perform their duties as students better as Cambodian students. Participate in promoting Khmer culture and civilization in order to attract Chinese investors and Chinese tourists to visit and invest in Cambodia.
"Cambodia will surely move towards a new era of prosperity and strength," the ambassador said. As a strong friend, China will always stand with Cambodia and strongly support Cambodia in continuing its journey towards development that suits its country.
The Ambassador emphasized the strong friendship between China and Cambodia, saying that China will continue to closely cooperate with Cambodia in the fields of economy, culture, education and other fields to jointly promote the well-being of the people of China. Both countries.
At the same time, the Ambassador expressed his support and gratitude to the Cambodian Students Association in China for organizing this event.
The Ambassador said that the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia will continue to support the work and activities of the Cambodian Students Association in China and will do its best to help solve difficult problems and jointly provide a better learning and living environment for students. Cambodia in China.
The Chinese Ambassador also sent a warm welcome message to Cambodian students preparing to study in China. The Ambassador encouraged students to study hard to become a pillar of the motherland and contribute to the development of Cambodia.
The celebration not only marked the deep friendship between China and Cambodia, but also built a platform for exchange and cooperation between the youth of the two countries. In the future, the two countries will continue to strengthen cooperation in various fields and jointly create a better future.
Dr. Hang Chuon Naron delivered a speech in Chinese and Khmer, expressing deep gratitude to the Chinese side for its long-term support for the development of education in Cambodia and hope that the friendship between Cambodia and China will continue. Good to each other forever.
In addition, the Deputy Prime Minister wished all scholarship students success in their studies in China and return to their homeland with full and rich abilities.
