(Phnom Penh): In addition to announcing the strategic plan and priority work for civil servants of the Ministry of Tourism, Mr. Sok Soken, Minister of Tourism, also announced the launch of three major priority groups to assist in achieving the strategic plan. Key policies and strategic plans related to tourism.
The first priority focus group focuses on strengthening institutional capacity and tourism governance:
1. Promote the common values of the organization "unity, integrity, responsibility, efficiency and excellence", improve the work environment and job satisfaction, as well as increase communication opportunities between officials and management to promote efficiency and improve the well-being of civil servants.
2. Build the foundation for job excellence, including improving the work environment, strengthening the capacity, skills and talents of officials, promoting the effective use of modern methods and technologies in work operations, such as promoting creative thinking, design tools, digital tools and technology.
3. Take steps to improve current programs and activities that require intervention to restore and promote efficiency and achievement as expected.
4. Initiate updates, revisions and preparation of legal documents, structures, procedures, human resources and financial resources in accordance with strategic goals.
The second priority group focuses on strengthening and expanding partnerships in tourism development:
1. Strengthen and increase partnerships to develop a vibrant tourism sector and respond to the needs of the development of tourism in a timely manner.
2. Strengthen cooperation with ministries, institutions, the private sector, development partners and all stakeholders in the promotion of tourism marketing and promotion, development of tourism products and services, training of tourism professionals, facilitation of travel and transportation, tourism and destination development. Tourism to be attractive and highly competitive.
The third priority group focuses on promoting the development of a competitive, sustainable and environmentally friendly tourism sector to achieve a common vision for promoting economic growth and social progress:
3. Continue to implement key policies and strategic plans to enhance the effectiveness of tourism management and development in line with the vision towards the future goals of clean, green and sustainable Cambodia to attract about 8 million international tourists and about 16 million domestic tourists. In 2028.
4. Strengthen the capacity to study tourism marketing and promotion, expand the use of new technologies and digital tourism, promote tourism diplomacy, promote the development of innovative and innovative tourism products and services, especially improving the quality of tourism services, promoting tourism attractiveness , Additional tourism vocational training, travel facilitation and tourism transportation.
5. Continue to promote domestic tourism activities and international tourist flows to visit Cambodia in line with education, encourage people to understand the importance of tourism and participate in the development of attractive tourism.
It should be informed that the announcement of these priority work groups was made during the meeting ceremony of Dr. Thong Khon, Senior Minister in charge of Special Mission and Mr. Sok Soken, Minister of Tourism with the leadership-civil servants of the Ministry of Tourism. 400 people on the morning of August 25, 2023 at the Ministry of Tourism. Honorary Dr. Hing Bun Heang Chairs a Meeting to Summarize the Results of the 7th National Assembly Election in Kandal Stung District
