(Phnom Penh): On August 23, 2023, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation organized a meeting to say goodbye to the old Minister, Mr. Prak Sokhon, and welcome the new Minister, Deputy Prime Minister Sok Chenda Sophea.
During the farewell ceremony, Mr. Prak Sokhon delivered a 10-page speech, which was his handwritten speech. In that speech, Mr. Prak Sokhon highlighted the memories of working relationships, working methods and many achievements during his tenure at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs for 7 years.
The speech also highlighted the success of hosting the 13th Asia-Europe Summit and chairing the ASEAN Summit and related summits. Through these summits, Cambodia's foreign policy capabilities were clearly demonstrated.
