(Phnom Penh): At least "5 strategic pillars" and "3 priority support work" were first launched during the inauguration of Mr. Sok Soken as Minister of Tourism in order to promote the development of tourism. The nation will progress further and achieve the growth of international and national tourism as planned.
The announcement of these strategic plans was made during a meeting between Dr. Thong Khon, Senior Minister in charge of Special Mission and Mr. Sok Soken, Minister of Tourism, with a total of 400 leaders and civil servants of the Ministry of Tourism on the morning of the 25th. August 2023 at the Ministry of Tourism.
On that occasion, Minister Sok Soken said that the Ministry of Tourism still has some necessary and urgent tasks to be continued in the vision of developing Cambodia's tourism sector to make Cambodia a leading global tourism destination with rich attractiveness.
In order to support and promote the implementation of the above five strategic pillars, it is necessary to focus on three other priority support activities, which the Minister calls the development of 3-3Ds, with the following details:
First. Develop institutional structure and strengthen tourism governance mechanisms, including taking into account the establishment of National Tourism Councils and strengthening tourist destination management units (DMOs) in capitals and provinces and major tourism destinations by enhancing inter-state partnerships. And private and collaboration with relevant institutions.
Third. Develop human resources with a focus on education, training, professional skills, will, conscience, virtue and ethics for employees - employers and civil servants and other stakeholders in the tourism sector in accordance with their roles and responsibilities to ensure That each employee has a special skill, especially training of tourism professionals in accordance with ASEAN standards, as well as promoting the welfare of tourism officials with equity and environment.
It should be informed that the Ministry of Tourism has a big vision: in 2025, attract 6.4 million international tourists with 16.7 million national tourists and in 2026 attract 7 million international tourists with 17 million national tourists. By 2028, Cambodia also has a vision to attract about 8 million international tourists and about 16 million domestic tourists.
First, to maintain and nurture the hard-won peace with priceless sacrifice and to embrace the dynamics of economic growth and overall development.
The following is a description of the work in the five pentagons:
+ Pentagon 2: Economic Diversification and Increasing Competitiveness, in which the Royal Government continues to focus on five priority tasks, including:
1: Development of key sectors and new sources of economic growth with a strategic focus on expanding and diversifying the base of economic growth by adding value to existing key sectors and developing new sources of growth that are not factors. May be lacking in increasing growth potential and strengthening resilience to crises.
2: Promoting the connectivity and optimization of the transport and logistics sectors, the energy sector, the water sector and the digital sector, with strategic goals focused on continuing to build and strengthen the infrastructure and key preconditions for increasing productivity, raising Increase competitiveness and promote diversification through support infrastructure optimization, and the construction and development of new infrastructure.
3. Improving the business and investment environment with strategic goals, focusing on continuing to improve the business, trade and investment environment through the facilitation and simplification of relevant procedures, digitalization. For the provision of public services and administration, institutional capacity building, and enhancing the effectiveness of inter-ministerial-institutional coordination.
5. Innovation of financing mechanisms and financial products to support investment with strategic goals, focusing on the design and improvement of financing mechanisms and mechanisms and diversification of financial products and services that ensure liquidity in the market. And investment financing options aimed at contributing to investment promotion and economic diversification.
+ Pentagon 3: Private Sector Development and Employment, in which the Royal Government continues to focus on five priority tasks, including:
+ Pentagon 4: Sustainable, Sustainable and Environmental Development, in which the Royal Government continues to focus on five priority tasks, including:
1: Optimization of demographic yields, strengthening demographic resilience and the promotion of gender equality with strategic goals focused on maximizing demographic yields and strengthening demographic resilience. By continuing to promote the implementation of national policies, people and promoting the participation of women in leadership work.
2: Sustainable management of natural resources, cultural heritage and tourism with strategic goals focused on conservation for development, to enhance the contribution of this work to the development of agriculture, industry and tourism, strengthening the management of mineral resources, ensuring sustainability Forest resources, fisheries and soil quality, as well as the protection, development and potential exploitation of sustainable cultural and tourism heritage.
3. Promoting agriculture and rural development with strategic goals, focusing on continuing to strengthen the role and development of modern, diversified and resilient agricultural sector that supports rural development to ensure food security and safety, increase value added, Promote competitiveness and improve the quality of life in rural areas.
4. Strengthening the management and modernization of urban areas with strategic goals, focusing on urban expansion and the development of new cities in the capitals and provinces, the establishment of public parks and green parks, and strengthening the management and modernization of urbanization. To ensure safety, aesthetics, good environment and well-being for living and efficiency in socio-economic development.
5. Ensuring environmental sustainability and climate change preparedness, as well as promoting a green economy with strategic goals focused on maximizing pollution and environmental impacts, strengthening water management and strengthening Resilience to climate change, and contributing to mitigating the effects of global climate change to ensure sustainable development.
+ Pentagon 5: Digital Economic and Social Development, in which the Royal Government continues to focus on five priorities, including:
1: Building a Digital Government and Digital Citizens with Strategic Goals Focusing on Leading the Digital Revolution, with the Royal Government as a Model and Leading in Capturing Digital Technology through the Digitalization of Public Works to Strengthen Public Efficiency The work and efficiency of providing public services to the people and the private sector, and strengthening data-based governance.
3. Building and developing digital infrastructure with strategic goals, focusing on building and expanding digital infrastructure, including: digital connectivity and telecommunications and cloud infrastructure or data centers to enhance the quality and efficiency of digital connectivity, distribution; Share information and telecommunication services.
4: Building Digital Trust with Strategic Goals Focusing on Building Digital Trust through the Establishment of Digital Security Institutions and Mechanisms and Raising Awareness on Digital Security to Promote the Use of Digital Technology Extensive.
5. Development of financial technology with strategic goals, focusing on the development of financial technology by seizing the opportunities and maximizing the benefits of digital technology to improve the financial environment, maintain financial stability and promote financial innovation through Implement Cambodia's financial technology development policy 2023-2028.
