Article and pictures by Cambodia-China Friendship Radio Deputy Prime Minister Tea Seiha chaired the first meeting of the Ministry of National Defense to divide the duties and responsibilities
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Tea Seiha, Minister of National Defense, on the evening of August 25, 2023, chaired the first meeting of the Ministry of National Defense to allocate duties and responsibilities to the Secretary of State and Under Secretary of State. Implement the law and lead the general affairs of the Ministry of National Defense.
The first meeting was attended by leaders of the Ministry of National Defense, the General Command and the National Gendarmerie.
Deputy Prime Minister Tea Seiha continued that in the political program of the Royal Government, the 7th legislature of the National Assembly has clearly defined development policies in the ministries and institutions of the Royal Government. For the defense sector, defining national defense, security, order, and social security prioritizes eight key tasks, including the following:
1. Strengthen the people's national defense with the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces as the core to ensure the protection of peace, independence, sovereignty, territorial integrity, stability in all circumstances, make the people live in harmony on their territory and have opportunities Complete for socio-economic development.
3. Develop, strengthen and expand the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces as a major force in maintaining national security, socio-economic development, infrastructure construction, protection of natural resources, demining and unexploded ordnance, and rescuing people in the event of a disaster. Disasters such as floods, droughts, epidemics.
6. Ensure the effectiveness of the implementation of policies to improve the lives of the army, the lives of disabled soldiers, retired soldiers, disabled soldiers, families of soldiers, victims and veterans. Increase political and psychological education in the army to have a strong will, a strong defense force, strong discipline, moral ability and dignity as an army born of the people, respect, love and serve the people.
7. Promote sisterhood between the military units guarding the border with ministries, institutions, private companies, civil society and other social circles in order to strengthen the connection between the people and the army. Increase the education of the people, especially students, youth, about history, about national pride and about the duties of the people, promote the spirit of patriotism and commitment to defend the motherland.
8. Strengthen cooperation with countries in the field of defense based on the Constitution, national law and international law to expand national defense capabilities, strengthen national sovereignty and promote Cambodia's active participation in the cause of peace, stability and prosperity of the region and the world. Continue to send Cambodian forces to participate in peacekeeping missions under the United Nations umbrella in countries.
On this occasion, Deputy Prime Minister Tea Seiha also paid tribute to the dignitaries, the Secretary of State, the Undersecretary of State, as well as the Director General of the Department under the Ministry of National Defense, who worked hard to fulfill the historic mission in the second legislature. Six of the National Assembly's achievements in the field of national defense should be a source of pride for the motherland.
