(Phnom Penh): Oknha Sin Chanthy, President of the Cambodian Logistics Association, said that the transportation sector in Cambodia has not improved yet, while in the first seven months of 2023, transportation has decreased by about 20% to 30%. % Compared to the previous year due to declining exports and declining overseas orders.
He said factors contributing to the transport sector continued to be affected by the Russia-Ukraine war, trade disputes between major economies and rising inflation. The decline led to a reduction in export and import activity, while the sector was just 19% affected by the Kovid crisis.
He said air transport seemed to be the hardest hit, falling by more than 60 percent, while water transport fell by about 20 percent.
He pointed out that despite the drop in transportation and the continuous rise in fuel prices, most transport companies did not raise prices to help the Cambodian economy.
According to the report of the General Department of Customs and Excise in the first seven months of 2023, trade between Cambodia and international markets was worth more than 27 billion US dollars, down 15.6%, of which Cambodia's exports worth more than 13 billion US dollars fell. 1.8 percent and more than $ 14 billion in imports, down 25.6 percent. Anti-Drug Department sends 2 Thai criminals involved in drug trafficking 118 kg to court
