The Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority (PPWSA) emphasizes this as it begins to drill a 2-meter-wide water main pipe under the bottom of the Tonle Sap River to bring clean water from the east bank to the west at the Prek Pnov bridge.
This 2-meter diameter water main pipe will play an important role in sending clean water from Bak Kheng Water Treatment Plant, Phase 1 and Phase 2 to supply to the people in Phnom Penh and its suburbs.
Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority expects that this 2-meter-diameter water main pipeline will deliver 390,000 cubic meters of clean water per day from Bak Kheng Water Treatment Plant Phase 1 and Phase 2 while Bak Kheng Water Treatment Plant Second, it is planned to launch a test run in the first quarter of 2024 to supply people living in Phnom Penh and Takhmao, especially people living on the outskirts of Phnom Penh.
The 2-meter-diameter water main pipe will be drilled to the bottom of the Tonle Sap at a depth of 25 to 30 meters and a distance of 540 meters. It will take about three to four months to build, scheduled for completion by the end of 2023. Entering the beginning of 2024.
