Banteay Meanchey Military sends a suspect to court in connection with the theft and illegal possession of drugs
(Banteay Meanchey): Brigadier General Yan Sovann, Commander of the Serei Sophorn Municipal Gendarmerie, said that the theft was based on a complaint from two victims, one of whom lost his phone while charging at work.
After receiving the complaint, the Municipal Gendarmerie conducted an operation and search until August 22, 2023, arrested an 18-year-old suspect named Leang Bat, and confiscated two mobile phone exhibits. Stolen and a small package of white crystalline powder at O'Ambel Village, Sangkat O'Ambel, Serey Sophorn City, Banteay Meanchey Province and sent to the Municipal Gendarmerie for questioning and processing.
Based on the confession and the actual evidence, Brigadier General Born Bin, the Provincial Gendarmerie Commander and the representative of the Prosecutor's Office of the Serei Sophorn Municipal Gendarmerie, prepared a case file and sent it to the Provincial Gendarmerie Command to proceed with the procedure.
Lieutenant Colonel Prohm Theng, Director of the Criminal Investigation and Suppression Department, confirmed that the suspect, named Leang Bat, was sent to the Provincial Court by the Provincial Criminal Police on the morning of August 24, 2023. Has been returned to the original owner by professional forces. Prime Minister Hun Manet posted a picture of the first day in the new office at the Peace Palace
