Debate over the expansion of the BRICS bloc has led to the adoption of a new agenda for the three-day summit in Johannesburg, which ends Thursday. All BRICS members have publicly expressed support for the bloc's growth, but there has been some disagreement among their leaders over the number and timing of new members.
It should be noted that the BRICS was established in 2010 by a group of developed countries. It currently has five members: Brazil, Russia, India, China and South Africa.
