His Excellency Sun Sovannarith would like to express his sincere congratulations and support to His Excellency Say Sam Al, who has been appointed Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Land Management for the 7th term.
(Phnom Penh): HE Sun Sovannarith, Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province and Armed Forces Officials throughout the province would like to sincerely congratulate HE Say Sam Al, who has been appointed by the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of HE Dr. HUN Manet. Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction for the 7th legislature.
This statement was made on the occasion of the first plenary session of the new Council of Ministers of the seventh mandate on the morning of August 24, 2023.
HE Dr. HUN Manet stated, "I will lead the 19th Royal Government-Private Sector Forum which will be held in November to listen to opinions and suggestions, as well as the introduction of sharp measures and "Obviously, to continue to support the private sector, which is the driving force of economic growth."
At the same time, HE Dr. HUN Manet would like to delegate the task to Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the Economic and Financial Policy Committee, to coordinate with ministries, institutions, the private sector and other stakeholders. To organize this forum.
HE Dr. HUN Manet emphasized that Cambodia is extremely proud of the achievement of complete and strong peace over the past 25 years, and under this cold shadow of peace, Cambodia has achieved great achievements. Not priceless.
It should be noted that the Royal Government-Private Sector Forum is held once a year by the Royal Government of Cambodia as a dialogue mechanism led by the Prime Minister of Cambodia and with the participation of ministers from all ministries, institutions, governors in all capitals. The province represents the private sector in all fields, the ambassador to Cambodia and representatives of some international institutions.
The Royal Government-Private Sector Forum provides an opportunity for the private sector to raise challenges and suggestions for the Royal Government to review and take appropriate action to address, and all decisions in this forum are considered by the Council of Ministers.
