More than 1 million tons of water used to lower the temperature of the Fukushima nuclear reactor core, which was devastated during the 2011 earthquake and tsunami, is now being stored in steel tanks around 1,000 pools there. The release of the radioactive waste into the sea is a key part of the plan to dismantle this highly dangerous nuclear power plant.
